of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T10:45:49-08:00","id":16697,"title":"","content":"You don't quite grasp the concept of working behind the scenes do ya?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They call me... Mr. Demmywinks.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1210-demetrius7997","name":"Demetrius7997","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T11:47:08-08:00","id":16714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the idea. Indeed, what I'm saying is that a clandestine conspiracy is the <i>only explanation</i> that makes those character's interactions with each other in the original series make any sense, after the prequels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay, I misunderstood you then. My bad. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They call me... Mr. Demmywinks.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1210-demetrius7997","name":"Demetrius7997","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:20:46-08:00","id":17020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=16648#post16648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t let anyone fool you: R2 is the main character of the movie series, around which everything else revolves. When he finally kicks the bucket, the series will be over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truer than one might think, at least initially. I was just listening to the New Hope commentary, and Lucas talks about how the entire series was originally to be told thru the eyes of the &quot;insignificant&quot; droid nobodies...But everyone he shared the idea with HATED it, so he toned it down considerably. He does muse about what a risk it was to start the movie with, what, almost a half hour of the droids before getting to the hero of the tale, tho!<br /> <br /> As for the new movies, I'm not crazy about the idea. Honestly, by this point, I just wish they would leave it alone. What makes it worse is that the Disney sale killed off all the interesting things they were already doing, like the Clone Wars show, and will probably make all the post RotJ comics and books completely non canonical (if they continue them at all). Interestingly, Disney's purchase of Marvel could mean that Marvel might start publishing the comics again...<br /> <br /> Aside from Disney making money tentacle over claw with Marvel, Star Wars, AND the Muppets, we also have the original actors signing on, pretty clearly for the money (except maybe Mark Hamill; I could believe that HE is actually still passionate about it). Really, even if I was eager to see these movies, I wouldn't want Han and Leia to be in them; I'm fine with Luke, in the role of aged, wise Jedi Master, who probably sacrifices himself as his mentor did for the new heroes, and the droids, but that's it. <br /> <br /> I'm sure they've already approached John WIlliams, but what will they do if he turns them down?<br /> <br /> Last I heard, JJ Abrams might be close to walking on the project, as Disney wants this in the theaters ASAP, and he can't guarantee a decent movie rushed like that. Who else would make a good director? Personally, I hope they go for a different one each installment. Imagining a SW movie by Brad Bird almost makes me excited to see this happen!<br /> <br /> But then I remember that Disney also wants to make spin-off side movies, like Young Han Solo, Boba Fett and Yoda. I know they want a return on the massive amount of cash they spent, but surely they are aware of the dangers of market oversaturation?? If they did those as made for TV movies, or straight to DVD, preferably animated, I'm in, but actual theatrical releases seems excessive to me. <br /> <br /> Ok, I've ranted long enough. What do you all think about these points?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T05:40:07-08:00","id":17090,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure anything in the extended universe, comics, books, etc. was only tenuously canon at best anyway.I know that George Lucas shot holes in a lot of it with the prequels already.<br /> <br /> I'm personally excited about the idea of spin off movies. I'd love to see more of the universe on film outside the main plot lines covered in the trilogies. If they do a Han Solo movie I would hope it would be animated. It's not like they can get Harrison Ford to handle that role any more and people might have a hard time accepting anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They call me... Mr. Demmywinks.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1210-demetrius7997","name":"Demetrius7997","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T08:03:08-08:00","id":17121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=17020#post17020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure they've already approached John WIlliams, but what will they do if he turns them down?</div> </div> </div> </div>I, for one, would be okay with Alan Silvestri.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T21:28:00-08:00","id":17503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=17121#post17121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I, for one, would be okay with Alan Silvestri.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll probably get Hans Zimmer...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T21:41:11-08:00","id":17506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demetrius7997</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=17090#post17090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure anything in the extended universe, comics, books, etc. was only tenuously canon at best anyway.I know that George Lucas shot holes in a lot of it with the prequels already.<br /> <br /> I'm personally excited about the idea of spin off movies. I'd love to see more of the universe on film outside the main plot lines covered in the trilogies. If they do a Han Solo movie I would hope it would be animated. It's not like they can get Harrison Ford to handle that role any more and people might have a hard time accepting anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>The expanded universe did a pretty good job of tying things together, esp the material after the prequels. There were a few spots that were iffy (like the Horn family all being Jedi once the prequels established that Jedi of that era couldn't have families), but for the most part, the comics, books and cartoon ran mostly smoothly, as far as I saw.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see spin off movies if they DID cover the universe outside the main plot lines, but I'm not convinced that Disney cares about that. I think they'll play it conservatively, and assume that we just want to see more of the same. Which is a real shame, as I once saw a map of the SW galaxy, and the 6 movies have only covered a TINY part of what's out there. The EU has pushed the envelope a bit, but there should be *so much more* one can do with this setting!<br /> <br /> As far as accepting other actors in the classic roles, I'd have agreed before the recent Star Trek reboot movies proved successful. In fact, I'm absolutely positive that some Disney executive is pushing for a remake of the original trilogy with &quot;hot young actors&quot; solely because the ST franchise did it!<br /> <br /> Even if it were animated, I'm not sure I'd want to have Ford reprise Han Solo. Aside from the aged quality of his voice, which may not be a real problem, if you've seen Ford in interviews for a while now, it's pretty clear that he just doesn't care. And Carrie Fisher (whose voice on the commentaries is almost unrecognizable) is the same, only more sarcastic. We'd probably get another &quot;Blade Runner&quot; style performance from Ford, at best; only where it arguably worked for the beaten down by life character in that movie, it wouldn't fit for Solo at all...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T07:33:53-08:00","id":17695,"title":"","content":"I'm... interested to say the least. I don't know if I could trudge through another trilogy of Lucas' &quot;vision&quot; which makes me want to nerd rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T21:47:39-08:00","id":18167,"title":"","content":"I got yer Nerd Rage, <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QBeAjISBb2U\" target=\"_blank\">right here!</a><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T05:39:57-08:00","id":18364,"title":"","content":"I think Lucas needs to keep his hands off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T08:58:51-08:00","id":18435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=18167#post18167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got yer Nerd Rage, <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QBeAjISBb2U\" target=\"_blank\">right here!</a><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Hahahahahahahahaha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T12:32:58-08:00","id":18623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=18364#post18364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Lucas needs to keep his hands off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure he has to? He sold the rights, he can't have anything to do with SW anymore, unless Disney lets him. And his interviews suggest he's staying very hands off and is happy to do so. BUT...despite how it may seem to us on the internet, there are plenty of fans who honor and respect Lucas, and apparently want him to be involved. Disney may well pursue him, with the idea that fans won't accept it as &quot;true&quot; SW without his name being on it. Even if this does happen, it will most likely be a vanity credit, like how Stan Lee gets executive producer credits on Marvel films despite not actually contributing anything to them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T14:01:15-08:00","id":18696,"title":"","content":"Didn't Lucas write up a treatment for episodes 7-9 that's being used as a foundation for what they're planning? I seem to remember having read that somewhere. Might have been a rumor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They call me... Mr. Demmywinks.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1210-demetrius7997","name":"Demetrius7997","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T14:34:07-08:00","id":18727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demetrius7997</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=18696#post18696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't Lucas write up a treatment for episodes 7-9 that's being used as a foundation for what they're planning? I seem to remember having read that somewhere. Might have been a rumor.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the last I heard he is involved in the production. Just not as the person that has the final say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T19:36:22-08:00","id":20029,"title":"","content":"With it being a Disney film, I will not keep my hopes up, even with Mr. Lucas's involvement with the production of the movie(s).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1393-bent-twig","name":"Bent Twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1393_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T21:09:07-08:00","id":20070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bent Twig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=20029#post20029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With it being a Disney film, I will not keep my hopes up, even with Mr. Lucas's involvement with the production of the movie(s).</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you aware that Disney owns Marvel too, and therefore every movie in the Marvel shared universe (Thor, Captain America, The Avengers, etc.) for the last several years have technically been Disney films? I think having low expectations simply because it's under the Disney umbrella is a bit unrealistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They call me... Mr. Demmywinks.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1210-demetrius7997","name":"Demetrius7997","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T21:39:46-08:00","id":20083,"title":"","content":"Yes I am aware Disney owns Marvel. That is why I only read D.C Comics now<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1393-bent-twig","name":"Bent Twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1393_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T21:50:53-08:00","id":20089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bent Twig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=20083#post20083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes I am aware Disney owns Marvel. That is why I only read D.C Comics now<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And you are missing out.<br /> <br /> Also, they need to make Joss Whedon have a whack at Star Wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T12:40:44-08:00","id":20301,"title":"","content":"These days I'm beginning to have some misgivings about Disney and Marvel-related stuff. As long as they keep the comic-books separated from the movies it'll be ok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T10:40:08-08:00","id":22421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=20089#post20089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And you are missing out.<br /> <br /> Also, they need to make Joss Whedon have a whack at Star Wars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I get a little tired of the whole &quot;Disney is EVIL!!&quot; nonsense thrown around, as if whatever they do must be badwrong just because they're a giant, faceless, soulless corporation...when there really is no such thing (except for legal purposes). All such groups are made of *people*, with all that that implies. Some of them are jerks, but many are decent and cool, and often they're all caught up in cross purposes trying to follow whatever their vision of &quot;good entertainment&quot; is. Sure, the bottom line is $$, as it is for all financial institutions, but that doesn't somehow mean that they can't produce quality products along the way! Avengers was well worth my money, as are almost all of the movies tied into it, and reports about Frozen say the same. <br /> <br /> As to the comics, I dropped Marvel a bit ago, but from what I hear with my ear to the ground, it sounds like Disney's pretty hands off, there. Some comics will copy things from the movies, like costumes, but comics have always done that, usually willingly. Probably the biggest change I've heard about is that mainstream Nick Fury now looks like the Sam Jackson version of the character (although apparently that's a new character, not actually classic NF)...<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure Joss is on lock for Avengers for the forseeable, but I'd love to see him on this, too. Maybe if the movies tank, they'll throw him over there...Who else would be good? What kind of a job do you think Kevin Smith would do?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T10:56:51-08:00","id":22443,"title":"","content":"Frozen was excellent Hand-of-Omega.<br /> <br /> I believe Joss is locked in with marvel through phase 2. I'm not sure if he's going to be sticking around through the next phase. <br /> <br /> I think Kevin Smith could give us an interesting look into parts of the Star Wars universe, but I'm not sure he'd be up to handling part of one of the trilogies. I've got a ton of respect for the guy, but that might be a bit ambitious for him. <br /> <br /> As to possibilities for directors, I wouldn't mind seeing Antoine Fuqua (Boba Fett or young Han Solo movie maybe more than part of the trilogy), Joe Johnston (directed Captain America), James Gunn, or Alan Taylor (both directed Thor: The dark World.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They call me... Mr. Demmywinks.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1210-demetrius7997","name":"Demetrius7997","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T06:38:28-08:00","id":23104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demetrius7997</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=20070#post20070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you aware that Disney owns Marvel too, and therefore every movie in the Marvel shared universe (Thor, Captain America, The Avengers, etc.) for the last several years have technically been Disney films? I think having low expectations simply because it's under the Disney umbrella is a bit unrealistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which also means that Natalie Portman is twice a Disney Princess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T06:55:50-08:00","id":23114,"title":"","content":"My lowered expectations aren't geared towards the Star Wars movies.<br /> They are geared toward Marvel movies however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T08:48:49-08:00","id":54028,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://io9.com/is-star-wars-boba-fett-movie-going-to-be-about-a-whole-1504770166?utm_campaign=socialflow_io9_facebook&amp;utm_source=io9_facebook&amp;utm_medium=socialflow\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/is-star-wars-boba-fet...ium=socialflow</a><br /> <br /> That mentions the possibility of the rumored Boba Fett movie being about a guy who kills Fett and takes his armor and name. Now that I can get behind. Apparently, if the rumor is true, Lawrence Kasdan didn't like Boba Fetts origin in the prequels.<br /> <br /> How awesome would it be if Fett in the OT isn't the same dude from the prequels? That'd be awesome!<br /> <br /> Oh!! What if they did something like The Princess Bride and the Dread Pirates Roberts? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br