is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T06:37:58-07:00","id":122302,"title":"","content":"The cast for Star Wars VII has officially been announced. <a href=\"http://www.philly.com/philly/entertainment/20140429_ap_72d63fb4563e4f49a47a32314c84860a.html\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T07:53:38-07:00","id":126697,"title":"","content":"Supposedly the title for the new star wars is making the rounds. <a href=\"http://io9.com/and-star-wars-episode-viis-title-is-1572331000\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/and-star-wars-episode...-is-1572331000</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T07:55:21-07:00","id":126701,"title":"","content":"Ok, lets turn this into the Lets Talk Star Wars thread.<br /> <br /> Yoda with a lightsaber, yay or nay? We were talking about this at work today, and I think I dislike the idea of Yoda with a lightsaber in the movies. Maybe when Yoda was a Jedi Knight I could see it, but he's a Jedi Master, and I feel like at his mastery level of the Force he no longer needs it.<br /> <br /> What do y'all think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T09:16:28-07:00","id":126747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=126701#post126701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, lets turn this into the Lets Talk Star Wars thread.<br /> <br /> Yoda with a lightsaber, yay or nay? We were talking about this at work today, and I think I dislike the idea of Yoda with a lightsaber in the movies. Maybe when Yoda was a Jedi Knight I could see it, but he's a Jedi Master, and I feel like at his mastery level of the Force he no longer needs it.<br /> <br /> What do y'all think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm okay with it. A lightsaber has symbolic importance even if it's never used - it's a reminder of the Jedi's training, and of their duty to protect the Republic with their lives if it proves necessary. And in some cases (ex. Yoda's duel with Dooku, or his interventions during the Clone Wars), a lightsaber is a useful tool. It's capable of doing things which the Force just can't.<br /> <br /> As a sidenote, this is (according to Wookieepedia) an idea which occasionally appears in Star Wars lore. Palpatine in particular looked down on lightsaber combat and felt he'd outgrown the need for it as a Sith, preferring to rely on his Force powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","user":"Cielle","date":". 05-06-2014, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T10:12:49-07:00","id":126774,"title":"","content":"I've been talking about this on Facebook too. While I have no issues with Yoda having used a lightsaber as a Jedi Knight, I just feel like he shouldn't be in situations where he needs to lightsaber fight. If that makes sense. Like how Palpatine felt he didn't need one anymore. Makes perfect sense to me.<br /> <br /> Aside from cutting a hole in a door or something, I can't think of a single thing you can do with a lightsaber you couldn't do with the force....aside from have a bitching sword fight. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You can deflect energy with the Force, throw things around, etc. Though I suppose a battle of wills isn't as cool visually as a lightsaber fight...but you know what I'm saying. Yoda didn't even bother trying to teach Luke anything lightsaber related in Empire. Granted, Luke wasn't there very long...but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T11:27:21-07:00","id":126829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=126774#post126774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can deflect energy with the Force.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something I wasn't aware of. The ability to use a lightsaber to deflect blaster bolts seems to me like one of the prime advantages of the weapon. (I also get the sense it's why nobody except Force users bothers with lightsabers. If you don't have the superhuman reflexes to parry energy bolts in flight, why use a melee weapon instead of a gun? And if you prefer melee, why use an expensive lightsaber when a vibroblade will work just as well?)<br /> <br /> I still do think it makes sense for a Jedi Master to keep a lightsaber. Wielding the Force takes willpower and focus, and even someone like Yoda has their limits - so if a lightsaber can do the job with less effort, then why not use it? But then, I'm kinda getting in over my head with the lore here, and it's always difficult saying with certainty what a fictional metaphysical force can and cannot do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T12:19:22-07:00","id":126854,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=126829#post126829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's something I wasn't aware of. The ability to use a lightsaber to deflect blaster bolts seems to me like one of the prime advantages of the weapon. (I also get the sense it's why nobody except Force users bothers with lightsabers. If you don't have the superhuman reflexes to parry energy bolts in flight, why use a melee weapon instead of a gun? And if you prefer melee, why use an expensive lightsaber when a vibroblade will work just as well?)</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I guess they never show anyone actively deflecting a blaster bolt. But, in Empire Vader just holds out his hand and stops Han's blaster fire. And Yoda deflects Count Dooku's and Palpatines lightning(least I'm pretty sure he does).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=126829#post126829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still do think it makes sense for a Jedi Master to keep a lightsaber. Wielding the Force takes willpower and focus, and even someone like Yoda has their limits - so if a lightsaber can do the job with less effort, then why not use it? But then, I'm kinda getting in over my head with the lore here, and it's always difficult saying with certainty what a fictional metaphysical force can and cannot do.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a good point.<br /> <br /> Though, let me throw this out there. If a Jedi uses the Force to kill someone, that's bad right? But, if they use the Force to wield a Lightsaber a kill someone that's good? Hmmm....<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T12:52:53-07:00","id":126881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=126854#post126854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, let me throw this out there. If a Jedi uses the Force to kill someone, that's bad right? But, if they use the Force to wield a Lightsaber a kill someone that's good? Hmmm....</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to agree with KOTOR 2's Kreia that the whole lightside/darkside divide is a lot more inconsistent than the Jedi and Sith like to believe. (Granted, she's like my favorite character in the entire Star Wars mythos, so I may be predisposed to agree with her.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T12:59:33-07:00","id":126888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=126854#post126854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I guess they never show anyone actively deflecting a blaster bolt. But, in Empire Vader just holds out his hand and stops Han's blaster fire. And Yoda deflects Count Dooku's and Palpatines lightning(least I'm pretty sure he does).</div> </div> </div> </div>the EU kinda expands on that a bit. Short version, that kind of energy manipulation or absorption is a difficult skill to perfect*, worthy of a master. On the other hand, anyone with minimum training can sense incoming attacks and block them.<br /> <br /> As for the killing them, the argument is primarily intent. Are you trying to defend yourself or others from agression and they won't back down? You may have little choice but kill them. Killing them because they're in your way, or choking the crap outta a guard for guarding a gangster like Jabba? Dangerously Dark Side actions be there.<br /> <br /> <br /> *-Like anything in the EU there are exceptions, There's a whole bloodline that tends to spit out Jedi that are very naturally good at absorbing and redirecting energy as well as mental manipulation, but are absolutely terrible at other things like levitation.<br /> <br /> The Horn family IIRC... they might not be able to lift your X-Wing out of a swamp without a crane, but they can certainly make you *think* they did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T14:58:35-07:00","id":127002,"title":"","content":"1) I actually liked the Yoda fight because anything else they did would have been even more cheesie. You are just not going to make a 2' green dude fighting with a sword against a guy over 6 feet look anything but stupid otherwise. As to a force power battle I have to disagree a bit in that starts hovering too close to the Dark Side. The only parts that were any good in those movies where the Qui-Gon fight, Natalie Portman in a tight outfit bearing midriff, Yoda fight, and Anakin's short choreography with double lightsabers. That and Natalie Portman in a tight outfit bearing midriff...wait did I already say that?<br /> <br /> 2) They've kind of waffled a bit on blaster blocking. What seems to be staying established is that it is a precognitive ability and not a reflexive one. Just like Anakin's piloting ability. I don't know who started it, but Zhan kind of codified it. Well, before Lucas decided to throw most of that out the window(he approved the first three book on a chapter by chapter basis at some points). Still what I've read of the Eu tends to stick to that going forward from there.<br /> <br /> The how is the big waffle. Originally Vader blocked it with the force. I think Lucas later retconned it that it was also because of his armor(blocked out of reflex but the armor absorbed the damage). So the cans and can'ts in the EU have waffled back and forth. It now pretty much seems like with comics they will do what ever the writer's dramatic license says they can do.<br /> <br /> As to reflecting that is a special quality of the forming of the lightsaber blade itself. As far as I know no one as bucked that at least. Even Sith alchemical items only absorb as far as I recall.<br /> <br /> 3) As to light and dark that is another one as well. Lucas has said that unequivocally there is no Grey. All actions are light or dark. EU all depends on who is in charge at the time. I get Lucas's stance because otherwise you get monks that can teleport using the force with no consequences to their actions.<br /> <br /> As to whether an action itself is light or dark I've always like that intent(as Odd_Canuck brings up) meant a lot. We can debate morality(which is subjective any way), but what makes killing someone because you are protecting yourself or other vs just killing someone just because? Dead is dead after all. Our standard morality is based on that intent(well in the end at least). Even our judicial system allow for that in some part. If the courts would rule it self-defense then generally it is thought to be light side. The force just has the bonus of knowing instead of guessing intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T15:06:15-07:00","id":127009,"title":"","content":"When I first pictured Yoda with a lightsaber, I pictured Yoda standing still, eyes closed and serene look on his face while his lightsaber dances through the air on its own, parrying incoming attacks and striking at his foes. <br /> <br /> Jedi are able to throw crates around with ease; maneuvering a small, metal tube should be trivial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T15:28:52-07:00","id":127023,"title":"","content":"Surprisingly, there's only ever been a single Jedi who was able to wield a lightsaber through telekinesis alone. (It was Kreia. Told you she was awesome.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","user":"Cielle","date":". 05-06-2014, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T17:48:23-07:00","id":127105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=127023#post127023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surprisingly, there's only ever been a single Jedi who was able to wield a lightsaber through telekinesis alone. (It was Kreia. Told you she was awesome.)</div> </div> </div> </div>spoilered for any who have yet to play Knights of the Old Republic 2<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoil