y":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T17:52:07-07:00","id":127110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=127009#post127009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I first pictured Yoda with a lightsaber, I pictured Yoda standing still, eyes closed and serene look on his face while his lightsaber dances through the air on its own, parrying incoming attacks and striking at his foes.<br /> <br /> Jedi are able to throw crates around with ease; maneuvering a small, metal tube should be trivial.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you on that...that would have been bad ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T18:42:00-07:00","id":131157,"title":"","content":"Just got done watching that <a href=\"http://kotaku.com/someone-edited-star-wars-episodes-i-iii-into-one-bette-1573980743\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars Prequel all-in-one edit</a> thats been making the rounds . The saying holds true, you can't polish a turd. But, whoever made this did make a pretty good go of it. <a href=\"http://nerdology.tumblr.com/post/85248127225\" target=\"_blank\">This review</a> is pretty spot on for the most part. There were some really good ideas in this edit, I liked how it opened(it starts with the Darth Maul fight and thats all of Episode 1 you get), and I really liked how it ended(with Vaders helmet coming down, and then him breathing..fade to credits). There were some good edits made in this(extremely limited Jar Jar and no Midichlorians to be found), and some really bizarre choices(Obi-Wan shows up on Geonosis for no reason, there is almost no Clone War at all). So, they made a good effort, but I feel like maybe they needed another pass or two. Hell, could have been alittle shorter. If you like the Prequels, this edit isn't for you and if you're no fan of the prequels this certainly won't change your mind. They tried, I'll give them that.<br /> <br /> If you're curious, I'm sure you can find a copy. It's worth a watch just to see they did with it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T20:12:59-07:00","id":131449,"title":"","content":"I decided to watch it, and it has been taken down for copyright reasons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T20:51:54-07:00","id":131492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=131449#post131449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I decided to watch it, and it has been taken down for copyright reasons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, it was removed from that site. If you dig around...you can still find it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you do find it, you'll have to let me know what you thought. It had it's flaws....but I really loved the ending.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T08:56:23-07:00","id":133804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=131157#post131157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just got done watching that <a href=\"http://kotaku.com/someone-edited-star-wars-episodes-i-iii-into-one-bette-1573980743\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars Prequel all-in-one edit</a> thats been making the rounds . The saying holds true, you can't polish a turd. But, whoever made this did make a pretty good go of it. <a href=\"http://nerdology.tumblr.com/post/85248127225\" target=\"_blank\">This review</a> is pretty spot on for the most part. There were some really good ideas in this edit, I liked how it opened(it starts with the Darth Maul fight and thats all of Episode 1 you get), and I really liked how it ended(with Vaders helmet coming down, and then him breathing..fade to credits). There were some good edits made in this(extremely limited Jar Jar and no Midichlorians to be found), and some really bizarre choices(Obi-Wan shows up on Geonosis for no reason, there is almost no Clone War at all). So, they made a good effort, but I feel like maybe they needed another pass or two. Hell, could have been alittle shorter. If you like the Prequels, this edit isn't for you and if you're no fan of the prequels this certainly won't change your mind. They tried, I'll give them that.<br /> <br /> If you're curious, I'm sure you can find a copy. It's worth a watch just to see they did with it...</div> </div> </div> </div>This may or may not having anything to do with it, but if you like Zhan's version of the clone wars you really couldn't show anything.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T05:27:59-07:00","id":135254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=133804#post133804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may or may not having anything to do with it, but if you like Zhan's version of the clone wars you really couldn't show anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, since cloning in his story was alittle different(same in some of the comics, like Dark Empire).<br /> <br /> <br /> Theres another all-in-one prequel edit I'll be checking out called Downfall of the Old Republic. Once I see it, I'll report back..we'll see if it's better than the one above. Just skipping to the end of it, it ends in almost the same way, so that's a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T06:20:51-07:00","id":135297,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve mentioned elsewhere (I think) how I consider there to be four distinct Star Trek universes, which I call Classic Trek, the Star Fleet Universe, the NextGen retcon, and the Abrams-Trek reboot. With the official abandonment by Disney of the Star Wars Expanded Universe, I now consider there to be two Star Wars universes as well: and I\u2019m quite comfortable thinking of Episodes I-III being exclusive to the New Star Wars. Heck, I\u2019ll even be willing to say that there\u2019s some divergence in the two universes\u2019 versions of Episodes IV-VI: in the Classic Star Wars universe, Han shot first; in the New Star Wars universe, Greedo was an incompetent boob who couldn\u2019t even shoot straight. We have never seen Classic Star Wars\u2019 Episodes I-III, although we\u2019ve seen hints about it in Episode VI deleted scenes and in the Thawn Trilogy: for instance, Owen Lars had no relation to Anikan Skywalker; he was Obi-Wan\u2019s brother(-in-law). Anikan never set foot on Tatooine until Episode IV. And so on. <br /> <br /> There are a few novels that came out after Episode I that are slightly problematic because they attempt to reconcile the EU with the new revelations in the prequel series; I have no problem excising such connective tissue as needed. <br /> <br /> There are now two Star Wars; and I intend to judge each on its own merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T11:55:26-07:00","id":135608,"title":"","content":"There's more like five or six versions, all built from changes in canon. THe Star Wars Universe looks different before the prequels compared to after, and the same with consideration for the Clone Wars shows, as well as various other pokings and proddings from Lucas and his company. Hell, there was even some shifting with just the 90's special editions.<br /> <br /> Point is that an idea of the EU versus Lucas's Canon has always been a messy affair, so once again, I can't blame the VII-IX team deciding to just say &quot;Fuck it, we're keeping this simple&quot;. Wrestling with the stupidity of midichlorians is easier then wrestling with the EU.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-13-2014, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T12:38:15-07:00","id":135666,"title":"","content":"Yup, I agree. At one point things fit together pretty good, but it got pretty convoluted so I can see why they decided to just start over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T10:51:17-07:00","id":136879,"title":"","content":"Continuing the Trek tangent, Abrams should have worked with the Mirror Universe IMO, instead of rebooting the main one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T16:57:06-07:00","id":137355,"title":"","content":"Eh; I\u2019m glad he didn\u2019t. I don\u2019t mind at all what he did; my complaints about Abrams-Trek center entirely around how he did it. Actually, I take that back: I have a major problem with the introduction of man-portable interstellar-ranged transporters and immortality serums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T17:22:36-07:00","id":137408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">At one point I was in a Stormtrooper locker room and found an open locker with a hamburger in it. So, of course, I tell the game to &quot;TAKE HAMBURGER&quot;, because <i>any</i> item that can be added to inventory is going to be vital later. Then later, I found a security panel guarded by a <i>huge dog with Darth Vader's name on its collar</i>. So I tried to distract it by feeding it a hamburger (after like an hour and a half of trying to discover the correct syntax to do so), but the game was all &quot;YOU DID NOT TAKE THE ALUMINUM FOIL OFF OF THE HAMBURGER. THE DOG ATE IT AND DIED. DARTH VADER SHOWS UP AND HE IS SO MAD THAT YOU KILLED HIS DOG THAT HE CUTS YOU IN HALF. THE END.&quot;<br /> <br /> That right there is the one true Star Wars.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is... the way that text based games work(ed). That's... just... okay.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T10:48:25-07:00","id":138220,"title":"","content":"Aside the fact that the issues were also with the script, Abrams was totally the wrong director for the new Star Trek. However the things that made him wrong for Star Trek would make him right for Star Wars. I was totally disappointed when I heard he was directing Star Trek(Michael Bay is the only one I can think that would have made it worse), but kind of excited with him doing Star Wars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T15:50:39-07:00","id":156960,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking a lot about Star Wars recently (more so than usual, even!)...And I'm moving my Anticipation-meter to &quot;Cautiously Optimistic&quot;. I still wish they would leave well enough alone, but that ship has sailed, so let's deal with what's coming. Or, even more fun, speculate how we'd do it!<br /> <br /> One night, Abrams, Kennedy, Lucas and whoever else is involved turns up at your door, confesses that they just can't get this thing right, and since you're the biggest SW geek they can find, they need *your help*. What decisions will you make?<br /> <br /> For me, the biggest problem is the overall story: SW is *not* Science-Fiction, it's Science-Fantasy, or Space Opera, if you prefer. It's a fairy tale, a pulp fable in skiffy trappings. It's not deep or complex, it's just telling a basic story of Good Vs. Evil. The original trilogy told the straightforward tale of how Good rose up to defeat Evil. The Prequels expanded this by showing how the Evil was originally Good that fell into Evil, only to be redeemed later. <br /> <br /> But, that tale is done. Where else can the story go, without repeating the same story all over again?<br /> <br /> I said that SW isn't &quot;deep&quot;, but it does borrow from Western and Eastern sources. Ultimately, however, it is a Western tale, and one of the big differences in Western and Eastern philosophies are their take on the role of Evil in Life. Greatly oversimplifying here, but *in general*, the Western idea is that Evil is fundamentally *wrong*, it is a twisted perversion of the natural order that never should have existed, and Good can only win once it destroys Evil utterly (the paradox is that one must often use Evil's methods to do so); Eastern religion/philosophy, otoh, allows for there to be a place for Evil in the natural order of things. It may be unpleasant and undesirable, and it certainly can still be opposed, but at the end of the day, it is Right that it exists for it has a role to play. <br /> <br /> In six movies, SW has told the Western version of Good triumphing over Evil. IF the series must continue, then I would expand it into an Eastern direction. The upcoming movies would examine the true nature of both sides of the Force and what exactly it means to have them in &quot;Balance&quot; (think of the <a href=\"http://www.bing.com/images/search?q=Yin+Yang+Designs&amp;FORM=RSRIMG#a\" target=\"_blank\">Yin-Yang</a>). This would necessitate the revival of the Sith (or at least, some Dark Side users), and their eventually establishing some sort of working relationship with the new Jedi Order Skywalker founds. The easiest way to bring that about would be by introducing a new, third element to threaten both sides...maybe an invasion, like the Yuuzahn Vong, or a cosmic menace, like Abeloth, though obviously not those themselves. <br /> <br /> So, the broadest outline: Movie 1, catch up with Luke and introduce his new Jedi who discover a new Sith threat; ends with suggestions that there's something else out there; Movie 2, Jedi and Sith go into all out war on each other, while the new threat is revealed to the audience as manipulating both. Movie 3, Jedi and Sith realize both have been duped, and reluctantly join forces to defeat new threat. This done, both warily call a cease-fire, which hopefully will build into a lasting peace...<br /> <br /> (Also, aside from the droids, I would ONLY have Luke back...and he dies at the end of part 1 saving the youngsters. The circle is now complete!)<br /> <br /> That's the basic story I would tell, the rest is all details. It may not be the most original or profound idea, but then SW never was, that was never its strength! Of course, I also see that as a Final Ending, and I know Disney is going to want to keep driving this horse until it dies and no one wants to see it anymore, but this is about as far as I care to take it. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T16:10:29-07:00","id":156998,"title":"","content":"Where would I want to take the story? Away from the Jedi. <br /> <br /> One mistake I think that Star Wars made with increasing regularity was that Force users came to be increasingly central to everything, to the point that the galaxy ended up (figuratively) revolving around them. Make the central protagonist of the new Trilogy be a smuggler, or a politician, or a soldier or spy or bounty hunter or any number of other occupations; as long as he or she is <i>not</i> a Jedi, or Sith, or any other sort of Force user. <i>Don\u2019t</i> make him or her strong in the Force; and avoid the temptation to recruit him or her into the ranks of the Jedi as the series progresses. Place all Jedi characters and the like in supporting roles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T19:03:35-07:00","id":157253,"title":"","content":"It's kinda difficult in a way. <i>\u201cDon't be too proud of this technological terror you've constructed. The ability to destroy a planet is insignificant next to the power of the Force.\u201d</i> Just to illustrate that Force users can easily dominate any scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T07:14:36-07:00","id":157801,"title":"","content":"The point though was that the series resolves around the force and its good/evil white hat/black hat premise. They are the most direct reflection of that since for most people they don't have to live with the consequences and restrictions dealing with the Force entails.<br /> <br /> And really the last Trilogies least problem was the number of Jedi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T09:29:25-07:00","id":157958,"title":"","content":"Something from a series that has nothing to do with Star Wars at all. But...Raymond Feist had a series that dealt with black robed sorcerers that were a huge power for the world that they were in. We were treated to a destructive scene involving one of them (Pug/Milamber) unleashing his temper in an arena. In a followup series, we saw that same scene from a different point-of-view (a slave and a noble) and we saw the aftermath which was chaos. (It was a good book)<br /> I don't see why there couldn't be a story with such an alternate view point that could be told well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T09:35:54-07:00","id":157963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=156960#post156960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In six movies, SW has told the Western version of Good triumphing over Evil. IF the series must continue, then I would expand it into an Eastern direction. The upcoming movies would examine the true nature of both sides of the Force and what exactly it means to have them in &quot;Balance&quot; (think of the <a href=\"http://www.bing.com/images/search?q=Yin+Yang+Designs&amp;FORM=RSRIMG#a\" target=\"_blank\">Yin-Yang</a>). This would necessitate the revival of the Sith (or at least, some Dark Side users), and their eventually establishing some sort of working relationship with the new Jedi Order Skywalker founds. The easiest way to bring that about would be by introducing a new, third element to threaten both sides...maybe an invasion, like the Yuuzahn Vong, or a cosmic menace, like Abeloth, though obviously not those themselves.<br /> So, the broadest outline: Movie 1, catch up with Luke and introduce his new Jedi who discover a new Sith threat; ends with suggestions that there's something else out there; Movie 2, Jedi and Sith go into all out war on each other, while the new threat is revealed to the audience as manipulating both. Movie 3, Jedi and Sith realize both have been duped, and reluctantly join forces to defeat new threat. This done, both warily call a cease-fire, which hopefully will build into a lasting peace...<br /> (Also, aside from the droids, I would ONLY have Luke back...and he dies at the end of part 1 saving the youngsters. The circle is now complete!)<br /> That's the basic story I would tell, the rest is all details. It may not be the most original or profound idea, but then SW never was, that was never its strength! Of course, I also see that as a Final Ending, and I know Disney is going to want to keep driving this horse until it dies and no one wants to see it anymore, but this is about as far as I care to take it.<br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=156998#post156998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where would I want to take the story? Away from the Jedi.<br /> <br /> One mistake I think that Star Wars made with increasing regularity was that Force users came to be increasingly central to everything, to the point that the galaxy ended up (figuratively) revolving around them. Make the central protagonist of the new Trilogy be a smuggler, or a politician, or a soldier or spy or bounty hunter or any number of other occupations; as long as he or she is <i>not</i> a Jedi, or Sith, or any other sort of Force user. <i>Don\u2019t</i> make him or her strong in the Force; and avoid the temptation to recruit him or her into the ranks of the Jedi as the series progresses. Place all Jedi characters and the like in supporting roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'd go middle of the road between these two, leaning more towards putting the Jedi in the background.<br /> <br /> While I'm not exactly sure what I'd do, I'd definitely not have the villain of the movies be Sith...again. The Sith are played out, at least for now. So, I like the idea of checking in with the old characters, and then having a new set of characters take off from there. Be it a new generation(i.e. Their children), or just people close to them they're passing the torch to.<br /> <br /> I really wish we're weren't visiting Tattooine in the new movies, but we are...again. Maybe it won't be for long. As much I love the places, the only reason for them to go back in these movies is nostalgia, and that's not the best reason.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'd steer clear of any examination of the Force. It needs to remain mysterious and we need to pretend the term Midicholorian doesn't exist. There was no talk of &quot;Balance to the Force&quot; or lame, undefined prophecies in the OT, so we should avoid that in the new ones as well. Jedi are apart of the universe and should be in the new movies, but keep them alittle lower key like in the OT. Though, the idea of Luke training new Jedi is great, so we should check in on that for sure.<br /> <br /> Though honestly, I think if I had my way, I'd have just made the Thrawn trilogy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think I'm rambling...but you get the idea. Jedi should be there, and maybe be a main character, but the story shouldn't be about the Jedi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</