hewbacca is back. The laughable thing is after they killed him off writers over and over tried to refill his role because it had become such an integral par of Han's own story. It never really panned out though. I was never as upset about his death. For one they dropped a moon on him and he died saving tons of people.<br /> <br /> Mara's death bother me for 3 reasons. First, I liked the character. On her own she was a enjoyable character and had a lot of depth to her. Second, she had been and continued to be the vehicle that finally allow Luke to grow up and continue to do so. Finally, her death was really pathetic. She is struck down in the last few pages of a book and all it signifies is a character finally fully falls to the Dark Side. It was an utter bull shit move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T08:20:23-07:00","id":163606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=163549#post163549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't think, but that might mean Chewbacca is back. The laughable thing is after they killed him off writers over and over tried to refill his role because it had become such an integral par of Han's own story. It never really panned out though. I was never as upset about his death. For one they dropped a moon on him and he died saving tons of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never read that book series because of that. When I heard about them killing Chewie, that's pretty much when I gave up on the EU. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Some good ideas came out of that, don't get me wrong. But killing Chewie, along with that whole series running for like 20 novels just drove me away. I just don't have time to read that much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=163549#post163549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mara's death bother me for 3 reasons. First, I liked the character. On her own she was a enjoyable character and had a lot of depth to her. Second, she had been and continued to be the vehicle that finally allow Luke to grow up and continue to do so. Finally, her death was really pathetic. She is struck down in the last few pages of a book and all it signifies is a character finally fully falls to the Dark Side. It was an utter bull shit move.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I heard about that. Didn't care for what I heard, so again, I didn't read it. Plus, I'm not a huge fan of people killing off someone else's characters..if that makes sense. If Zahn wanted to write a story where he killed her off, that'd be one thing. But just another writer doing it to be shocking, I just don't care for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T08:35:46-07:00","id":163616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=163606#post163606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I heard about that. Didn't care for what I heard, so again, I didn't read it. Plus, I'm not a huge fan of people killing off someone else's characters..if that makes sense. If Zahn wanted to write a story where he killed her off, that'd be one thing. But just another writer doing it to be shocking, I just don't care for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Zahn was livid. He said he had several stories to still write about her and he didn't even know anything about it till after that book came out.<br /> <br /> Dang. I tried looking real quick, but I can't find that interview he did shortly after that happened. It was a good one. He was diplomatic, but at the same time you could tell he was pissed. Here is an even more diplomatic one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First of all, let me remind everyone that none of the writers or artists or gamers owns any of the Star Wars stuff we\u2019ve created. LFL owns it all, and they have every right to maim, kill, or allow to be consumed on the premises anyone they choose. That again was the risk, and the price, we all knew about when we went in.<br /> <br /> That said, I disagree in particular with Mara\u2019s death for a couple of philosophic reasons. (And lest anyone think it\u2019s only because she was my character, I have the same problems with Chewbacca\u2019s death in the NJO series.)<br /> <br /> Star Wars, to me, is an old-fashioned tale of Good v. Evil, with the heroes stepping up to an overwhelming challenge, working through it with sweat and courage and sacrifice, and ultimately winning the day. Part of that is that the chief good guys are alive at the end in order to see their victory.<br /> <br /> I would argue that the movies themselves support this view. If Lucas had been into killing off major characters, either Han or Lando could easily have died in RotJ. (In fact, I understand that Harrison Ford actually requested such a death scene and that Lucas turned him down.)<br /> <br /> I realize that there are times when characters need to die for the plot to work. Obi-Wan, in ANH, is one example. (Though I still suspect Lucas planned to do more with him \u2013 \u201cI shall become more powerful than you can possibly imagine\u201d \u2013 and somehow that plot development never quite jelled.)<br /> <br /> I often hear the argument that having major characters die is more realistic than having them always come through unscathed. Of course it is. But I personally don\u2019t want my fiction to necessarily be \u201crealistic\u201d \u2013 I want my fiction to be entertaining. For me, that means watching engaging characters I care about get into and out of dangerous predicaments, working and thinking together in order to defeat the bad guys. While some authors (and readers) like the tension of wondering who will live and who will die, I prefer the tension of seeing how the heroes are going to think or work their ways out of each difficult or impossible situation they find themselves in. If I want realism and the deaths of people I care about, I can turn on the news.<br /> <br /> Of course, that\u2019s just me. It could very well be that the audience has changed over the years (the word \u201cmatured\u201d is often tossed in at this point), and that they no longer want the sort of books I like to write. If that\u2019s true, so be it. They\u2019ll continue to buy and read the new Star Wars books, and dinosaurs like me will fade gracefully away.<br /> <br /> I also believe that given Mara\u2019s background and character, she was too useful a character for the writers to eliminate. But again, that may just be me. </div> </div> </div>I liked he other response better. Hehe. What he says is kind of how I feel about major character deaths too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:38:02-07:00","id":163683,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=163616#post163616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zahn was livid. He said he had several stories to still write about her and he didn't even know anything about it till after that book came out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awww man, they didn't even give him a heads up? That is pretty shitty...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:46:15-07:00","id":163697,"title":"","content":"I take it you must not care for George R.R. Martin's work then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I agree though, in the case of Star Wars, because of its roots as a modernized version of the archetypal hero myth. In the heroe's journey, important characters don't just die because it's realistic. On the rare occasion that an important character does die, it represents an important step in the hero's growth, like with Owen, Beru, Obi-Wan, and Yoda. Main characters only die because they HAVE to die for the hero's journey to continue. I don't think all, or even most stories should be the hero's journey, but Star Wars should. That's what made it good in the first place, and if they want it to be good again, that's what they need to restore to the series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T14:12:26-07:00","id":163996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=163697#post163697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take it you must not care for George R.R. Martin's work then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not just no but hell no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree though, in the case of Star Wars, because of its roots as a modernized version of the archetypal hero myth. In the heroe's journey, important characters don't just die because it's realistic. On the rare occasion that an important character does die, it represents an important step in the hero's growth, like with Owen, Beru, Obi-Wan, and Yoda. Main characters only die because they HAVE to die for the hero's journey to continue. I don't think all, or even most stories should be the hero's journey, but Star Wars should. That's what made it good in the first place, and if they want it to be good again, that's what they need to restore to the series. </div> </div> </div>Not to mention savage teddy bears wouldn't be taking out elite shock troops and little green guys wouldn't be the wisest and one of the longest lived races in the galaxy. I read/watch fantasy for the fantasy. Heroes don't die they just become legends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T15:18:16-07:00","id":164086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not just no but hell no.</div> </div> </div> </div> A kindred spirit, at least in this regard. (Got to the 4th book and then thought &quot;The hell with this shit.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T17:13:57-07:00","id":164219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=163996#post163996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention savage teddy bears wouldn't be taking out elite shock troops and little green guys wouldn't be the wisest and one of the longest lived races in the galaxy. I read/watch fantasy for the fantasy. Heroes don't die they just become legends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, those things don't really have anything to do with the hero's journey. True enough, they wouldn't happen in &quot;gritty&quot; or &quot;realistic&quot; works, but my point was more that Star Wars was originally more than just fantasy. It was THE monomyth, plot point for plot point, with scifi aesthetics. It's not just that it's fantasy so it doesn't have to be realistic, it's that it directly follows the formula of legends like Hercules or Gilgamesh, and any attempt at Martinesque &quot;realism&quot; would have cheapened that, and gone against the spirit of what it was trying to emulate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T18:01:16-07:00","id":164256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=163379#post163379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, but so is Clone Wars....which I enjoyed for the most part, but there was weirdness in that one. Like that planet the Force originated from, with the siblings fighting each other... That was a hard watch.<br /> <br /> I really liked it early on, but towards the end I wasn't as interested. Still not sure what I think of the Darth Maul and Dathomir stuff.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about Rebels yet....we'll see how it goes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually loved the Mortuus trilogy. If you want some more explanation, from what I gather is the three were either Ancients or part of a group of beings who inhabit a well, spirit world. It brought some mysticism back to the Force. I am grateful to that.<br /> <br /> As for Mara's death? It was shitty, and for shock value. It'd be nice of Zahn got some say in it, but that parts gone now. The book series had many, many good moments, and it'd be worth to salvage some of it. Though, on the other hand, Mara Jade probably doesn't exist anymore. So, that's not much better. =/<br /> <br /> Anyways, on Chewies death. It affected me, but... I thought it was well done enough. I can see how it'd put some people off the EU, however, if a OT character hadn't died, people would complain also and also would have left. So, can't please everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T18:35:40-07:00","id":164279,"title":"","content":"One of the advantages I've always thought was great about the nebulous canon nature of anything not the movies or the shows was that you could cherry pick what you like, write stuff to fill in the blanks, and do your own branch off. I doubt it got that much use, but the idea was still solid in theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T23:10:58-07:00","id":164543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=164256#post164256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I actually loved the Mortuus trilogy. If you want some more explanation, from what I gather is the three were either Ancients or part of a group of beings who inhabit a well, spirit world. It brought some mysticism back to the Force. I am grateful to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very similar to the reason I enjoyed the Dathomir stuff. It made the galaxy feel much bigger and mysterious. I mean, there's the Jedi and the Sith, who basically use the same powers, just mirrored versions of each other. However the Nightsisters were doing what they were doing, it was distinctly different from the &quot;normal&quot; uses of the Force that we've seen everywhere else, and opened the door for the existence of even <i>more</i> strange mystical powers. The Star Wars that Clone Wars is part of is one where the Kaiburr Crystal from <i>Splinter of the Mind's Eye </i>isn't out of place, unlike the later EU, and that would win me over, even if nothing else had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T00:10:15-07:00","id":164571,"title":"","content":"Yep, I liked the Nightsister's arc for much the same reason. It harkens back to the Sorcerers of Tund and other such, stranger, and weird versions of the Force. (Sith alchemy too). It does make the Jedi ways looks constrained, and small compared to the power some of the sorcerers had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T05:29:10-07:00","id":164746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=163697#post163697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take it you must not care for George R.R. Martin's work then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the show Game of Thrones, but I haven't read the books. I don't have as much issue with characters dying there, one because of the setting, and two because he's killing off his own characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=164256#post164256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually loved the Mortuus trilogy. If you want some more explanation, from what I gather is the three were either Ancients or part of a group of beings who inhabit a well, spirit world. It brought some mysticism back to the Force. I am grateful to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, don't get me wrong, I'm glad for the mysticism, but I feel like a strange planet where they think the Force originated from, which has weird siblings, obvious analogies for light side and dark side, fighting was just alittle too far in the other direction for me. The Dathomir stuff was better....I just wish they hadn't made it so Darth Maul was from there. I get they were tying it in so they could pave the way to bring him back...but I wish they didn't have a planet of Darth Mauls..<br /> <br /> I love the Nightsisters stuff though, and that episode where they raised the undead army to fight the droids was admittedly pretty bad ass.<br /> <br /> Though, they're plan to kill Count Dooku was alittle convoluted, when they could easily just poisoned his drink when he arrived to get a new apprentice. They handed him a drink and he just downed it. PUT THE RAT POISON IN THE DRINK! :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=164543#post164543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's very similar to the reason I enjoyed the Dathomir stuff. It made the galaxy feel much bigger and mysterious. I mean, there's the Jedi and the Sith, who basically use the same powers, just mirrored versions of each other. However the Nightsisters were doing what they were doing, it was distinctly different from the &quot;normal&quot; uses of the Force that we've seen everywhere else, and opened the door for the existence of even <i>more</i> strange mystical powers. The Star Wars that Clone Wars is part of is one where the Kaiburr Crystal from <i>Splinter of the Mind's Eye </i>isn't out of place, unlike the later EU, and that would win me over, even if nothing else had.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm no fan of Splinter of the Minds Eye, especially how Darth Vader was portrayed. But I get what you're saying, and I did like it for that. It was nice to see something other Jedi and Sith for a change, and I hope we get something equally cool in the new movies, if different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":24,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","user":"Mr Gone","date":". 06-10-2014, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T09:06:27-07:00","id":164860,"title":"","content":"Personally I hate when they use the force as just magic. The Light/Dark nature and the fact there are limitations to it that you don't normally find in &quot;magic&quot; is what made it unique. When they start making it do anything and everything just because then devalues the impact of those very restrictions. It feels too much like the writer wanted to one up everyone else's characters. Its the literary version of power creep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T15:36:55-07:00","id":165303,"title":"","content":"Oh, there's still a Dark side to it. The Dathromiri way is undoubtedly Dark, and so is Sith sorcery. The Dark Side is more seductive, easier; not more powerful. I think the Dark side having some perverted sorcery shows that. It's not that it's stronger, but it is stranger.<br /> <br /> As for Maul being from Dathromir. What threw me off is I knew the Dathromir as humans. However, as them being human/zabrak mixes, with some pure Zabrak there? I an see it happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T15:42:20-07:00","id":165305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=164746#post164746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, don't get me wrong, I'm glad for the mysticism, but I feel like a strange planet where they think the Force originated from, which has weird siblings, obvious analogies for light side and dark side, fighting was just alittle too far in the other direction for me. The Dathomir stuff was better....I just wish they hadn't made it so Darth Maul was from there. I get they were tying it in so they could pave the way to bring him back...but I wish they didn't have a planet of Darth Mauls..</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea if this is what was intended, but I got the impression that that &quot;planet&quot; and everything on it was exactly as real as the Darth Vader that Luke fought in the cave on Dagobah. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=164746#post164746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the Nightsisters stuff though, and that episode where they raised the undead army to fight the droids was admittedly pretty bad ass.<br /> <br /> Though, they're plan to kill Count Dooku was alittle convoluted, when they could easily just poisoned his drink when he arrived to get a new apprentice. They handed him a drink and he just downed it. PUT THE RAT POISON IN THE DRINK! :P</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I saw it, the Nightsisters' plan to kill Dooku made perfect sense, once I realized that they were implementing a sort of &quot;eye for an eye&quot; style of 'justice'. Dooku betrayed his apprentice, and tried to kill her, so he would be betrayed by his new apprentice, who would then kill <i>him. </i>Symmetry. <br /> (And if they <i>had</i> tried to simply poison him, I wouldn't have been surprised if Dooku had been able to sense the danger he was in. After that, I don't things would have gone well for the Nightsisters.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=164860#post164860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I hate when they use the force as just magic. The Light/Dark nature and the fact there are limitations to it that you don't normally find in &quot;magic&quot; is what made it unique. When they start making it do anything and everything just because then devalues the impact of those very restrictions. It feels too much like the writer wanted to one up everyone else's characters. Its the literary version of power creep.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't mind my asking, what are the limitations you see as being violated here? I don't disagree, they got up to some pretty strange stuff in the EU (that whole time travel Force power, for example), but I don't really see what the issue is with what was done in the Clone Wars series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T17:57:15-07:00","id":165450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=165305#post165305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea if this is what was intended, but I got the impression that that &quot;planet&quot; and everything on it was exactly as real as the Darth Vader that Luke fought in the cave on Dagobah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm....maybe. If thats the case, I Really wish they'd done a better job with it then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=165305#post165305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I saw it, the Nightsisters' plan to kill Dooku made perfect sense, once I realized that they were implementing a sort of &quot;eye for an eye&quot; style of 'justice'. Dooku betrayed his apprentice, and tried to kill her, so he would be betrayed by his new apprentice, who would then kill <i>him. </i>Symmetry.<br /> (And if they <i>had</i> tried to simply poison him, I wouldn't have been surprised if Dooku had been able to sense the danger he was in. After that, I don't things would have gone well for the Nightsisters.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that makes sense, in a twisted logic kind of way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T07:21:24-07:00","id":165887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=165305#post165305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't mind my asking, what are the limitations you see as being violated here? I don't disagree, they got up to some pretty strange stuff in the EU (that whole time travel Force power, for example), but I don't really see what the issue is with what was done in the Clone Wars series.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beside the time travel you mention there was among others shapeshifting and teleporting that just went too much into the &quot;magic&quot; realm. As to violating there was a whole bunch of Grey Side where they could freely mix light and dark without consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":787,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","user":"Sorwen","date":". 06-11-2014, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T11:43:17-07:00","id":166133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=157801#post157801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point though was that the series resolves around the force and its good/evil white hat/black hat premise. They are the most direct reflection of that since for most people they don't have to live with the consequences and restrictions dealing with the Force entails.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this, exactly. The main conflict is the Light and Dark Sides of the Force, which express themselves through the Jedi and Sith, who use the Republic/Rebellion and Separatists/Empire as their weapons. Frankly, anything that gets far away from that is arguably &quot;not Star Wars&quot;. <br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, there are some really cool non-Force users, both in the movies and the EU (love me some Booster Terrik!) I just finished a SW novel that was about Han and Lando pulling an &quot;Oceans 11&quot; style caper with NO Force shenangans whatsoever, and thoroughly enjoyed it! <br /> <br /> BUT. I wouldn't want to see a movie like that. If you take the Force/mystical element from SW, or put it in the backthen you wind up with any of the dozens of SF clones that have flooded tv ever since `77. In fact, I'm amazed that so few shows picked up on the &quot;mystical&quot; element of the movie they were trying to emulate (Battlestar Galactica probably came closest)! <br /> <br /> Basically, any space-based show can give you stories of cool, but regular, people doing cool things in space. It's the Force that sets SW apart from all the rest!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T11:53:52-07:00","id":166143,"title":"","content":"And yeah, I'm starting to really look forward to Rebels. Except that...<br /> <br /> Hm, how to put this: Most people agree that the Prequels were a misfire. So, while they are still canon, it's interesting seeing the approach to the new material. Basically, I see them trying to recapture the feel of the original trilogy. Now, this is smart; but is it *right*? <br /> <br /> Part of me sees this as a cynical &quot;Cue Cullen&quot; attempt to manipulate the fans; but another part simply sees it as giving the fans what they (apparently) want. <br /> <br /> I guess my uneasiness comes down to my post above, about how I would do the new ones; I don't think rehashing the exact same thing is the right way to go, here. Just as the prequels had a different feel to the originals (however well they did or didn't pull it off), I think the new ones should have a different, tho related feel as well. <br /> <br /> But I'm sure Disney is flooding Abrams with memos aimed at &quot;doing just what the original films did.&quot; This is strongly implied by the fact that the original script only had the original heroes as cameos, and they fired that guy, and replaced it with a new script that is apparently full of the old heroes. I think the original treatment would have been better...<br /> <br /> Of course, &quot;Cue Cullens&quot; aren't always bad! Getting John Williams on the project is the FIRST thing I would have done, too! And Rebels, which takes place basically in the same era as the originals, has every reason to have the same mood and tone, so I have no problem with it seeming like them. Also, it looks like it's going for a &quot;Firefly&quot; vibe!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, does any of the above make sense? Sometimes it's hard for me to tell...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T12:14:20-07:00","id":166154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=166143#post166143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yeah, I'm starting to really look forward to Rebels. Except that... Hm, how to put this: Most people agree that the Prequels were a misfire. So, while they are still canon, it's interesting seeing the approach to the new material. Basically, I see them trying to recapture the feel of the original trilogy. Now, this is smart; but is it *right*? Part of me sees this as a cynical &amp;quot;Cue Cullen&amp;quot; attempt to manipulate the fans; but another part simply sees it as giving the fans what they (apparently) want. I guess my uneasiness comes down to my post above, about how I would do the new ones; I don't think rehashing the exact same thing is the right way to go, here. Just as the prequels had a different feel to the originals (however well they did or didn't pull it off), I think the new ones should have a different, tho related feel as well. But I'm sure Disney is flooding Abrams with memos aimed at &amp;quot;doing just what the original films did.&amp;quot; This is strongly implied by the fact that the original script only had the original heroes as cameos, and they fired that guy, and replaced it with a new script that is apparently full of the old heroes. I think the original treatment would have been better... Of course, &amp;quot;Cue Cullens&amp;quot; aren't always bad! Getting John Williams on the project is the FIRST thing I would have done, too! And Rebels, which takes place basically in the same era as the originals, has every reason to have the same mood and tone, so I have no problem with it seeming like them. Also, it looks like it's going for a &amp;quot;Firefly&amp;quot; vibe!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Anyway, does any of the above make sense? Sometimes it's hard for me to tell...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Makes sense. It's a tough line to walk between doing something new and original at the risk of losing the feel of the originals, versus sticking to what worked before at the risk of sticking too close and just being more of the same. I still stand by my opinion that it's the mythological roots that makes Star Wars so good. That's where that mysticism of the force comes from, it's the supernatural aid, the elixir. But if they tried to do the hero's journey again it would just be the same movies with slightly different details. But the hero's journey is not the only archetypal myth out there. If they pick another one and Star Wars it up, they'll have another great film trilogy. Of course, that's all the films. I think Rebels should stay away from that and create its own identity. What works for movies and what works for television are not the same things. I think a firefly-esque episodic serial adventure in the Star Wars universe would be great, Force or no Force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T12:36:06-07:00","id":171894,"title":"","content":"One video I saw that was criticizing the newer movies claimed that &quot;Star Wars is a Western&quot;. Well, kinda...but it's also a WWII dueling aces movie, and a samurai movie, etc...<br /> <br /> Which makes me wonder: SW is essentially a combo of all the things that George Lucas loved, mixed together into a coherent whole. It's his genuine *passion* for these things that rings true, and that audiences responded to. BUT--now that SW is in different hands, should they stay true to those influences, and risk the new movies being shallow copies? Or follow their own passions, and risk them being unrecognizable as SW?<br /> <br /> When I ask myself, for instance, what are MY influences, things that I'm passionate about, I answer Superhero Comics, Kaiju movies, Anime/Manga, Shakespeare, RPGs, the Victorian Era, Film Noir, Wuxia, just to start. If I make my SW movies reflecting the above in some way, would you enjoy them? Rather, would you recognize them as &quot;true Star Wars&quot;?<br /> <br /> Along similar lines, why should the technology in the new movies be the same as the old? Surely there would have been some advances? Would it throw you too much if the new movies had teleporters, personal forcefields/cloaking devices, antigrav units enabling anyone to make great leaps, powered armor, shapeshifting starfighters, talking, shipboard AIs? Where should that line be drawn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T13:31:20-07:00","id":171951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=171894#post171894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">personal forcefields/cloaking devices</div> </div> </div> </div>These already existed at a certain point in the Old Republic, if the items in the Knights of the Old Republic games are valid references.<br /> <br /> In general, though, considering the gigantic span of time from the Old Republic stuff to post-movie-timeline material, it seems that technology in the Star Wars universe is pretty static, advancing at an <i>incredibly</i> slow pace. Looking at weapons, droids, starships...there is almost no significant difference in technology after <i>thousands</i> of years. So a few decades between the original trilogy and the new movies likely shouldn't see much advance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T14:21:24-07:00","id":172031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=171951#post171951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These already existed at a certain point in the Old Republic, if the items in the Knights of the Old Republic games are valid references.<br /> <br /> In general, though, considering the gigantic span of time from the Old Republic stuff to post-movie-timeline material, it seems that technology in the Star Wars universe is pretty static, advancing at an <i>incredibly</i> slow pace. Looking at weapons, droids, starships...there is almost no significant difference in technology after <i>thousands</i> of years. So a few decades between the original trilogy and the new movies likely shouldn't see much advance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yea, can't remember where I read it, but for thousands of years the tech in the Star Wars Universe reached it's peak. Thats why everything in the OT has that lived in feel(or that was their excuse anyway). I love the idea of that too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T20:12:42-07:00","id":172323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=171894#post171894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where should that line be drawn?</div> </div> </div> </div> At some point, it loses the <i>feel</i> of Star Wars and just becomes another generic sci-fi. They should avoid having things that take away from that Star Wars <i>feel</i>. I'm not sure where that is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T21:16:52-07:00","id":172350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=172031#post172031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yea, can't remember where I read it, but for thousands of years the tech in the Star Wars Universe reached it's peak. Thats why everything in the OT has that lived in feel(or that was their excuse anyway). I love the idea of that too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...<br /> <br /> 1) The real (meta) reason for the KOTOR setting being nearly identical to the current age is...pretty much what we're discussing now. The lack of innovation in setting is because of that same lack out of setting, because the creators are (prob justifiably) concerned with losing that SW *feel*. &quot;Realistically*, the tech should be VERY different...at the very least, Droids shouldn't exist and travel times should be much longer. I really can't imagine why a society so huge, and with so many intelligent life forms should remain so stagnant for so long...unless some force were keeping them that way, which could be a good EU plothook.<br /> <br /> 2) But I'm disregarding that anyway, since this discussion is about the new movies, which are also disregarding that part of the EU (for now/as far as we know/etc). The 6 movies only cover 30-40 years, there could very well have been significant jumps in tech in the decades before Phantom Menace!<br /> <br /> 3) I don't think the &quot;lived in&quot; look in the OT had anything to do with the general tech level and more to do with the fact that, well, people lived in/around the machinery. Although, for all that everyone praises the OT for that, if you reeeally look at it, ONLY the Falcon really lived up to it! Well, to be accurate, the first part of New Hope does, with Luke's home and the spaceport, as well. After that, pretty much *every set* you see for the next two movies is as clean and spit polished as anything you ever saw on Star Trek!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T07:20:48-07:00","id":172780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=171951#post171951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These already existed at a certain point in the Old Republic, if the items in the Knights of the Old Republic games are valid references.<br /> <br /> In general, though, considering the gigantic span of time from the Old Republic stuff to post-movie-timeline material, it seems that technology in the Star Wars universe is pretty static, advancing at an <i>incredibly</i> slow pace. Looking at weapons, droids, starships...there is almost no significant difference in technology after <i>thousands</i> of years. So a few decades between the original trilogy and the new movies likely shouldn't see much advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for the original Star Wars think of it like Germany after WWII but in reverse. Germany was pushing a lot of tech at the time and we were all trying to keep up and surpass. Then we won and Germany lost a lot of that and was split up.<br /> <br /> That reflection in reverse can be seen in Star Wars. You had a highly technological &quot;free&quot; market to one where it was almost totally controlled by the Empire after they were through blasting any opposition to their rule. Tech is going to fall back and progress stagnate as they keep a strangle hold on the best. You general market isn't going to grow by much if at all. Many would take to supporting the status quo. Then after that regime is gone it would start to grow again.<br /> <br /> As to the thousand years you have more the fall of Rome in a way. Tech did advance, but not in leaps and bounds. Also don't forget that there were a lot of various small resets over the years because the Republic also had a lot of wars. While the Old Republic would be the biggest I know of till its fall the Sith would come back in various ways off and on. And while unlike Rome they were not expanding through conquest, but they were growing and they grew very decadent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T09:10:28-07:00","id":172883,"title":"","content":"From a logical and thinking-about-actual-history-and-actual-human-behavior perspective you are likely right, Sorwen. But fiction doesn't always go with that and I'd say the source material disagrees you assertion*.<br /> <br /> Take any Star Wars thing set at <i>any** </i>point in the multiple thousand years of the timeline and, while empires (and republics) may rise and fall, overall the technological level is nearly the same thoroughly.<br /> Innovations can be found here and there, some technologies are seemingly lost with time (as one could expect in 1000s of years) but to a large extent the most pervasive technologies like droids, blasters, vehicles*** and so on stay just about the same at all points.<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Disclaimer</b>: my knowledge of the Expanded Universe is limited. There are a lot of novels I have not read, games I have not played and so on. So I may have missed things that make my statement false. Feel free to correct me.</span><br /> <br /> **<span style=\"font-size:10px\">Except maybe some things from very early in the timeline, though only the early Lightsabers with their external battery belts come to mind. But from well-established old Republic onward, things get static.</span><br /> <br /> ***<span style=\"font-size:10px\">The Star Wars Saga RPG had a clever little way of sneaking-in some advancement in Starships without making play at earlier eras feel much different. Stats for ships from, say, Old Republic and &quot;modern&quot; ones were comparable, but if you flew an ancient ship in &quot;current&quot; times, that ship got a template that made it worse in comparison to the newer model. Still, slight improvements aside, it is still the same technologies: large blasters, tractor beams, the same sort of missiles, no noticeable difference in types of sensors... </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T15:43:10-07:00","id":173271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=172350#post172350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) The real (meta) reason for the KOTOR setting being nearly identical to the current age is...pretty much what we're discussing now. The lack of innovation in setting is because of that same lack out of setting, because the creators are (prob justifiably) concerned with losing that SW *feel*. &quot;Realistically*, the tech should be VERY different...at the very least, Droids shouldn't exist and travel times should be much longer. I really can't imagine why a society so huge, and with so many intelligent life forms should remain so stagnant for so long...unless some force were keeping them that way, which could be a good EU plothook.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have used that as a plot point in a game one time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for why a society might get so stagnant, hard to say. But, just imagine if an alien race showed up with space ships. It'd be a huge leap for us, but we'd only basically be copying their tech. Eventually, we'd hit a point where it isn't any better than what it was based on. So, I could totally see technology hitting a point where it's just so common place, and everyone just copies whats already there, that you lose the innovation.<br /> <br /> Its actually kind of sad to think about...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=172350#post172350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) But I'm disregarding that anyway, since this discussion is about the new movies, which are also disregarding that part of the EU (for now/as far as we know/etc). The 6 movies only cover 30-40 years, there could very well have been significant jumps in tech in the decades before Phantom Menace!</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=172350#post172350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) I don't think the &quot;lived in&quot; look in the OT had anything to do with the general tech level and more to do with the fact that, well, people lived in/around the machinery. Although, for all that everyone praises the OT for that, if you reeeally look at it, ONLY the Falcon really lived up to it! Well, to be accurate, the first part of New Hope does, with Luke's home and the spaceport, as well. After that, pretty much *every set* you see for the next two movies is as clean and spit polished as anything you ever saw on Star Trek!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to a point. Some of the stuff on Hoth didn't look that great. It's mainly cloud city and Imperial stuff that looks so shiny... But I get what you mean. But, I was more meaning how the technology is incidental to the story. It feels lived in because no one feels the need to explain anything technologically. All the tech simply is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T21:18:50-07:00","id":175759,"title":"","content":"Yeah Hoth looked very much like something that had been built in a short amount of time and was very ad-hoc in its look. Which sums up a lot of the Rebel Alliance in the films. The Yavin Moon Base, the Hoth Base, their ships looked like they were either made on the cheap or re-purposed from a non-military role. For instance Ackbar's flagship, <i>Home One</i>, was a civilian vessel that was later on turned into a military one.<br /> <br /> And It'd like to point that while the technology in the KotOR and Film eras are similar the technology of KotOR generally looks more primitive. Look at the protocol droids between the eras. In the films they look pretty human-like while in those games they're much cruder and primitive in their appearance. As for travel time, which I assume you mean Hyperspace/Light Speed/FTL/whatever, we don't really have an accurate measure measure of it either era as in both the films and games they gloss over that for the sake of the story and gameplay respectively.<br /> <br /> It's also worth nothing that the most advanced race in the KotOR era, who designed and created the original infrastructure of the planet-spanning city that is Coruscant, the Gree were in severe decline by the time of the Empire, becoming little more than caretakers of their technology and wonders at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T10:57:32-07:00","id":176194,"title":"","content":"Pretty much everything in the last two movies looks like a set to me (well-done ones, tho), even when it has an &quot;incomplete&quot; feel like the Hoth base. There's a fan legend that Lucas was displeased by the standard clean looks of the Falcon and the Lars farm sets and went around personally kicking and scuffing stuff up to get that used, lived in look. I don't think anyone did that in the later films...Maaaybe Jabba's palace and barge looks like that, I'll have to go back and rewatch (yeah, like I need a reason to see Slave Leia again!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).<br /> <br /> As far as the tech goes, tracing the development of such things is hard enough just dealing with one species over 6 thousand years; doing it for multiple alien races, over an entire galaxy for tens of thousands of years?! Yeah, there's no &quot;realistic&quot; basis to do that with, even if you assume all the aliens are essentially psychologically identical to humans (which they shouldn't be), so we pretty much have to handwave the whole thing. And since SW isn't &quot;real&quot; SF anyway, it's not like the tech stuff really matters, but it's still something that bugs me when the KOTOR era is brought up.<br /> <br /> Still, I'd like to learn more about the Techno Union from ep II...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T11:07:00-07:00","id":176197,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.bleedingcool.com/2014/06/20/rian-johnson-to-write-and-direct