"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T12:52:54-07:00","id":188879,"title":"","content":"Hey, I'll be fine with any Star Wars movie as long as they don't say the Dark Side is fed by negative emotions and the Light Side is fed by positive emotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T13:07:53-07:00","id":188884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=188879#post188879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I'll be fine with any Star Wars movie as long as they don't say the Dark Side is fed by negative emotions and the Light Side is fed by positive emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div> Correct me if I'm wrong, but I thought any strong emotion could amplify one's Force abilities, but the Sith teach that positive emotions are dangerous because they make one weak, while the Jedi teach that all emotions are dangerous because of some convoluted x leads to y leads to z hand waving. That may just be my own head canon though, since I always saw the Force as a neutral thing - an energy field that surrounds us, binds us, and penetrates us - and that &quot;light&quot; and &quot;dark&quot; are more about how you use it than some objective quality about different force powers. <br /> <br /> Ok, maybe I didn't so much interpret it that way as stick my fingers in my ears and say &quot;la la la I can't hear you!&quot; every time canon material talked about the light side and dark side like they were two separate, diametrically opposed Forces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T12:38:31-07:00","id":192635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=188027#post188027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Eli Roth, but yea, doesn't need to work on Star Wars.<br /> <br /> That reminds me, what was that Star Wars book about zombies that came out a bit back ago? Can't think of the title...but I wondered how it was.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ummm, there were two. One in the Old Republic and one about the Imperial project using the old sith's records. Death Troopers was the one set (After I think?) the OT, and Red Harvest was set during the Old Republic era. I read Red Harvest, and personally found it enjoyable. But I also found the Plagueis book to be the best EU book ever. So, there's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 07-11-2014, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T19:47:48-07:00","id":193013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong, but I thought any strong emotion could amplify one's Force abilities, but the Sith teach that positive emotions are dangerous because they make one weak, while the Jedi teach that all emotions are dangerous because of some convoluted x leads to y leads to z hand waving. That may just be my own head canon though, since I always saw the Force as a neutral thing - an energy field that surrounds us, binds us, and penetrates us - and that &quot;light&quot; and &quot;dark&quot; are more about how you use it than some objective quality about different force powers.</div> </div> </div> </div> I thought that was how the Jedi developed such problems to begin with; the idea that emotions were dangerous altogether. The code was changed from <i>Emotion, yet peace</i> to...<i>There is no emotion, only peace</i>...Which was wrong.<br /> At least that's how I saw it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":".  clarification 07-09-2014, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T22:34:28-07:00","id":193176,"title":"","content":"For the Sith, it's<i> Peace is a lie, there is only passion</i>. For the Jedi, it's <i>There is no emotion, there is only peace</i>.<br /> <br /> Subtle distinctions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T22:39:00-07:00","id":193179,"title":"","content":"And yet, it\u2019s always <i>presented</i> as \u201cJedi <i>good</i>; Sith <i>eeevil\u2026\u201d</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T23:26:56-07:00","id":193210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=193179#post193179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, it\u2019s always <i>presented</i> as \u201cJedi <i>good</i>; Sith <i>eeevil\u2026\u201d</i></div> </div> </div> </div>And to most of the Galaxy it's only a question of tactics. Sith are brutal, but straightforward. You have something a Sith wants, the Sith takes it. you oppose the Sith, they kill you. This is hardly nice or good but it's moderately predictable.<br /> <br /> The Jedi are indirect. They always present as being friendly, even if they are there to steal information. They will break into anywhere they want, and this includes using jedi powers to control the minds of innocent guards. They will claim diplomatic immunity and claim to being impartial when it suits their needs. Even if you do nothing to offend a visiting jedi and all your actions are fairly &quot;clean&quot; there's a very good chance they'll manipulate things so your business is shut down... and they will do this all the while smiling and being polite and even claiming there is nothing they can do because it would violate the law... like breaking and entering, stealing state secrets and mentally assaulting civilians and military personnel isn't.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T23:37:16-07:00","id":193214,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a bit like the Vorlons and the Shadows. Now all we need it a Sheridan-like figure to tell them both to \u201cget the hell out of our galaxy!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T03:23:03-07:00","id":193335,"title":"","content":"I feel as though the whole Jedi thing became overburdened and confused by all the sorts of Expanded Universe additions supplemented by Prequel movie stuff.<br /> <br /> Like, the idea that Jedi are supposed to be unemotional, where was that in the original movies?<br /> <br /> I don't think the idea that the Jedi were ultimately kind of dubious and cloistered really added much to the concept, nor the usual kitschy idea of &quot;oh, the good and bad guys are basically the same maaaaaaaan&quot;.<br /> <br /> It might be kind of worse for the Sith as well, where they're not only excessively detailed, but their details are pretty stupid (and yet we're supposed to buy that this group is endlessly recurring through all of history). Like, were the Emperor and Darth Vader really enhanced by the idea that they were adherents of this kind of ideological position on evil and treachery? That they kind of conspired against each other as a matter of what they were rather than who they were?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T05:41:33-07:00","id":193433,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=193335#post193335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, the idea that Jedi are supposed to be unemotional, where was that in the original movies?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it was Yoda in the Empire Strikes Back. He says some things that struck me as...a bit off. I'll have to look for it later but it seemed to me that for the Jedi passions were repressed to the point of being buried. Where as the Sith let those passions rule them. And I felt that either side just simply took this to extremes, when said passions should be controlled, not repressed. I was glad to read that Luke got married. Love is a passion that should burn free in such a union.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=193335#post193335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be kind of worse for the Sith as well, where they're not only excessively detailed, but their details are pretty stupid (and yet we're supposed to buy that this group is endlessly recurring through all of history). Like, were the Emperor and Darth Vader really enhanced by the idea that they were adherents of this kind of ideological position on evil and treachery? That they kind of conspired against each other as a matter of what they were rather than who they were?</div> </div> </div> </div>Evil for its own sake is an idea that is really annoying to me as it's not believable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T08:08:41-07:00","id":193625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=193335#post193335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though the whole Jedi thing became overburdened and confused by all the sorts of Expanded Universe additions supplemented by Prequel movie stuff.<br /> <br /> Like, the idea that Jedi are supposed to be unemotional, where was that in the original movies?<br /> <br /> I don't think the idea that the Jedi were ultimately kind of dubious and cloistered really added much to the concept, nor the usual kitschy idea of &quot;oh, the good and bad guys are basically the same maaaaaaaan&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was on the posters for Episode Two. THer might have been more, but I don't remember. I've avoided the prequels after I was done with my director phase.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=193179#post193179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, it\u2019s always <i>presented</i> as \u201cJedi <i>good</i>; Sith <i>eeevil\u2026\u201d</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, let's be fair-a person's passions<i> are</i> more likely to run amuk than to stay pure. If you could keep passion geared in the right direction, the Sith would be a better choice, but passion resists steering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T09:16:12-07:00","id":193692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=193335#post193335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be kind of worse for the Sith as well, where they're not only excessively detailed, but their details are pretty stupid (and yet we're supposed to buy that this group is endlessly recurring through all of history). Like, were the Emperor and Darth Vader really enhanced by the idea that they were adherents of this kind of ideological position on evil and treachery? That they kind of conspired against each other as a matter of what they were rather than who they were?</div> </div> </div> </div>The best analysis of this I ever heard was that the Sith are basically full of it, and that their philosophy on passion and freedom is just empty words to justify selfish behavior. The Jedi made the mistake of taking them seriously and defining themselves in opposition to both those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T09:56:44-07:00","id":193740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evil for its own sake is an idea that is really annoying to me as it's not believable</div> </div> </div> </div> I take it you mean &quot;evil for its own sake&quot; as the same thing I'm complaining about, rather than imagining it as the thing that I feel the Emperor and Vader were and should have been, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T10:20:57-07:00","id":193755,"title":"","content":"Yes. We are in agreement. *raises a toast*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T10:35:35-07:00","id":193778,"title":"","content":"*twirls mustache* *poisons drinks* <br /> [if Sith make comment about getting revenge on the Jedi] [If Jedi make comment about stopping a danger to the galaxy] [else if not Jedi or Sith mention something about doing it for the 'lullz']","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T11:15:20-07:00","id":193798,"title":"","content":"*starts singing*<br /> <img src=\"http://www.kurts-smilies.de/trink4.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <i>All you need is love...love...</i><br /> <br /> What the hell ...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T13:45:32-07:00","id":193935,"title":"","content":"I don't know much about Star Wars beyond the original three, but I know someone here can explain for me. Why is there always only two Sith?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T14:07:17-07:00","id":193962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=193935#post193935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about Star Wars beyond the original three, but I know someone here can explain for me. Why is there always only two Sith?</div> </div> </div> </div>By the expanded universe information, which is now non-canon so take with a grain of salt...<br /> <br /> There didn't used to be. The Rule of Two (A master and an apprentice) was put in place by a Sith lord that came to the realization that power hungry sith (and they're all power hungry) are massively destructive as they try to kill each other off (for more power natch).<br /> <br /> There used to be massive wars where sith fleets would take over whole sectors and build small empires only to fall apart due to infighting among the leaders. So the Rule of Two. Which is more of a guideline really since every bloody Sith lord since it was developed has broken it. But that's just how Sith do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So the basic way it works, there is a master. they get an apprentice from wherever. They train them. Either the apprentice tries to kill them and the master is irked enough to kill the apprentice starting the cycle over again, or else the apprentice wins and becomes the new master. Who then goes out and finds an apprentice to train up.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T14:22:04-07:00","id":193977,"title":"","content":"On Sith I think it is a matter of just what appeals. Think how many Dictators go down almost the exact same road. That type of mind produces common results. There will be variations, but there were be more things in common in their results if not the approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T14:41:42-07:00","id":193988,"title":"","content":"I think whichever side runs things long enough, is considered something of a success. An empire won't last forever. But one that lasts for at least a few generations can be considered a qualified success. Sith are more upfront rulers, where as the Jedi seem to prefer a more subtle approach. Hmm..indeed, I can see the Jedi in a negative light....my rage at such COWARDICE....WHERE'S MY RED LIGHT SABRE???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T15:41:48-07:00","id":194030,"title":"","content":"Real Sith use purple lightsabers.<br /> <br /> THat makes the prequel trilogy a lot more entertaining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T15:52:20-07:00","id":194038,"title":"","content":"Stolen from elsewhere (an acquaintance of mine wrote it I think) ;<br /> <br /> <i>Dear Unnamed;<br /> <br /> My family has been Sith and involved with the <b>Dark Side </b>for generations. My great grandfather was Darth Bastage responsible for slaughtering an entire city of Gungans just for kicks. Needless to say, they expect me to continue the family line as a Sith Lord being strong with the <b>Dark Side</b>. And for a long while I thought that was what I wanted.<br /> <br /> But one night while at the Backstab Academy, a &quot;friend&quot; and I were up late smoking some midichlorians, and we got a little ... you know, &quot;experimental.&quot; Long story short, I'm ashamed to admit it, but we saved a Wookie from being eaten by a Tuk'atak. I'm not sure how to say this, but it just felt &quot;right&quot;. (Freaking weird, I know!) So we started fooling around with the <i>Light Side</i> of the force more and more.<br /> <br /> Now I'm confused as to which side I really am. Should I come out of the closet to my family and admit that I might be <i>Light Side</i>? (Or as they put it, The Wrong Side) My Mother alone is likely to kill everything within a parsec if I do. Often I feel like I have pure hate and fury in my heart, but then sometimes I think there really is no emotion, only peace. But then I remember the Sith code that says peace is a lie. Sometimes I think I swing both ways and I'm really a Revanite.<br /> <br /> What should I do?<br /> <br /> Signed,<br /> Damned if I do, damned if I don't.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T21:55:00-07:00","id":194336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=194038#post194038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Dear Unnamed;<br /> <br /> My family has been Sith and involved with the <b>Dark Side </b>for generations. My great grandfather was Darth Bastage responsible for slaughtering an entire city of Gungans just for kicks. Needless to say, they expect me to continue the family line as a Sith Lord being strong with the <b>Dark Side</b>. And for a long while I thought that was what I wanted.<br /> <br /> But one night while at the Backstab Academy, a &quot;friend&quot; and I were up late smoking some midichlorians, and we got a little ... you know, &quot;experimental.&quot; Long story short, I'm ashamed to admit it, but we saved a Wookie from being eaten by a Tuk'atak. I'm not sure how to say this, but it just felt &quot;right&quot;. (Freaking weird, I know!) So we started fooling around with the <i>Light Side</i> of the force more and more.<br /> <br /> Now I'm confused as to which side I really am. Should I come out of the closet to my family and admit that I might be <i>Light Side</i>? (Or as they put it, The Wrong Side) My Mother alone is likely to kill everything within a parsec if I do. Often I feel like I have pure hate and fury in my heart, but then sometimes I think there really is no emotion, only peace. But then I remember the Sith code that says peace is a lie. Sometimes I think I swing both ways and I'm really a Revanite.<br /> <br /> What should I do?<br /> <br /> Signed,<br /> Damned if I do, damned if I don't.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Dear... What was this one's name again? Oh never mind. Didi. Yes that'll do. Dear Didi.<br /> <br /> Blah blah family linage? Generations? That's the start of your problem right there. Look, only wimpy Sith have family lines. You know what we call family in the Academy? A WEAKNESS. Whatever else you do, you should make a point of killing your parents and grandparents as far back as you can. Siblings too. If you have your eye on the prize you can't afford to have a moment of weakness such as what comes from family.<br /> <br /> Make yourself an Orphan, it's what works. It's also classic, like wearing black. Never goes out of style.<br /> <br /> Now blah blah blah, saved a Wookie., blah blah angst angst doubt, think you're going light side.... <br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> BHWAHAHAAHAHAHAHAHA!!! By the Dark side that was a good laugh. Oh wait, you're actually serious. Are you guys shitting me? This is a real letter? What are they teaching kids these days?<br /> <br /> Okay, clearly your education in the Dark side has been woefully lacking, possibly due to those wimpy &quot;parents&quot; that brought you up in the wading pool they laughingly consider the Dark side. Do you know what the Number One Rule of being a Sith steeped in the Dark Side is? It's You. Do. What.You. Want. If someone tries to stop you from doing what you want, you kill them. If someone more powerful than you tries to stop you, you maneuver you way around 'em until you can kill 'em.<br /> <br /> So you wanna save a Wookiee 'cause it amuses you to do so? Do it. You wanna toss a Wookiee into a sarlacc pit? Do it. That's just icing on the cake of what you are. Worried you're turning Jedi? Bleh, you know what separates us from the Jedi? We know that we have the power to reach out and take the galaxy by the short and curlies... and we do it. That's why some of the most powerful Sith started out as Jedi, because they were shown first hand with all the diplomacy and backstabbing that the universe is just a huge pile of fightin' dogs. And that YOU have the biggest fangs on the block.<br /> <br /> So Deedee or whatever, time for you to put on the big girl pants, and act like a proper Sith. Stop caring what other people think of you. Hell, if Vader could make phone grade heavy breathing into something to feared instead of mocked, you can do anything. Kill off that family that sounds like it's holding you back. Let the emotion flow through you and give you strength.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yours, etc etc etc<br /> <br /> Darth Lord Zh'mby Muhuse","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T21:59:48-07:00","id":194340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode