//forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T14:44:23-07:00","id":194996,"title":"","content":"Yeah; Jar Jar makes Boss Nass look <i>good</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T16:17:18-07:00","id":195094,"title":"","content":"Look, I'ma gonna say three things y'all will heavily disagree with.<br /> <br /> 1)I like the Gungans. I'm sorry, I do. I don't think they're bad in and of themselves, and while they're involvement in the final fight is a little Ewok-y, on the whole I like them well enough.<br /> 2)I don't hate Jar Jar Binks. Yes,I know he's mind-boggling,teeth-gratingly bad for most people, and I won't defend him on that front because the elements are right, but Jar Jar never really bothered me.<br /> 3)I don't hate Boss Nass. If anything, his problem is that I don't even think of him when I think on the prequels.He's just not there enough for me to give a shit. The guy who arrests Jar Jar has more impact in my mind.<br /> <br /> There. Castigate me if you will, but I just don't hate these things. Do I think Jar Jar was a mistake? Yes. Do I think Boss Nass was a mistake? I actually don't care. Do I think the Gungans are a mistake? No, not at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T16:47:58-07:00","id":195107,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"http://postimage.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://s3.postimg.org/klrcrhbin/mob.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>...oh, well. At least you are sorry for it <a href=\"http://postimage.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://s3.postimg.org/8mfuk65xr/image.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T16:48:14-07:00","id":195108,"title":"","content":"You are evil and must be stopped. And if the Jedi aren't willing to do it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T17:01:13-07:00","id":195110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=193335#post193335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though the whole Jedi thing became overburdened and confused by all the sorts of Expanded Universe additions supplemented by Prequel movie stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or is that the other way around?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, the idea that Jedi are supposed to be unemotional, where was that in the original movies? </div> </div> </div>Mainly during Luke's training in Empire, where Yoda tells him how hate and anger lead to the quicker, more seductive solutions of the Dark Side. And how he will be able to tell the good from the bad when he is calm and at peace...<br /> <br /> An interesting point I think a lot of people miss, because Yoda and Obi-Wan are presented as so cool and wise, is that they were ultimately <i>wrong</i>. It is, instead, Luke who is right about the Dark Side NOT forever dominating your path, and that redemption from it is indeed possible. <br /> <br /> The EU books kind of run with this, as they openly have Yoda realizing that the Jedi had grown stagnant and somewhat...corrupt is a strong word, but they were losing their way (he does have a speech to this effect in Ep III), and he intends for Luke to restart the Order, in his own way, without repeating the mistakes of the past, hence why Jedi are allowed to marry and have families in the NJO...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T17:02:03-07:00","id":195111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=192635#post192635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ummm, there were two. One in the Old Republic and one about the Imperial project using the old sith's records. Death Troopers was the one set (After I think?) the OT, and Red Harvest was set during the Old Republic era. I read Red Harvest, and personally found it enjoyable. But I also found the Plagueis book to be the best EU book ever. So, there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah cool. I didn't know there were two of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T17:04:12-07:00","id":195113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=193935#post193935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about Star Wars beyond the original three, but I know someone here can explain for me. Why is there always only two Sith?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You've already gotten the in-universe answer, but I myself have often wondered about the &quot;real&quot; or Meta-reason for this. Near as I can figure, it's simply because there were two Sith in the original series (even though the word &quot;Sith&quot; never appears in it!) and someone thought that needed explaining. <br /> <br /> I'm sure most fans will assume that that's a bad thing, but it has led to some interesting stories...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T17:06:05-07:00","id":195114,"title":"","content":"Those Sith letters are amusing! Esp considering that the first one is essentially what happens with Ben Skywalker's Sith &quot;girlfriend&quot; from the Lost Tribe of the Sith...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T17:10:52-07:00","id":195116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=195094#post195094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I'ma gonna say three things y'all will heavily disagree with.<br /> [snip]<br /> There. Castigate me if you will, but I just don't hate these things. Do I think Jar Jar was a mistake? Yes. Do I think Boss Nass was a mistake? I actually don't care. Do I think the Gungans are a mistake? No, not at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who honestly doesn't hate the Prequels in general, and even likes elements of them, I commend you, for having the gumption to stand against the prevailing popular opinion! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://0.media.collegehumor.cvcdn.com/40/12/b11be4e2f03dbe3918e8644c7ca80cd7-star-wars-han-solo.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T18:01:52-07:00","id":195150,"title":"","content":"Thanks Omega.<br /> <br /> As for Shadow, well, you know. Someone has to be evil.[WARNING: Arcane is more Neutral/Chaotic Good/Neutral than Evil, but will totally propagate and take advantage of the assumption. Be wary of his trickery.]<br /> <br /> But in all seriousness, I get it. I get why people don't like these things.I don't even think they're wrong. It just isn't a big issue for <i>me</i>.<br /> <br /> I still hate the prequels, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T19:57:57-07:00","id":195203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=195113#post195113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You've already gotten the in-universe answer, but I myself have often wondered about the &quot;real&quot; or Meta-reason for this. Near as I can figure, it's simply because there were two Sith in the original series (even though the word &quot;Sith&quot; never appears in it!) and someone thought that needed explaining.<br /> <br /> I'm sure most fans will assume that that's a bad thing, but it has led to some interesting stories...</div> </div> </div> </div>not really, or at least not people able to sit back and look at things objectively. So much stuff ended up getting twisted around and changed even as the first three movies progressed that it's crazy. The only reason Luke and LIea are brother and sister? The audience responded better to the Bad Boy Han than the original character that was going to rescue (and marry/pair up/mate/whatever) the princess didn't do as well. Result, need a reason to toss a metaphorical bucket of water on those two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T20:31:46-07:00","id":195217,"title":"","content":"Yeah, probably why we were getting promotional photos like <a href=\"http://img2.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20070114235637/starwars/images/1/1c/Leia_luke_kiss.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> right before the movie that would make the Big Reveal about those two...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> When Borders was closing, I found a book I still kick myself for not buying: It was a huge hardcover book about the making of Star Wars, but it was written by a journalist who had been given unprecedented access to Lucasfilm's archives, and who did not hesitate to call George Lucas on his bullshit! The book had photocopies of many dated letters, scripts and other such evidence to prove when certain ideas came into being (for ex, he concludes that there's pretty much no way Lucas knew Vader was Luke's father until sometime after Empire was being revised). Man, there was so much more I could have learned from that book why didn't I get it arglebargle!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T20:35:26-07:00","id":195220,"title":"","content":"Because Prometheus didn't hand out the gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T19:39:51-07:00","id":203391,"title":"","content":"Well, looks like the recent trend of leaked info has hit the SW galaxy: <a href=\"http://www.ign.com/articles/2014/07/21/this-is-the-rumored-plot-for-star-wars-episode-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the plot of Episode 7!!</a> (Maybe.)<br /> <br /> Needless to say, <b>S P O I L E R S ! ! !</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T19:44:34-07:00","id":203393,"title":"","content":"Wow... Just learned about <a href=\"http://www.ign.com/articles/2014/07/21/this-is-the-rumored-plot-for-star-wars-episode-7\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> from this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DeTBuQe-lXU\" data-code=\"DeTBuQe-lXU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/DeTBuQe-lXU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I hope the rumor's wrong...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T20:34:37-07:00","id":203421,"title":"","content":"I had the same initial ideas that vidblogger did...but on reflection, it's clear that the hand isn't meant to be the one Luke lost on Bespin, which should have decayed and/or burned up looong before reaching another planet's atmosphere. It's likely his metal hand, which he lost in some recent adventure, and which could plausibly withstand the rigors of outer space and reentry and landing (they must build those things well!). <br /> <br /> I like the notion of the focus being put on new characters and their quest, with the classic characters helping them along. I don't like the notion that Luke's been missing for so long, and that maybe the Star Warriors haven't seen each other since RotJ! And yet another SuperWeapon? That can blow up a solar system? What's the friggin point of that?! How is that functionally any scarier than blowing up someone's planet? Even DBZ didn't go over that threshold, because it's pretty much pointless!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T22:31:57-07:00","id":203524,"title":"","content":"Hello Sun Crusher.<br /> <br /> EDIT: But in all seriousness, I hope this opening is bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-21-2014, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T00:36:17-07:00","id":203594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=203421#post203421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And yet another SuperWeapon? That can blow up a solar system? What's the friggin point of that?! How is that functionally any scarier than blowing up someone's planet? Even DBZ didn't go over that threshold, because it's pretty much pointless!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Trying to one-up the Death Star with increasingly ridiculous super weapons was one of the worst things in the expanded universe, so I hope they don't go that route. By the way, the villain in the recent (and awful) DBZ movie Battle of the Gods could destroy galaxies instead of planets =/<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T01:57:12-07:00","id":203642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=203421#post203421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had the same initial ideas that vidblogger did...but on reflection, it's clear that the hand isn't meant to be the one Luke lost on Bespin, which should have decayed and/or burned up looong before reaching another planet's atmosphere. It's likely his metal hand, which he lost in some recent adventure, and which could plausibly withstand the rigors of outer space and reentry and landing (they must build those things well!). <br /> <br /> I like the notion of the focus being put on new characters and their quest, with the classic characters helping them along. I don't like the notion that Luke's been missing for so long, and that maybe the Star Warriors haven't seen each other since RotJ! And yet another SuperWeapon? That can blow up a solar system? What's the friggin point of that?! How is that functionally any scarier than blowing up someone's planet? Even DBZ didn't go over that threshold, because it's pretty much pointless!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well it wouldn't decay in the vacuum of space, since there's no microorganisms to break it down. But I agree, if this rumor is true (and I kind of hope it's not), it would make far more sense to be his robotic hand, or even someone else's hand if they try to go for a not-so-surprising twist. Anyway, SOMEONE's hand holding his green saber. I mean, finding the hand he lost on Bespin would be a curiosity, not a call to adventure. Finding his hand holding the saber he was using the last time they saw him is a reason to go looking for him, because it means he must have lost it recently and nearby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T02:54:21-07:00","id":203677,"title":"","content":"Well, there are some microorganisms inside our bodies, but most are on the surface - and between the vacuum and the cold (the space background temperature is 3 Celsius degrees away from absolute zero) this shouldn't be an issue.<br /> <br /> Then again, even if the hand disintegrated in the atmosphere, as long as the lightsaber is intact it can sort of work as a hook. You don't see lightsabers every day, and adventurous souls who know of the jedi and have a reasonably good opinion of them can certainly consider giving it back. It doesn't have to be only from the goodness of their heart, though - they may expect they are getting some reward. After all, a lightsaber is a priceless relic and the jedi used to be known for their fair dealings. They may not be rich, but I imagine that after the fall of the Empire Luke and whoever he recruited would have a fair amount of influence and important friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 07-21-2014, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T08:33:04-07:00","id":203875,"title":"","content":"It reads like misinformation plant. That is too stupid to be real. Either released purposely to cause confusion or in place to track down if someone was trying to get the script. Have an idea of who or how based off what is leaked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"