er":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T06:35:05-07:00","id":210091,"title":"","content":"...Dammit, did I break *another* Star Wars thread? Again?!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Well, with any luck, you all are reviewing the Prequels, hopefully with newly open minds unclogged by the bias of years of accumulated Hatedom to see that, while clearly flawed and far from perfect, they really are not the total abortions we've been told by rants that they are over and over again...<br /> <br /> Incidentally, read the comments for the NC's video. There are many posters there who grew up with the Prequels as THEIR childhood SW movies! Now, they grew up liking them a lot, until they got older and started to see the flaws in them (helped, no doubt, by their older peers who wouldn't stop raving about how much they sucked), but many of them outright state that <i>the Originals weren't much better!</i> Blasphemy, I know, and yet that's an honest opinion unbiased by childhood nostalgia, which even the most clear minded of us have to admit is a part of our vision, however small.<br /> <br /> Of course, for a truly unbiased POV, we'll have to wait a generation or two for people who grew up with ALL the films, not just one series or the other, so that they don't have favorites at all. But then, THEY will be growing up with the newer Disney films, which I'm sure Disney will be making for the foreseeable future, so maybe that won't be possible after all...[shrug]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactio