eet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T12:55:43-07:00","id":240528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=238420#post238420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might work.... Just have to see where they go with it. There is an Inquisitor in the new animated series, so we'll see if that ties in some how.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really like the animation any more than Clone Wars, but I have to admit I'm actually interested in this one where I never was in Clone Wars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T04:24:33-07:00","id":241217,"title":"","content":"The Clone Wars animation grew on me after awhile. I didn't care for it at first. We'll see about this new one...<br /> <br /> My only issue I guess is the Inquisitor on the show. I saw a video where they go out of their way to say he's not a Sith, but then he looks like one, acts like one, has a red lightsaber and uses the Force. Sounds like a Sith to me. :P I know, theres a difference between being trained BY and a Sith and a trained AS a Sith....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T06:26:03-07:00","id":241289,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a Revanite...<br /> <br /> Hmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T07:11:48-07:00","id":241307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=241217#post241217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Clone Wars animation grew on me after awhile. I didn't care for it at first. We'll see about this new one...<br /> <br /> My only issue I guess is the Inquisitor on the show. I saw a video where they go out of their way to say he's not a Sith, but then he looks like one, acts like one, has a red lightsaber and uses the Force. Sounds like a Sith to me. :P I know, theres a difference between being trained BY and a Sith and a trained AS a Sith....</div> </div> </div> </div>They came up with a reason for the red a long time ago. The most abundant on the Sith home world (Korriban) was read. Later the formula(for lack of the proper word) for the synthetic crystals they make always turns out red. That might all be EU though so that may or may not exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T15:52:21-07:00","id":245674,"title":"","content":"Yea, that might be something they decide to change...who knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T13:06:51-08:00","id":306868,"title":"","content":"So, Star Wars: Rebels! What do we think of it?<br /> <br /> So far, I like it ok, but I'm not really &quot;wowed&quot; by it. I like the crew, what I've seen of their personalities so far, the squabbling...if anything, it feels like old-time Marvel Comics as much as Firefly! The two recurring villains are nice and menacing, but I hope there's something more to them than just &quot;Evil!&quot; Clone Wars did pretty good with that, hopefully this show will as well. <br /> <br /> I was often shocked by how violent CW could get...It looks like Rebels is continuing that tradition, even moreso considering that the &quot;faceless mooks&quot; are no longer battle droids, but living Stormtroopers, which the heroes don't hesitate to blow away in a variety of (sometimes darkly comic) ways! <br /> <br /> One thing I'm of two minds about is the music. It's clear that they want to evoke the original movies in every way possible, and one of the best ways is in digging through their OSTs (including at least one track from Indiana Jones, for some reason!). But I know that music so well, that even when they use minor cues, it throws me out of the episode because I'm remembering &quot;Oh, that's the music playing when Old Ben first hears that R2 was looking for Obi-Wan!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Maybe I'll get used to it in time, but it's pretty distracting, right now...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T06:02:22-08:00","id":307354,"title":"","content":"I haven't watched it yet. Think I'll wait till the season is done and maybe check it out then.<br /> <br /> Interesting about the music...surprised to hear they borrowed from Indiana Jones. Seems odd...but hey, if it works I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T06:13:18-08:00","id":307357,"title":"","content":"The movie is out or there is only a trailer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T07:03:31-08:00","id":307381,"title":"","content":"Cartoon Network has this &quot;Star Wars; Rebels&quot; thing. It's a cartoon show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T07:13:09-08:00","id":307387,"title":"","content":"I don't watch Cartoon Network.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T08:36:24-08:00","id":307451,"title":"","content":"The protagonist seems like an Aladdin expy, not only for his appearance but also personality and background. It's like the Genie messed up one of his wishes and left him retroactively in the Star Wars universe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T00:57:25-08:00","id":307973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=306868#post306868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Star Wars: Rebels! What do we think of it?<br /> <br /> So far, I like it ok, but I'm not really &quot;wowed&quot; by it. I like the crew, what I've seen of their personalities so far, the squabbling...if anything, it feels like old-time Marvel Comics as much as Firefly! The two recurring villains are nice and menacing, but I hope there's something more to them than just &quot;Evil!&quot; Clone Wars did pretty good with that, hopefully this show will as well.<br /> <br /> I was often shocked by how violent CW could get...It looks like Rebels is continuing that tradition, even moreso considering that the &quot;faceless mooks&quot; are no longer battle droids, but living Stormtroopers, which the heroes don't hesitate to blow away in a variety of (sometimes darkly comic) ways!<br /> <br /> One thing I'm of two minds about is the music. It's clear that they want to evoke the original movies in every way possible, and one of the best ways is in digging through their OSTs (including at least one track from Indiana Jones, for some reason!). But I know that music so well, that even when they use minor cues, it throws me out of the episode because I'm remembering &quot;Oh, that's the music playing when Old Ben first hears that R2 was looking for Obi-Wan!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Maybe I'll get used to it in time, but it's pretty distracting, right now...<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I already watched 5 episodes of this new &quot;SW - Rebels&quot;. Well, what to say? I don't like this new &quot;Rebels&quot; cartoon. At all.<br /> <br /> The show is super dumb. In ep.5 we have a &quot;basic training&quot; for the Stormtrooper cadets (totally not the &quot;Ender's Game&quot; rip off, nope!) that is tough even for the main character, Ezra (again - totally not Alladin's rip off!), and he is a Jedi in training. In theory, at the end of this training green teenagers will become tough as nails, capable of killing and maiming Rebel scum in droves.<br /> <br /> Instead, as this show keeps telling us, your ordinary Stromtrooper is easily defeated by a <i>fruit</i>. After the graduating from this super-duper academy they totally forget how to shoot straight, take cover from fire and that it is no use to just look at therma-detonator slowly rolling to your feet.<br /> <br /> Said protagonists are just a super team of damned John Rambos. Really! Their kill ratio is already greater then that of rebel pilots during the &quot;New Hope's&quot; attack on the Death Star. Needless to say, I have no simpathy for them.<br /> <br /> I had to wonder - how Empire with so ridiculously incompetent mooks have managed to survive for so long if a rag-tag bunch of misfits(tm) can easily foil its plans and inflict colossal damage in the process? There are a lot of shows (and, you know - books) about &quot;Resistance&quot; or guerilla movements on the occupied territories and about dangers and challenges that they had to face daily in order to survive and carry on with their work. &quot;Rebels&quot; play this for giggles which totally kill the atmosphere.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T10:18:47-08:00","id":308324,"title":"","content":"And all of that is different from the original movies' portrayal of Stormtroopers...how? <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ImperialStormtrooperMarksmanshipAcademy\" target=\"_blank\">Imperial Stormtrooper Marksmanship Academy</a> is an established trope for a reason...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T10:59:02-08:00","id":308371,"title":"","content":"I think SW:R isn't bad. I like the animation better than Clone Wars, but not that much. I think they have something here to work with, but I'm not sure it will ever get any where. I think the main character should have been a few years older(16 maybe) since they seem to want to make him older.<br /> <br /> I do like they are continuing reversing Lucas's attempt to make all Stormtroopers in this era clones(how Luke could still try to pass himself off as a short Stormtrooper if that were the case is beyond me). Though it begs the question what happened to the clones or are they going with their own multi-canon universe(which I thought they said they were not doing).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=307973#post307973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I already watched 5 episodes of this new &quot;SW - Rebels&quot;. Well, what to say? I don't like this new &quot;Rebels&quot; cartoon. At all.<br /> <br /> The show is super dumb. In ep.5 we have a &quot;basic training&quot; for the Stormtrooper cadets (totally not the &quot;Ender's Game&quot; rip off, nope!) that is tough even for the main character, Ezra (again - totally not Alladin's rip off!), and he is a Jedi in training. In theory, at the end of this training green teenagers will become tough as nails, capable of killing and maiming Rebel scum in droves.<br /> <br /> Instead, as this show keeps telling us, your ordinary Stromtrooper is easily defeated by a <i>fruit</i>. After the graduating from this super-duper academy they totally forget how to shoot straight, take cover from fire and that it is no use to just look at therma-detonator slowly rolling to your feet.<br /> <br /> Said protagonists are just a super team of damned John Rambos. Really! Their kill ratio is already greater then that of rebel pilots during the &quot;New Hope's&quot; attack on the Death Star. Needless to say, I have no simpathy for them.<br /> <br /> I had to wonder - how Empire with so ridiculously incompetent mooks have managed to survive for so long if a rag-tag bunch of misfits(tm) can easily foil its plans and inflict colossal damage in the process? There are a lot of shows (and, you know - books) about &quot;Resistance&quot; or guerilla movements on the occupied territories and about dangers and challenges that they had to face daily in order to survive and carry on with their work. &quot;Rebels&quot; play this for giggles which totally kill the atmosphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually how it always has been. Luke, an untrained farm boy that shot only basically a hunting rifle occasionally, was out shooting the elite Stormtroopers. And before the whole clone thing the Academy took in young people and trained them for several years though they didn't train specifically as Stormtroopers till older that I remember.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you should like it and I can agree in part with why you don't. Just that it is a nice throw back to how Star Wars was before. I do think they could have done a much better job with the story. I get the feeling that they want appeal to all ages and they are just doing that poorly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T16:47:57-08:00","id":324858,"title":"","content":"So. There's a new trailer for Force Awakens:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OMOVFvcNfvE\" data-code=\"OMOVFvcNfvE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/OMOVFvcNfvE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Alright, we know that:<br /> <br /> 1. The special effects are going to be <i>great</i>.<br /> <br /> 2. They're taking a chance and experimenting a bit with the designs (check out the droid in the trailer - I like it)<br /> <br /> 3. Cast diversity! (The first dude we see is a black man, and the next person is a young woman)<br /> <br /> 4. Canon awareness (Take a look at the Millennium Falcon - notice anything different that might of been because of Return of the Jedi? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Possibility: restoring the Force to its previous mystique? (The voiceover dude talks about the Force in a manner that suggests magic to me)<br /> <br /> Current Mood: Cautious Optimism!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T01:00:23-08:00","id":325858,"title":"","content":"I am cautiously optimistic as well. I wish I could be as super enthusiastic about it as some people are, though. Not because of everything in the teaser, which looks great, it's just that sometimes I wonder if the original trilogy wasn't a fluke...<br /> <br /> I really want to see this one recapture the look and feel of the original trilogy. I still remember seeing amidala's ship at the beginning of Phantom Menace and thinking &quot;that ship doesn't belong in star wars...&quot; it was all chrome and reminded me of the ship from Flight of the Navigator. I half expected Pee Wee Herman to start taking people's commands.<br /> <br /> The ships and vehicles in Star Wars were always so angular... even the Falcon, with it's vaguely circular shape still has this cluttered, unelegant, and highly detailed design. We have seen TIE fighters and the Falcon and the X-wings (all yay!) but no new vehicle designs yet. I hope to see something like the AT-ATs or the AT-STs. Those things are awesome.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T07:28:20-08:00","id":326003,"title":"","content":"Yea, I'm pretty excited about it. I love the look of that new lightsaber, the way the blade crackles is awesome, and makes it seem different from the traditional blade. And that shot of the X-Wings skimming the water was so bad ass!<br /> <br /> So, I'm getting excited about it...don't want to get my hopes up too high, but still, so far it looks awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T07:02:51-08:00","id":326923,"title":"","content":"Having the Baby Bears around, we're getting to watch the older Disney movies again. As much as the loved the latest one (<b>Frozen</b>), they were totally enraptured by <b>Beauty and the Beast</b> and wanted to watch it again immediately.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, the folks at Disney know how to tell <i>good stories</i>, which was always the more important part to me in <b>Star Wars</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T10:18:10-08:00","id":327156,"title":"","content":"The lightsaber's crossguard just looks ridiculous to me. With a weapon already liable to cut your hand off, let's make it twice as likely to do just that! It'll be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T11:18:20-08:00","id":327215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=327156#post327156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lightsaber's crossguard just looks ridiculous to me. With a weapon already liable to cut your hand off, let's make it twice as likely to do just that! It'll be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see the utility if it was something intended to actually catch other lightsaber blades but... it's a metal tube sticking out of a lightsaber all nice and vulnerable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T11:32:00-08:00","id":327219,"title":"","content":"Well, if we're going to get into what's going to cut off a hand by mistake, then we have to get into the whole thing about a heat source strong enough to melt metal not giving the Jedi 3rd degree burns on their hands every time they turn the thing on.<br /> <br /> Despite all the attempts to explain it, when all is said and done, the Jedi fill the &quot;holy warrior/wizard&quot; slot in the story. So, a wizard did it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T11:51:14-08:00","id":327267,"title":"","content":"What Papa Bear said-It's a fantasy setting wearing a rusted, scrapped-together science-fiction dress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T12:33:13-08:00","id":327310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=327267#post327267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Papa Bear said-It's a fantasy setting wearing a rusted, scrapped-together science-fiction dress.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's that whole internally consistent rules thing. Saying it's magic it is fine. Saying it's even more magical magic that completely undoes the existing magic is annoying.<br /> <br /> Previously it's shown &quot;lightsaber blade shoved into lightsaber handle = destroyed electronics, likely destroyed target lightsaber&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T12:45:27-08:00","id":327318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=327310#post327310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's that whole internally consistent rules thing. Saying it's magic it is fine. Saying it's even more magical magic that completely undoes the existing magic is annoying.<br /> <br /> Previously it's shown &quot;lightsaber blade shoved into lightsaber handle = destroyed electronics, likely destroyed target lightsaber&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If it's just another blade stuck thru the handle, sure. Looked like an intentional crossguard to me, but I'll admit, I've seen the trailer once on the evening news.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T13:24:34-08:00","id":327353,"title":"","content":"Well, my interpretation of the crossguard is that the crossguard utilizes some kind of &quot;overflow&quot; energy from the blade channeled into it... it's not like there are two tiny lightsabers attached to hilt... and if another lightsaber were to strike at that seemingly vulnerable point, instead of chopping it off rather uselessly, within that tube is a lightsaber blade that would deflect the blow.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I am conveying the idea correctly, and I could be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T13:38:01-08:00","id":327357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=327318#post327318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's just another blade stuck thru the handle, sure. Looked like an intentional crossguard to me, but I'll admit, I've seen the trailer once on the evening news.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the clip I posted, just a few posts up.<br /> <br /> Yeah, crossguard. Definitely. I take it the way one is supposed to take the double-lightsaber from Phantom Menace:<br /> <br /> &quot;Any guy who can use this weapon the way it is obviously intended to be used is a major badass and should be taken <i>very</i> seriously.&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: To Froggy: The lightsaber could have three emitters instead of just one; no rule against that. Also the emitters themselves could be made of Cortosis alloy, an uncommon-to-rare material that can stand up to a lightsaber, which was used by non-jedi expecting to go up against a saber-slinger.<br /> <br /> The crackling look of the blade looks to be the result of a novice attempting to construct a lightsaber and failing to synthesize a red crystal properly, creating instability in the blade. Although the &quot;overflow management&quot; theory might be correct, considering the saber may have been manufactured incorrectly using second-hand instructions and jury-rigged parts and oh lord I am nerding out so hard right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 12-01-2014, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T04:36:26-08:00","id":328048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=327353#post327353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, my interpretation of the crossguard is that the crossguard utilizes some kind of &quot;overflow&quot; energy from the blade channeled into it... it's not like there are two tiny lightsabers attached to hilt... and if another lightsaber were to strike at that seemingly vulnerable point, instead of chopping it off rather uselessly, within that tube is a lightsaber blade that would deflect the blow.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I am conveying the idea correctly, and I could be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heard a comment somewhere saying because the Sith use synthetic crystals, their blades have some instabilities, and those could be vents to help stabilize it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we'll have to see in it action I guess...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T11:40:31-08:00","id":328480,"title":"","content":"I'm caustiously pessimistic. After some of the things I've heard about the direction and pretty much totally throw out EU(Thrawn trilogy one of the most acclaimed book series ever for the SWU) just has me kind of down about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=325858#post325858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am cautiously optimistic as well. I wish I could be as super enthusiastic about it as some people are, though. Not because of everything in the teaser, which looks great, it's just that sometimes I wonder if the original trilogy wasn't a fluke...<br /> <br /> I really want to see this one recapture the look and feel of the original trilogy. I still remember seeing amidala's ship at the beginning of Phantom Menace and thinking &quot;that ship doesn't belong in star wars...&quot; it was all chrome and reminded me of the ship from Flight of the Navigator. I half expected Pee Wee Herman to start taking people's commands.<br /> <br /> The ships and vehicles in Star Wars were always so angular... even the Falcon, with it's vaguely circular shape still has this cluttered, unelegant, and highly detailed design. We have seen TIE fighters and the Falcon and the X-wings (all yay!) but no new vehicle designs yet. I hope to see something like the AT-ATs or the AT-STs. Those things are awesome.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I felt that way when I saw the new Stormtrooper armor. Part of the SW Universe is the fact that it doesn't all conform to demands of science. Its more science fantasy then science fiction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=326003#post326003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I'm pretty excited about it. I love the look of that new lightsaber, the way the blade crackles is awesome, and makes it seem different from the traditional blade. And that shot of the X-Wings skimming the water was so bad ass!</div> </div> </div> </div>I was a little off put by the guard on the lightsaber, but yeah that scene with the X-Wings looked awesome.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=327310#post327310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's that whole internally consistent rules thing. Saying it's magic it is fine. Saying it's even more magical magic that completely undoes the existing magic is annoying.<br /> <br /> Previously it's shown &quot;lightsaber blade shoved into lightsaber handle = destroyed electronics, likely destroyed target lightsaber&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually hate when they do that(allude to it as magic). That is when people start teleporting all over the place which wasn't the original intent(when Lucas had sane people keeping him in check). I like when it is played as mysticism more than magic. Fine line but definitely different limitations/expectations. Hopefully it is only because the new Sith is from a backwater like Dathomir or a place like that. Where they pretty much follow the same rules, but think/thought of it more as magic. Totally agree about the guard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":787,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","user":"Sorwen","date":". 12-02-2014, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T13:33:35-08:00","id":328575,"title":"","content":"you know I was thinking about it. A lightsaber with a crossguard is a cool thing. The problem is the exposed area RIGHT where any incoming blade would intercept it. An arrangement something like <a href=\"http://picascii.com/upload/FAVIQe.png\" target=\"_blank\">this(if it works)</a> would cover all the bases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T15:28:13-08:00","id":328689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=328575#post328575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you know I was thinking about it. A lightsaber with a crossguard is a cool thing. The problem is the exposed area RIGHT where any incoming blade would intercept it. An arrangement something like <a href=\"http://picascii.com/upload/FAVIQe.png\" target=\"_blank\">this(if it works)</a> would cover all the bases.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I went back and looked at it, I see what you're saying. The blade emitters come out far enough that they could be potentially useless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T16:42:39-08:00","id":328767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=328575#post328575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you know I was thinking about it. A lightsaber with a crossguard is a cool thing. The problem is the exposed area RIGHT where any incoming blade would intercept it. An arrangement something like <a href=\"http://picascii.com/upload/FAVIQe.png\" target=\"_blank\">this(if it works)</a> would cover all the bases.</div> </div> </div> </div>The link is broken for me, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Again, Cortosis might be a thing in this setting. Or the saber-slinger is good enough to always catch the enemy's blade on the crossguard.<br /> <br /> Or, that could very be the way to defeat the dark-sider in-movie, so...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T16:58:33-08:00","id":328777,"title":"","content":"Check this out: <a href=\"http://www.theverge.com/tldr/2014/11/28/7303233/please-hire-me-jj\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.theverge.com/tldr/2014/11...ase-hire-me-jj</a><br /> <br /> Thats an interesting redesign for that crossguard.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Colbert also weighs in: <a href=\"http://io9.com/stephen-colberts-defense-of-the-new-lightsaber-is-delig-1665665109\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/stephen-colberts-defe...lig-1665665109</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T21:48:20-08:00","id":329870,"title":"","content":"Tangent thought: So, the Star Wars RPGs put out by Fantasy Flight are pretty nice. They have their faults, but they're beautifully illustrated and have some interesting ideas.<br /> <br /> With this new trailer out and me on a Star Wars binge, I thought about what they could do after they've published the third game in their Star Wars line, Force and Destiny. For those who don't know, FF are publishing three games in the Star Wars universe in a manner similar to the World of Darkness method, being that they are based on a common ruleset and overarching setting (with crossover compatibility built in), with setting details and mechanics unique to each line.<br /> <br /> Two lines have come out so far: Edge of the Empire, focusing on Smugglers, Bounty Hunters, and other such vagabonds in the shadows of the galaxy; and Age of Rebellion, featuring those brave souls in the Rebel Alliance battling against tyranny and oppression. The third currently in Beta is Force and Destiny, following the Jedi who survived the purge and struggle to protect a galaxy that is trying to forget or destroy them.<br /> <br /> I was considering what game lines they could do after covering the rogues, rebels, and ronin of the galaxy, and I came up with five answers:<br /> <br /> 1. A villains book: let players see things from the Empire's perspective, perhaps as ace pilots, spies, officers, or perhaps even the oh-so-rare competent Storm Trooper. Show the fans why someone on the inside would choose to fight for a power that seems so monstrously and transparently evil from the outside.<br /> <br /> 2. The Clone wars: turn the clock back to the prequels, sending the PCs into battle alongside clones fighting against droids. Explore the politics behind the corrupt and crumbling Republic and the self-serving Separatist factions, and show the Jedi when they were still recognized as the guardians of peace and justice in the galaxy.<br /> <br /> 3. Go further back to the Old Republic: the Expanded Universe has been declared non-canon, so look on this as an opportunity to do what you want with the franchise. Case in point: The Old Republic era featured in the excellent Bioware games was formed by the company choosing to look way back into the setting's history so they could have plenty of room to do their thing. So give the setting that's brought about two successful RPGs and a MMORPG another look; it deserves it.<br /> <br /> 4. Go into the future after the war: the opposite of using the Old Republic, look at the after war period and use the trilogy everybody likes as the foundation for your own contributions. There is a TON of well-received after war fiction, like the Thrawn Trilogy or the Legacy comics that you can use as fodder for the line.<br /> <br /> 5. Tie-in with the new series: This one's pretty obvious, but if people like the new movies, than follow the Star Wars tradition and cash in on that lovely merchandising.<br /> <br /> And come on; you know you want to see the stats for that Sith light-broadsaber.<br /> <br /> So yeah, there's my two cents. Heck, it's Star Wars, they'll make money with whatever they do as long as they put effort into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T23:12:53-08:00","id":329904,"title":"","content":"You know, I think for most citizens, the Empire isn't terribly transparently evil. Remember, many of the truths you cling to depend greatly on your point of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T08:55:44-08:00","id":330194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=329904#post329904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I think for most citizens, the Empire isn't terribly transparently evil. Remember, many of the truths you cling to depend greatly on your point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I mean even with the Force that is a whole lot of evil people to find to run something as vast as the Imperial military. Most were average people that thought they were joining for good reasons. For many citizens they wouldn't see the effects. If you were on the fringes with 3rd rate Moffs that were kicked to the curb of fringe planets so all they had was being a petty Warlords or had a higher non-human population most citizens wouldn't know a thing. Imperial propaganda was how noble and good their actions were. The betterment of the galaxy.<br /> <br /> The Rebel Alliance was built on those people that actually felt that betterment of the galaxy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":787,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","user":"Sorwen","date":". 12-04-2014, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T10:39:03-08:00","id":330313,"title":"","content":"&quot;You think the average <a href=\"http://youtu.be/dGOVbXF7Iog\" target=\"_blank\">stormtrooper</a> knows how to install a toilet main? All they know is killing and white uniforms.&quot; -Randal<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T11:29:31-08:00","id":330361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=329904#post329904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I think for most citizens, the Empire isn't terribly transparently evil. Remember, many of the truths you cling to depend greatly on your point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my point; the book would show the average human Imperial's point of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T13:22:07-08:00","id":330497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=329904#post329904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I think for most citizens, the Empire isn't terribly transparently evil. Remember, many of the truths you cling to depend greatly on your point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing it is to the common person is corrupt and that it has all the power concentrated at the top, which means the ones with the most power are badly out of touch with the needs/wants of the locals or various beings.<br /> <br /> Why did the separatists movement gain such support? Because the republic was horribly corrupt with an elite government with all the power where they were badly out of touch with the needs/wants of the locals.<br /> <br /> Now the pro-human bias that became stronger, and the decrease of non-human rights (walking carpets becoming slaves and the like) increased under the Empire, so there's a reason you can point to for hate.<br /> <br /> Was the empire good for anything?<br /> <br /> Well, they were murder on pirates and any criminals that didn't pay the bribes. The more centrally planned economy meant stability and predictability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T09:22:45-08:00","id":362535,"title":"","content":"I was just thinking about bounty hunters in the Star Wars universe. Because our heroes were technically outlaws, this made the bh the defacto &quot;bad guys&quot;, but that's just one way of looking at it. Fett, IG-88 and those other guys hunted down a LOT of scum that they were instrumental in keeping out of circulation, and it'd be cool to see some of that. Hopefully, the new movies are taking place in a time with a more positive rule of law (otherwise, what the hell were our heroes fighing for in the OT??), and we can see some examples of outright heroic bounty hunters and even a good lawman or three...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RV5WqRnFejI\" target=\"_blank\">In other news, there's this, Force forgive me...</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:30:17-08:00","id":367389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=362535#post362535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just thinking about bounty hunters in the Star Wars universe. Because our heroes were technically outlaws, this made the bh the defacto &quot;bad guys&quot;, but that's just one way of looking at it. Fett, IG-88 and those other guys hunted down a LOT of scum that they were instrumental in keeping out of circulation, and it'd be cool to see some of that. Hopefully, the new movies are taking place in a time with a more positive rule of law (otherwise, what the hell were our heroes fighing for in the OT??), and we can see some examples of outright heroic bounty hunters and even a good lawman or three...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RV5WqRnFejI\" target=\"_blank\">In other news, there's this, Force forgive me...</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Ummm....In many cases that wasn't just one way looking at it. IG-88 was a assassin droid. He rarely took anyone alive unless it was a high enough bounty to be worth it. He mostly took jobs that held the most destruction/carnage. Fett is hard to argue because they did the most changes between the old and the new. Neither instance was he a &quot;good&quot; or &quot;neutral&quot; guy in either case though. He quite freely killed whom ever got in his way. Bossk, who would be in those other guys, would make most other Trandoshan's look warm and fuzzy in comparison. Dengar? Greedo? Even in the newer films/shows most of the bounty hunters have been assassins or amoral at best.<br /> <br /> That isn't to say there couldn't be decent bounty hunters in Star Wars, just that most(not all) were written as scum hunting scum or even hunting decent people. The Empire used them often to hunt people they wanted shut up and they were having problems finding. However there is no reason they couldn't write a heroic bounty hunter though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T07:33:14-08:00","id":369733,"title":"","content":"I've been watching the animated <i>Clone Wars</i> series recently. I'm not sure how I feel about it. On the one hand, it's delightfully fun. On the other hand, it doesn't really jive with a lot of things that I believe about Star Wars. Case in point: in one episode the AT-TE walkers go straight up the side of a cliff. This is cool and all, but I highly doubt the AT-AT walkers from ESB could go straight up a vertical cliff. Indeed, it seems that the AT-AT walkers being somewhat ungainly is part of the plot in ESB. Yet ESB is in the future from CW point of view, and so the walkers should have improved. Maybe they sacrificed mobility for armor...? I don't know.<br /> <br /> And another thing I'm not sure about in the series is that they make a point of the fact that the clones are individuals. They have different personalities and they have different thoughts. They seem to have affection for the Jedi that they work with. And yet, in Episode III, they ruthlessly execute the Jedi when Order 66 is given. I don't remember a single one even hesitating. (Granted, I've only seen III once and that was opening day, so it's been awhile and I could very well be wrong.)<br /> <br /> On the positive side of things, I think the show, taken in and of itself, is great. I think the characters are strong, I think the storylines are meaningful, I think they have variety, while a lot of EU stuff focuses solely on Jedi. If it weren't for the conflicts that I feel exist between the movies and the show, I would have no complaints.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":1041,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","user":"brjedi26","date":". 01-14-2015, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T09:27:36-08:00","id":373541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=369733#post369733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And another thing I'm not sure about in the series is that they make a point of the fact that the clones are individuals. They have different personalities and they have different thoughts. They seem to have affection for the Jedi that they work with. And yet, in Episode III, they ruthlessly execute the Jedi when Order 66 is given. I don't remember a single one even hesitating. (Granted, I've only seen III once and that was opening day, so it's been awhile and I could very well be wrong.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't watched the very last season of Clone Wars, but I believe there is an episode that deals with Order 66. I'm not exactly sure how it deals with it, but I caught wind of an episode where a clone discovers something off in their head, maybe an implant or something?<br /> <br /> Anyway, if you're not done with the series yet, that concern may be addressed. Still...I know what you mean, as there is a bit of a disconnect between this series and the movies...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T20:11:33-08:00","id":378621,"title":"","content":"I looked at the titles and it appears you're right. I'm still in the first season, like 15 episodes in so... it'll be awhile till I get there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, 