ck Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T16:51:23-08:00","id":379631,"title":"","content":"Will do, sir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T08:41:08-08:00","id":397590,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I understand that I'm beating a dead bantha here, but, again - the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies/page18\">Rebels</a>&quot; series...<br /> <br /> You know, I've rewatched &quot;SW - New Hope&quot; recently. I've counted how many TIE fighters and Imperials are killed in it - on screen, &quot;in your face&quot; variety.<br /> <br /> 6 TIE fighters. 34 Imperials<br /> <br /> &quot;Rebels&quot; over-achieved both of these &quot;records&quot; by episode 4 (well, counting shorts). Right now it has an absolute record of (destroyed) - 37 TIE fighters, 74 stromtroopers, 6 AT-STs, 2 APCs and 3 transport ships with all hands on deck.<br /> <br /> It won't surprise me in the slightest if &quot;General-Admiral Alladin&quot; and his crew of misfits would outperform proper rebels from <b><i>all 3 movies</i></b> by 1st season's end.<br /> <br /> But, maybe, I just can't grok &quot;TV Series for Kids&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T07:49:21-08:00","id":398759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=397590#post397590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I understand that I'm beating a dead bantha here, but, again - the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies/page18\">Rebels</a>&quot; series...<br /> <br /> You know, I've rewatched &quot;SW - New Hope&quot; recently. I've counted how many TIE fighters and Imperials are killed in it - on screen, &quot;in your face&quot; variety.<br /> <br /> 6 TIE fighters. 34 Imperials<br /> <br /> &quot;Rebels&quot; over-achieved both of these &quot;records&quot; by episode 4 (well, counting shorts). Right now it has an absolute record of (destroyed) - 37 TIE fighters, 74 stromtroopers, 6 AT-STs, 2 APCs and 3 transport ships with all hands on deck.<br /> <br /> It won't surprise me in the slightest if &quot;General-Admiral Alladin&quot; and his crew of misfits would outperform proper rebels from <b><i>all 3 movies</i></b> by 1st season's end.<br /> <br /> But, maybe, I just can't grok &quot;TV Series for Kids&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to count again. Death Star blew up. The first film has to count as the most killed in a single shot in the history of movies. Betting the second wasn't fully staffed since it wasn't finished. That of course doesn't count the bad guys that often blow up planets.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T02:26:21-08:00","id":400127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=398759#post398759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might want to count again. Death Star blew up. The first film has to count as the most killed in a single shot in the history of movies. Betting the second wasn't fully staffed since it wasn't finished. That of course doesn't count the bad guys that often blow up planets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said - &quot;in your face&quot; variety of deaths. I.e. - the one we were shown in details. Like TIE fighter blowing up or Stormtrooper getting shot <i>on screen</i>.<br /> <br /> And, yeah - the &quot;Rebels&quot; already outperformed the Original Trilogy in that regards. Do you know how many TIE Fighters go &quot;boom&quot; in the &quot;Emprie Strikes Back&quot;?<br /> <br /> <b><i>Four</i></b>.<br /> <br /> In &quot;Rebels&quot; its called &quot;Tuesday&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","user":"von Lyttenburgh","date":". 02-10-2015, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T04:44:42-08:00","id":400175,"title":"","content":"I disagree that there is a difference. Why does a TIE exploding <i>on screen</i> counts, but the Death Star exploding <i>on the very same screen</i> does not? I see no difference in detail. It is not like the camera zoomed into the cockpits as they were shot down, showing the last few moments of each TIE pilot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:41:50-08:00","id":400804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=397590#post397590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I understand that I'm beating a dead bantha here, but, again - the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies/page18\">Rebels</a>&quot; series...<br /> <br /> You know, I've rewatched &quot;SW - New Hope&quot; recently. I've counted how many TIE fighters and Imperials are killed in it - on screen, &quot;in your face&quot; variety.<br /> <br /> 6 TIE fighters. 34 Imperials<br /> <br /> &quot;Rebels&quot; over-achieved both of these &quot;records&quot; by episode 4 (well, counting shorts). Right now it has an absolute record of (destroyed) - 37 TIE fighters, 74 stromtroopers, 6 AT-STs, 2 APCs and 3 transport ships with all hands on deck.<br /> <br /> It won't surprise me in the slightest if &quot;General-Admiral Alladin&quot; and his crew of misfits would outperform proper rebels from <b><i>all 3 movies</i></b> by 1st season's end.<br /> <br /> But, maybe, I just can't grok &quot;TV Series for Kids&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Never played any of the Star Wars games out there? RPG or Video Game or Tactical etc. I did that in one session and more...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:51:09-08:00","id":400817,"title":"","content":"I am an Old School Star Wars fan, when I was a kid I saw every original Theatrical Run of the Holy Trilogy. Tells you how old I am. <br /> <br /> I am going to give Force Awakens a fair shot as I did the Prequels, which was a mixed bag for me. I am not going to base my thoughts on rumors. A trailer. Etc. <br /> <br /> If I end up enjoying it great. If it sucks then it sucks like Attack of the Clones suckage. I am not going to let it cloud me my opinion and love of things in Star Wars that were never canon in the first place. (we can argue what is and should all day. Not interested in that tired argument).<br /> <br /> I happen to think the Prequels would have been better if more developed and a better director than George Lucas. I get what he was trying to do but only Revenge of the Sith really is even worth mentioning but that is my opinion. I know kids who like the Prequels a lot so bringing in new Star Wars fans is always good. <br /> <br /> JJ Abrams is either going to do a good job or a bad one. Star Wars is more up his alley than Star Trek was. <br /> <br /> If the film stinks I'll say it after I see it. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T10:28:30-08:00","id":402019,"title":"","content":"I think JJ Abrams was a good choice(a much better choice for SW then ST), but a good director can't fix a bad script(Superman Returns?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T13:17:49-07:00","id":482671,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ngElkyQ6Rhs\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ngElkyQ6Rhs</a> These aren't your daddy's stormtroopers! <img src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/CCu3zR2WEAAAwxU.png:large\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T17:02:16-07:00","id":482956,"title":"","content":"<b>The Hype is Real.</b><br /> <br /> Oh lord, please let it be good... it doesn't have to be great, just please let it be good. (Although, if you can swing for great...)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T11:41:31-07:00","id":483770,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a friend mentioned the new trailer so I looked it up last night. There was some nice imagry and there are going to be some intersting scenes at least. I loved the scene with the Star Destroyer crashed(on Tatooine again?) and still love the scene with the X-Wings flying on planet. The mechanical hand and the end was cool.<br /> <br /> At the same time it made me even more meh for the film. First it felt like a cross between A New Hope and The Old Republic. We basically had Satele Shan meet Jace Malcom and Darth Revan showing up with his classic mask. Either that was all one hell of a coinsidence or this is the most forced cross promotion I've ever seen.<br /> <br /> Edit: This is what I'm getting instead of Thrawn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T20:57:28-07:00","id":484222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=482956#post482956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Hype is Real.</b><br /> <br /> Oh lord, please let it be good... it doesn't have to be great, just please let it be good. (Although, if you can swing for great...)</div> </div> </div> </div>After that teaser I'm pretty excited now!!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=483770#post483770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I loved the scene with the Star Destroyer crashed(on Tatooine again?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Word is its a different desert planet ( <a href=\"http://io9.com/lets-break-down-the-secrets-and-spectacle-of-the-new-st-1698268479\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/lets-break-down-the-s...-st-1698268479</a> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all y