nt, and hopefully much better.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We'll see, though. </div> </div> </div>Sooon...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (hopefully I'll soon have Exalted 3rd edition to keep me busy till then)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T04:11:59-07:00","id":506597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=497439#post497439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't hit Mr.Gone's links, but I know it had more to do with budget than being a &quot;choice&quot;, as such -- even as popular as the SW franchise was then, Lucas didn't have the funds to do the Wookies as he envisioned so he &quot;settled&quot; for making the Ewoks.<br /> <br /> EDIT: hit the links -- brought back memories... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Had a feeling people might like that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yea, I know there were probably budget reasons for the ewoks...but still. I don't mind them as much as some people do, but Wookies would have kicked ass!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T05:14:21-07:00","id":508866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=503062#post503062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have every reason to believe this will be terrible. I still can't wipe the visions of episodes 1-3 from my brain.<br /> <br /> We'll see, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, in fairness, the 2nd one was actually not bad (I was pleasantly surprised), and for me it went a long way to making up for &quot;Phantom Menace&quot;. Even &quot;Sith&quot; had the Emperor vs. Yoda for fanbois to fap-- er, cheer about. (I agree, though, that they could have been scripted/directed *SO* much better than they were... but that doesn't mean that the next 3 movies can't make up for the second-group's dip. *Hopefully*...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T11:55:21-07:00","id":510996,"title":"","content":"So...this next movie will come out on Dec 18th. Will this break the weekend record that the Avengers (first movie) set at the $207 million mark? Been reading a lot predictions...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T12:25:46-07:00","id":511030,"title":"","content":"I think opening weekend will be huge, possibly bigger than <i>Avengers</i>. If any movie has a shot at doing it, <i>Episode VII</i> does. Long term box office gross will depend on the quality of the film, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T17:52:56-07:00","id":511359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=508866#post508866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, in fairness, the 2nd one was actually not bad (I was pleasantly surprised), and for me it went a long way to making up for &quot;Phantom Menace&quot;. Even &quot;Sith&quot; had the Emperor vs. Yoda for fanbois to fap-- er, cheer about. (I agree, though, that they could have been scripted/directed *SO* much better than they were... but that doesn't mean that the next 3 movies can't make up for the second-group's dip. *Hopefully*...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be alone, but I'm actually not a fan of Yoda fighting with a lightsaber...or really Yoda fighting in general...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=510996#post510996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...this next movie will come out on Dec 18th. Will this break the weekend record that the Avengers (first movie) set at the $207 million mark? Been reading a lot predictions...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yea, I have no doubt. Even if it sucks, the opening will be huge! Though, Episode 1 does leave a lot of people cautious about Star Wars...so who knows.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T19:08:36-07:00","id":511413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=511359#post511359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might be alone, but I'm actually not a fan of Yoda fighting with a lightsaber...or really Yoda fighting in general...</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not alone. I feel the same way. The line Dooku says in episode 2, &quot;It is obvious that this contest cannot be decided by our knowledge of the Force... but by our skills with a lightsaber.&quot; Makes me think, &quot;Seriously? Who wrote that?&quot; Even when it first came out when I was a young teenager, I still thought the line was terrible. That scene in general is terrible. Yoda flying in on the drop ship and subsequently commanding the clones: awesome. Yoda personally fighting... Stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T20:57:34-07:00","id":511573,"title":"","content":"The only way that Yoda being involved in a lightsaber duel makes sense to me is if he's standing there, calm and composed, as he uses the Force to cause his lightsaber to dance around on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T04:31:04-07:00","id":511887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=511413#post511413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not alone. I feel the same way. The line Dooku says in episode 2, &quot;It is obvious that this contest cannot be decided by our knowledge of the Force... but by our skills with a lightsaber.&quot; Makes me think, &quot;Seriously? Who wrote that?&quot; Even when it first came out when I was a young teenager, I still thought the line was terrible. That scene in general is terrible. Yoda flying in on the drop ship and subsequently commanding the clones: awesome. Yoda personally fighting... Stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm totally with you. And yea, that line is just terrible... As for who wrote it, sadly, it was George Lucas.<br /> <br /> Now, if there was a young yoda jumping around like that, I'd be fine with it I suppose...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=511573#post511573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way that Yoda being involved in a lightsaber duel makes sense to me is if he's standing there, calm and composed, as he uses the Force to cause his lightsaber to dance around on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could get behind that.<br /> <br /> You know, the only scene of Yoda with a saber I like in the movies is in Revenge of the Sith, when he throws it at that clone, and then runs up him to retrieve it. And even then that's pushing my limit of liking Yoda with a lightsaber...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T20:04:03-07:00","id":512494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=511413#post511413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not alone. I feel the same way. The line Dooku says in episode 2, &quot;It is obvious that this contest cannot be decided by our knowledge of the Force... but by our skills with a lightsaber.&quot; Makes me think, &quot;Seriously? Who wrote that?&quot; Even when it first came out when I was a young teenager, I still thought the line was terrible. That scene in general is terrible. Yoda flying in on the drop ship and subsequently commanding the clones: awesome. Yoda personally fighting... Stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, again, in fairness, when one actually looks back at all/any of the SW movies, they *aren't* exactly known for being well *written* movies/scripts -- they're well *directed* (usually), *plotted* and special effects for days... but most emphatically *not* well written. (For every decent line/&quot;go-to&quot; phrase, there's a dozen shitty/&quot;okaaaaayyyy&quot; ones that are just <i>there</i> and not that good -- especially in the second set of movies.)<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> While I personally am indifferent to Yoda w/a saber, I am a little surprised at the past several posts of people being quite against him wielding one -- he *is* a Jedi Master, and had been one for centuries... *of course* he's going to be quite skilled with them! They're the in-narrative hallmark of his order. It would be rather shocking if he <i>wasn't</i> a whirling machine with them. (As far as his physical prowess while utilizing a saber people have to remember that while not gone into too much in the movies, the Jedi/Sith often do channel the Force directly through their bodies so as to perform various superhuman physical feats -- particularly those involving speed or agility -- and that's what Yoda did: he was all old and crippled, like usual, until he charges with his Jedi Master Card and lays down the whoop-ass. Afterwards, he &quot;powers down&quot; and is all old and decrepit again. It's actually not that strange given the narratives involved... just saying....)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T21:18:57-07:00","id":514764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=512494#post512494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, again, in fairness, when one actually looks back at all/any of the SW movies, they *aren't* exactly known for being well *written* movies/scripts -- they're well *directed* (usually), *plotted* and special effects for days... but most emphatically *not* well written. (For every decent line/&quot;go-to&quot; phrase, there's a dozen shitty/&quot;okaaaaayyyy&quot; ones that are just <i>there</i> and not that good -- especially in the second set of movies.)</div> </div> </div> </div>True. There's an interview where Hamil, Ford and Fisher are all laughing about how hard it was to master the dialog from the original movie. Ford even famously told Lucas, &quot;George, you can write this shit, but we sure as hell can't say it!&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Dialog and directing actors' performances have always been Lucas' weak spots. If he'd had someone really good working with him on those, then the prequels could have been much better than they were...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *****<br /> <br /> While I personally am indifferent to Yoda w/a saber, I am a little surprised at the past several posts of people being quite against him wielding one -- he *is* a Jedi Master, and had been one for centuries... *of course* he's going to be quite skilled with them! They're the in-narrative hallmark of his order. It would be rather shocking if he <i>wasn't</i> a whirling machine with them. (As far as his physical prowess while utilizing a saber people have to remember that while not gone into too much in the movies, the Jedi/Sith often do channel the Force directly through their bodies so as to perform various superhuman physical feats -- particularly those involving speed or agility -- and that's what Yoda did: he was all old and crippled, like usual, until he charges with his Jedi Master Card and lays down the whoop-ass. Afterwards, he &quot;powers down&quot; and is all old and decrepit again. It's actually not that strange given the narratives involved... just saying....) </div> </div> </div>Basically, this. Notice how Yoda's demeanor changes when he calls his cane back to himself (altho one friend of mine thinks he's just faking the entire &quot;old and infirm&quot; bit!). Really, Yoda's &quot;acting&quot; throughout all the movies is a masterful testament to the art and craft of the puppeteers and animators. Watch all of his little gestures...there's one there that's a reference to &quot;Seven Samurai&quot;!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T09:21:11-07:00","id":515241,"title":"","content":"Given who now owns the respective properties, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u3tC8TPh9oQ#t=0m32s\" target=\"_blank\">there's an added layer of amusement to this...!</a><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T20:19:51-07:00","id":516675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=512494#post512494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I personally am indifferent to Yoda w/a saber, I am a little surprised at the past several posts of people being quite against him wielding one -- he *is* a Jedi Master, and had been one for centuries... *of course* he's going to be quite skilled with them! They're the in-narrative hallmark of his order. It would be rather shocking if he <i>wasn't</i> a whirling machine with them. (As far as his physical prowess while utilizing a saber people have to remember that while not gone into too much in the movies, the Jedi/Sith often do channel the Force directly through their bodies so as to perform various superhuman physical feats -- particularly those involving speed or agility -- and that's what Yoda did: he was all old and crippled, like usual, until he charges with his Jedi Master Card and lays down the whoop-ass. Afterwards, he &quot;powers down&quot; and is all old and decrepit again. It's actually not that strange given the narratives involved... just saying....)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't have an issue the idea that Yoda <i>can</i> use a lightsaber. As a young Jedi(in his prime) I bet he kicked ass with one(much like we see in the prequels I guess). But, he is like 900 years old. I'd like to think that later in his life as a Jedi Master he would have moved beyond the need to use one.<br /> <br /> Just my thoughts though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T23:54:19-07:00","id":516819,"title":"","content":"I do have some doubts about the old crew returning for Episode VII. Anyone remember kingdom of the Crystal Skull? It's just not the same when Harrison Ford can't do all the things that he was able to do in the earlier Indiana Jones movies. I don't mind if Han pilots the Falcon, or if Luke is the head of a new Jedi order or something, but I doubt if Mark Hamill can do all of the crazy combat stunts that people now expect from a lightsabre duel.<br /> <br /> I think a major challenge of the new movie is if they can allow Han, Leia and Luke to gracefully exit and allow the new characters to take the stage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T06:18:53-07:00","id":516980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=516675#post516675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't have an issue the idea that Yoda <i>can</i> use a lightsaber. As a young Jedi(in his prime) I bet he kicked ass with one(much like we see in the prequels I guess). But, he is like 900 years old. I'd like to think that later in his life as a Jedi Master he would have moved beyond the need to use one.<br /> <br /> Just my thoughts though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>He *had* moved beyond the need to use one, as indicated by his (apparent) day-to-day life per the prequel movies. However he'd still have one, and as the raw expressions of force-powers between him and Dookey didn't resolve the situation the latter challenged him to a light saber battle, which moved the nature of the challenge from brute force to finessed skill/adroitness. And given Yoda's strong connection to the Force and his mastery of it, he was able to compensate for his infirmities (as indicated in a number of books, and validated by being shown in the movie). Makes perfect sense when you really stop to think about it....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T06:27:38-07:00","id":516983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=516819#post516819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have some doubts about the old crew returning for Episode VII. Anyone remember kingdom of the Crystal Skull? It's just not the same when Harrison Ford can't do all the things that he was able to do in the earlier Indiana Jones movies. I don't mind if Han pilots the Falcon, or if Luke is the head of a new Jedi order or something, but I doubt if Mark Hamill can do all of the crazy combat stunts that people now expect from a lightsabre duel.<br /> <br /> I think a major challenge of the new movie is if they can allow Han, Leia and Luke to gracefully exit and allow the new characters to take the stage.</div> </div> </div> </div>The KotCS is a valid comparison relative to the execution of the narratives involved and the &quot;feeling and flavor&quot; aspects (that is, where KotCS felt a bit &quot;off&quot; for Indiana Jones, and not just because they set it forward in both date and concept to the alien-pulp era from the earlier mystical-pulp era, the SW movies can similarly feel &quot;off&quot; if not implemented properly both script and tone-wise). However, Mark's ability to do this, that or the other is irrelevant (given that stunt people were used for the crazy shit, anyway, back in the day) -- they only need a stuntman to do x,y and z and then CGI Mark's face onto it when it comes to any of the crazy shit (like they did with Dooky in the prequel movies, when Chris was certainly in no condition to be do most of what they had him do: his face was CGI'd for many of the fight scenes in those movies, over a stunt-doubles body). The much more important aspect is whether or not the old crew can &quot;bring it&quot; to the new sequel or not, relative to having the right tone and narrative -- and that has more to do with the writing and directing, ultimately, than with what the actors themselves bring, as they *should* feel older and not as energetically youthful as they were back in the day... which is likely the point, narratively, in the long run...<br /> <br /> Just saying...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T12:11:11-07:00","id":517229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=516980#post516980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He *had* moved beyond the need to use one, as indicated by his (apparent) day-to-day life per the prequel movies. However he'd still have one, and as the raw expressions of force-powers between him and Dookey didn't resolve the situation the latter challenged him to a light saber battle, which moved the nature of the challenge from brute force to finessed skill/adroitness. And given Yoda's strong connection to the Force and his mastery of it, he was able to compensate for his infirmities (as indicated in a number of books, and validated by being shown in the movie). Makes perfect sense when you really stop to think about it....</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it? Dooku threw some rocks at him, Yoda blocked it. Then he threw some lighting at him, and Yoda blocked that. Dooku then decided they were perfectly matched in Force and the only way to settle it was with a lightsaber fight? How does that add up?<br /> <br /> Theres no way Dooku was more powerful in the ways of the Force than Yoda. I mean, I get the Jedi don't use the Force to kill or anything, but I'm pretty sure Yoda could have done a bit more with with the Force than block a few things, right? How about use the Force to subdue him or hold him in place?<br /> <br /> I guess I don't know what I would have rather have seen mind you, but I feel like it could have been different.<br /> <br /> But hey, to each his own, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T12:13:50-07:00","id":517232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=516819#post516819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have some doubts about the old crew returning for Episode VII. Anyone remember kingdom of the Crystal Skull? It's just not the same when Harrison Ford can't do all the things that he was able to do in the earlier Indiana Jones movies. I don't mind if Han pilots the Falcon, or if Luke is the head of a new Jedi order or something, but I doubt if Mark Hamill can do all of the crazy combat stunts that people now expect from a lightsabre duel.<br /> <br /> I think a major challenge of the new movie is if they can allow Han, Leia and Luke to gracefully exit and allow the new characters to take the stage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope they do that as well. I mean, it will be cool to see Luke with a lightsaber, but I'd want it more on par with the duels in the OT, rather than what we saw in the prequels(as cool at that could be sometimes).<br /> <br /> But yea, I hope they use the old crew as the jumping off point for the new cast, rather than it be another story about Luke, Han and Leia...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T09:43:34-07:00","id":518230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=517232#post517232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope they do that as well. I mean, it will be cool to see Luke with a lightsaber, but I'd want it more on par with the duels in the OT, rather than what we saw in the prequels(as cool at that could be sometimes).</div> </div> </div> </div>?? I dunno, I think the PT duels were head and tails above the OT's. Round One of Luke vs. Vader was pretty good, tho. I expect in the NT, we'll see lots of CG Luke leaping about, and maybe even CG Han and Leia, if they're in any physical action scenes. Harrison Ford's accident on set not only set back filming, but probably killed any chance of his returning as Indiana Jones, which Disney was considering before, but now they want to recase. Incidentally, I wonder if they're going to do anything about Carrie Fisher's voice...?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yea, I hope they use the old crew as the jumping off point for the new cast, rather than it be another story about Luke, Han and Leia... </div> </div> </div>Apparently, that was the idea Lucas had that Disney didn't want to use, which implies that they may think that fans really want to see the old cast, since everyone's always on about how much better the OT was...Unfortunately, those rants may prevent us from seeing new characters really used to their fullest potential. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'd rather just have Luke there to pass on the torch, as Obi-Wan did for him, and the droids to tie the whole thing together, but that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T10:00:50-07:00","id":518261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=517229#post517229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does it? Dooku threw some rocks at him, Yoda blocked it. Then he threw some lighting at him, and Yoda blocked that. Dooku then decided they were perfectly matched in Force and the only way to settle it was with a lightsaber fight? How does that add up?<br /> <br /> Theres no way Dooku was more powerful in the ways of the Force than Yoda. I mean, I get the Jedi don't use the Force to kill or anything, but I'm pretty sure Yoda could have done a bit more with with the Force than block a few things, right? How about use the Force to subdue him or hold him in place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are a couple of lines that deal with this: Yoda notes during the Force contest that Dooku has become much stronger than he was before...tho admittedly not as much as Yoda, as he shows by blocking and dissipating Force Lightning, something no one else in the series has been able to do (I'msure they knew that Yoda vs the Emperor was gonna happen, so they had to leave some room for that). Why shouldn't he challenge his old master to a duel in a field that he was one of the top masters in, even before falling to the Dark Side? Why shouldn't the master not take him up on that, to show his old pupil how wrong his choice was and how far he's fallen? <br /> <br /> The other line is from Empire, where Yoda instructs Luke that a true Jedi uses the Force ONLY for knowledge and defense, NEVER for offense. Which, staying true to that, puts him in the rather reactive position we saw him in in AotC. <br /> <br /> As for using the Force to paralyze your opponent, the movies don't really elaborate on this, but the books explain that experienced Force users have sort of a reflexive &quot;force field&quot; about them to prevent this, which is why no one (not even the evil Sith!) does a Force Choke in the middle of combat...unless you can distract or shake your opponent psychologically somehow and you can slip it through their protection (that would probably only work on a Padawan, tho). <br /> <br /> What other options are there for Yoda, in that situation?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T19:33:18-07:00","id":518682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=517229#post517229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does it? Dooku threw some rocks at him, Yoda blocked it. Then he threw some lighting at him, and Yoda blocked that. Dooku then decided they were perfectly matched in Force and the only way to settle it was with a lightsaber fight? How does that add up?<br /> <br /> Theres no way Dooku was more powerful in the ways of the Force than Yoda. I mean, I get the Jedi don't use the Force to kill or anything, but I'm pretty sure Yoda could have done a bit more with with the Force than block a few things, right? How about use the Force to subdue him or hold him in place?<br /> <br /> I guess I don't know what I would have rather have seen mind you, but I feel like it could have been different.<br /> <br /> But hey, to each his own, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am... at a loss, and just a touch perplexed, by your view on this, Gone. Like, seriously.<br /> <br /> Hand of Omega provided excellent responses to your questions/counter-views. I'd only add that, as implied and indicated in the movies, a force-user has to either be *much* stronger than his opponent to use directed force-powers on him, or he has to catch him distracted/off-guard. Yoda is stronger than Dookey, no question, but he isn't *that* much stronger, and unlike when Dookey got the drop on Obi in the third movie, Dookey himself was on full-guard against Yoda.<br /> <br /> The fight between them made perfect sense. Like, seriously.<br /> <br /> Like, <i>seriously</i>.<br /> <br /> I don't know what else to say...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T19:57:27-07:00","id":518733,"title":"","content":"I'm still with Gone on this. I don't like the fight between Dooku and Yoda in ep. 2. I don't think it makes much sense. I don't think that Dooku is a close match for Yoda in the ways of the force. Yoda has been learning the ways of the force for ~800 years. Dooku has maybe 50-60 years? I've always figured Yoda was thr most powerful Jedi master by a fairly large margin. I think other masters had specific things in which they were better than Yoda (for example, I think Windu was a better swordsman than Yoda). But as far as understanding of the metaphysics of the force, I think Yoda was far and away more advanced than any other being in the galaxy. Yes, since the lightsaber was the signature weapon of the Jedi, he certainly would have had one and known how to use it. I even acknowledge that he could have opened himself to the force and done exactly what he did in ep. 2. I believe it was within his capabilities. I don't think he would have, though. I think that the fight in ep. 2 is, from a real world standpoint, a masturbation fest for fanboys. I believe in universe, Dooku was trying to bait Yoda into a dick waving contest and Yoda fell for it. But I don't think he would have. I think Yoda would recognize it and not fall for the ploy. And just look at my avatar. Would Ben Kenobi really lie?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T20:33:16-07:00","id":520386,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.maxgladstone.com/2013/10/star-wars-a-long-time-ago-in-a-hive-far-far-away/\" target=\"_blank\">Really don't buy into this, but it's interesting.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T13:10:40-07:00","id":523624,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I went in think the Yoda fight was going to be one of the worst parts, but I think it turned out well. I think if you take it from the point of &quot;A Jedi uses the Force for knowledge and defense, never for attack.&quot; then Yoda switching to a lightsaber works. Yes, he was vastly more knowledgeable than Dooku in the force, but that doesn't mean his options are not more limited because he doesn't use the Dark Side. If he starts throwing things at him or pushing him around rather than in counter response then that would be Dark Side. In that respect the best counter to a lightsaber would be a lightsaber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T20:10:38-07:00","id":523912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=518733#post518733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't think that Dooku is a close match for Yoda in the ways of the force. Yoda has been learning the ways of the force for ~800 years. Dooku has maybe 50-60 years? I've always figured Yoda was thr most powerful Jedi master by a fairly large margin. I think other masters had specific things in which they were better than Yoda (for example, I think Windu was a better swordsman than Yoda). But as far as understanding of the metaphysics of the force, I think Yoda was far and away more advanced than any other being in the galaxy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, perhaps, our video-game/TTRPG mentalities creep in to our narrative thought processes when it comes to looking at extra-narratives: Yoda's age, relative to the assessment at hand, is all-but-irrelevant (not *totally* irrelevant, but not far off). Age does not necessarily equate to power, nor dominating finesse. Plenty of highly skilled individuals in The Real World(tm) can find themselves upstaged by the talent of a novice. In the metaphysical context of The Force, Yoda may well have a greater degree of finesse and meta-&quot;muscle&quot; than Dooky, but it isn't by *that* much of a margin. A Jedi naturally attuned and/or strong with the force at a young age may well be nearly as strong as a veteran like Yoda -- he just may lack some of the more nuanced and/or finessed uses/expressions of power and understanding that the latter may have. Also, unlike in a video game, a proper narrative will show how age is as much a debilitating influence as it is one that provides the opportunity for skill and knowledge -- Yoda's the best, but that can still only be by a level of more narrow degrees rather than a video-game-esque &quot;I'm a 143rd level Jedi Ass-Master&quot;. Yoda proved to be Dooky's superior (which is why the latter had to create a distraction in order to escape); but none of that involved Dooky being *dominated*, by any degree. It's all in the margins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T20:33:59-07:00","id":523936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=520386#post520386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.maxgladstone.com/2013/10/star-wars-a-long-time-ago-in-a-hive-far-far-away/\" target=\"_blank\">Really don't buy into this, but it's interesting.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah -- I get where this guy is coming from but a great deal of what he is conjecturing is both in-narratively and meta-narratively flawed, to say the least. He's missing several key meta-narrative elements, not the least of which (relative to his addressing the male-female ratio) is his not taking into account that the movies -- being inspired by the sci-fi pulp era -- <i>were always going to be heavily male-biased</i>. The three women presented in the original films filled archetypes and little more, and while females were numerically better presented in the second set of movies it was still in a typical narratively supporting role/position (regardless of the social stature of the female in question). That's all *meta-narratively* driven, and nothing that in any way should be inferred by the viewer as having anything to do with the biological processes (or species-biases) of the &quot;humans&quot; in the films. (I'd cite plenty of other examples, but that's the one that stood out for me.) Again, I *get* where he's coming from, but it really is a situation of someone going a step too far to the left and reading too much into a narrative as presented....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T20:45:14-07:00","id":523940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=518733#post518733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still with Gone on this. I don't like the fight between Dooku and Yoda in ep. 2. I don't think it makes much sense. I don't think that Dooku is a close match for Yoda in the ways of the force. Yoda has been learning the ways of the force for ~800 years. Dooku has maybe 50-60 years? I've always figured Yoda was thr most powerful Jedi master by a fairly large margin. I think other masters had specific things in which they were better than Yoda (for example, I think Windu was a better swordsman than Yoda). But as far as understanding of the metaphysics of the force, I think Yoda was far and away more advanced than any other being in the galaxy. Yes, since the lightsaber was the signature weapon of the Jedi, he certainly would have had one and known how to use it. I even acknowledge that he could have opened himself to the force and done exactly what he did in ep. 2. I believe it was within his capabilities. I don't think he would have, though. I think that the fight in ep. 2 is, from a real world standpoint, a masturbation fest for fanboys. I believe in universe, Dooku was trying to bait Yoda into a dick waving contest and Yoda fell for it. But I don't think he would have. I think Yoda would recognize it and not fall for the ploy. And just look at my avatar. Would Ben Kenobi really lie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh! But speaking of Kenobi, the original SW &quot;old master&quot;, notice that he also was not &quot;above&quot; using his lightsaber in a pitched battle in ANH, a fight whose ending showed that he had far greater understanding and mastery of the Force than his former pupil; also, that he surely must have been using the Force to compensate for his advanced age, as well. <br /> <br /> As to the &quot;masturbation-fest&quot;--well, yeah, it's Star Wars, probably the least subtle story in movies! I sometimes think fans want it to be more profound than it really is, as if to justify our loyalty to it, but all of its makers have always been upfront that it's simply the ultimate popcorn movie, a fairy tale dressed up in skiffy trappings, a modernized movie serial...<br /> <br /> This is like arguing that, realistically, WE have fighter jets with weapons that let them attack and destroy each other well within visual range, and SW, which has tech way beyond ours, shouldn't show outer space dog fights the way it does. But *every* movie/show that features dogfights, whether in air or space, shows the fighters getting up close annd personal, because that's where the *drama* is! <br /> <br /> Sure, maybe Yoda should be able to hum, levitate, and crush Dooku without lifting a hand/claw...but that would be visually *boring*, which is a far worse cinematic sin that being &quot;inaccurate&quot; (tho it might work much better in a novel). SW is all about playing out the conflict of Good and Evil, in as cool and exciting a way as possible! And theey don't get much more so than clashing laser swords!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T06:57:15-07:00","id":524382,"title":"","content":"I'm afraid this is where the difference between directors show. In Empire Strikes Back, we see Darth Vader casually killing his admirals for failing him, and all at a distance between starships. I found that less boring and far more sinister and scary.<br /> Although I am reminded that in one of the games we see &quot;Starkiller&quot; fighting TIE fighters with nothing but the Force and his light-saber, and even bringing down a star-destroyer.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T16:47:08-07:00","id":524924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=524382#post524382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) we see Darth Vader casually killing his admirals for failing him, and all at a distance between starships. I found that less boring and far more sinister and scary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely! I remember to this day seeing TESB in the theater (1980, as a kid) and overhearing some guy talking to another guy going &quot;See 'dat shit? -- Vader a *pimp* -- He ma' *boy*&quot;. Hardly a truer sentiment has ever been spoken.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T19:20:56-07:00","id":524982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=518261#post518261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there are a couple of lines that deal with this: Yoda notes during the Force contest that Dooku has become much stronger than he was before...tho admittedly not as much as Yoda, as he shows by blocking and dissipating Force Lightning, something no one else in the series has been able to do (I'msure they knew that Yoda vs the Emperor was gonna happen, so they had to leave some room for that). Why shouldn't he challenge his old master to a duel in a field that he was one of the top masters in, even before falling to the Dark Side? Why shouldn't the master not take him up on that, to show his old pupil how wrong his choice was and how far he's fallen?<br /> <br /> The other line is from Empire, where Yoda instructs Luke that a true Jedi uses the Force ONLY for knowledge and defense, NEVER for offense. Which, staying true to that, puts him in the rather reactive position we saw him in in AotC.<br /> <br /> As for using the Force to paralyze your opponent, the movies don't really elaborate on this, but the books explain that experienced Force users have sort of a reflexive &quot;force field&quot; about them to prevent this, which is why no one (not even the evil Sith!) does a Force Choke in the middle of combat...unless you can distract or shake your opponent psychologically somehow and you can slip it through their protection (that would probably only work on a Padawan, tho).<br /> <br /> What other options are there for Yoda, in that situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are some good points.<br /> <br /> I guess in that situation he doesn't have much of a choice. So maybe my problem isn't so much how Yoda reacted in that situation, rather that he was in the situation to begin with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=518682#post518682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am... at a loss, and just a touch perplexed, by your view on this, Gone. Like, seriously.<br /> <br /> Hand of Omega provided excellent responses to your questions/counter-views. I'd only add that, as implied and indicated in the movies, a force-user has to either be *much* stronger than his opponent to use directed force-powers on him, or he has to catch him distracted/off-guard. Yoda is stronger than Dookey, no question, but he isn't *that* much stronger, and unlike when Dookey got the drop on Obi in the third movie, Dookey himself was on full-guard against Yoda.<br /> <br /> The fight between them made perfect sense. Like, seriously.<br /> <br /> Like, <i>seriously</i>.<br /> <br /> I don't know what else to say...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what to say either. I'm just not a fan of that scene, or Yoda's fight with the Emperor. I don't much care for the Emperor with a lightsaber either. I know, I'm crazy...<br /> <br /> I just feel like characters like that are beyond the need for weapons like that, plus, I don't much see them getting into situations where they'd have to physically battle.<br /> <br /> Again, that's just me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=518733#post518733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still with Gone on this. I don't like the fight between Dooku and Yoda in ep. 2. I don't think it makes much sense. I don't think that Dooku is a close match for Yoda in the ways of the force. Yoda has been learning the ways of the force for ~800 years. Dooku has maybe 50-60 years? I've always figured Yoda was thr most powerful Jedi master by a fairly large margin. I think other masters had specific things in which they were better than Yoda (for example, I think Windu was a better swordsman than Yoda). But as far as understanding of the metaphysics of the force, I think Yoda was far and away more advanced than any other being in the galaxy. Yes, since the lightsaber was the signature weapon of the Jedi, he certainly would have had one and known how to use it. I even acknowledge that he could have opened himself to the force and done exactly what he did in ep. 2. I believe it was within his capabilities. I don't think he would have, though. I think that the fight in ep. 2 is, from a real world standpoint, a masturbation fest for fanboys. I believe in universe, Dooku was trying to bait Yoda into a dick waving contest and Yoda fell for it. But I don't think he would have. I think Yoda would recognize it and not fall for the ploy. And just look at my avatar. Would Ben Kenobi really lie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=523940#post523940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh! But speaking of Kenobi, the original SW &quot;old master&quot;, notice that he also was not &quot;above&quot; using his lightsaber in a pitched battle in ANH, a fight whose ending showed that he had far greater understanding and mastery of the Force than his former pupil; also, that he surely must have been using the Force to compensate for his advanced age, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was Obi-Wan a Jedi Master though? I guess he was on the counsel, wasn't he? But, he seemed like he still identified more as a Jedi Knight, and thus wasn't beyond the need to use a lightsaber.<br /> <br /> I don't know. I guess I don't really have a good justification for why I'm with with old Obi-Wan fighting with a lightsaber and not Yoda....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T20:32:00-07:00","id":525044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=524982#post524982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. I guess I don't really have a good justification for why I'm with with old Obi-Wan fighting with a lightsaber and not Yoda....</div> </div> </div> </div>It's because you likely have a pre-conceived notion of what &quot;x&quot; should be -- and despite visual/narrative evidence to the contrary (by the originator of the work, vis-a-vis Lucas' own movies) -- you are holding onto it tenaciously. Yoda having a lightsaber makes complete and utter sense. His using it, when the situation calls for it, also makes complete and utter sense. That he normally *isn't* in a position to use/need it (being on the council and not &quot;in the field&quot;, as it were) is a completely separate narrative issue. Again, I think my video-game/TTRPG post from further up sheds some light on the perceptual shift involved; it doesn't matter if you're even a video-game player or not -- the &quot;leveling-up&quot; mentality still crosses over, however overtly or subtly, into many geeks minds when gauging a situation like this one. Take a few steps back from it, mentally, and give it a while. I think you'll come around... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T20:33:38-07:00","id":525045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=524382#post524382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid this is where the difference between directors show. In Empire Strikes Back, we see Darth Vader casually killing his admirals for failing him, and all at a distance between starships. I found that less boring and far more sinister and scary.<br /> Although I am reminded that in one of the games we see &quot;Starkiller&quot; fighting TIE fighters with nothing but the Force and his light-saber, and even bringing down a star-destroyer.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid you're misremembering. Vader doesn't kill anyone he's not on the same ship with. You're probably thinking of Adm. Ozzel, who he killed via viewscreen...but, as we saw earlier, they were all on the same ship. In fact, there's even a scene that deliberately shows us one of the captains *taking a shuttle* to Vader's super star destroyer before a quick cut to Vader choking him to death (also shows that Imperial officers are not without admirable qualities, as he surely knew his fate, but went to take responsiblity anyway). <br /> <br /> I'm told there is a deleted scene from the beginning of TPM, where Sidious Force chokes Nute Gunray from wherever he is, saying that mere space is no barrier to a Sith Lord, but the scene was cut, possibly because someone thought it jarred with the above...<br /> <br /> And don't get me started about Starkiller...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T22:50:03-07:00","id":525170,"title":"","content":"&quot;Don't be too proud of this technological terror you've constructed. The ability to destroy a planet is insignificant next to the power of the Force.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T23:23:54-07:00","id":525182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=523940#post523940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh! But speaking of Kenobi, the original SW &amp;quot;old master&amp;quot;, notice that he also was not &amp;quot;above&amp;quot; using his lightsaber in a pitched battle in ANH, a fight whose ending showed that he had far greater understanding and mastery of the Force than his former pupil; also, that he surely must have been using the Force to compensate for his advanced age, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obi-Wan wasn't relying on a cane to hobble around. To me, that's the difference between Jedi Master Kenobi using a lightsaber and Jedi Master Yoda using a lightsaber. It's similar to my reaction in the second movie when R2-D2 suddenly sprouted rockets and began flying all over the place. It's jarring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T11:03:26-07:00","id":525628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=525044#post525044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's because you likely have a pre-conceived notion of what &quot;x&quot; should be -- and despite visual/narrative evidence to the contrary (by the originator of the work, vis-a-vis Lucas' own movies) -- you are holding onto it tenaciously. Yoda having a lightsaber makes complete and utter sense. His using it, when the situation calls for it, also makes complete and utter sense. That he normally *isn't* in a position to use/need it (being on the council and not &quot;in the field&quot;, as it were) is a completely separate narrative issue. Again, I think my video-game/TTRPG post from further up sheds some light on the perceptual shift involved; it doesn't matter if you're even a video-game player or not -- the &quot;leveling-up&quot; mentality still crosses over, however overtly or subtly, into many geeks minds when gauging a situation like this one. Take a few steps back from it, mentally, and give it a while. I think you'll come around... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I just gotta start this by saying I'm not sure the creator of Star Wars, George Lucas, can exactly be trusted these days. I mean, he's just about ruined the OT with all his &quot;improvements&quot; every time a new version is released. I mean, can you honestly tell that Vader screaming NOOOOO improves that scene in Return of the Jedi when he throws the emperor down the shaft? Because I think it completely ruins it. Young Anakins Ghost is horrible. Changing Boba Fetts Voice is terrible. Completing changing the dialogue of the Vader/Emperor scene in Empire is awful. Jabba the Hutt adds nothing to A New Hope, etc. Lucas lost his way I feel...<br /> <br /> You want to see some great &quot;Special Editions&quot; check out what Adywan is doing with the Revisted editions. <a href=\"https://swrevisited.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swrevisited.wordpress.com/</a><br /> <br /> Thats what the special editions should be!<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, sorry, I went off a tangent. While I'll always love Lucas for creating Star Wars, he should have learned when to step back and let other people have a go at the universe, especially when it came to the prequels. I'm glad we have someone new helming the newer Star Wars movies.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm still having trouble seeing how Yoda with a lightsaber makes sense. You're telling me why it makes sense to you. Like I've said before, a young Jedi Knight Yoda would absolutely have and use a lightsaber. He is a Jedi after all and the Lightsaber is the weapon of choice for most Jedi. But, 800 year old Jedi Master Yoda doesn't really need one. He might have it, for sentimental reasons, but I still think he'd be way beyond needing to using it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I have stepped away from the prequels many times. If I don't the idea of by now, I think at this point I'm probably not gonna like it. :P<br /> <br /> But hey, I understand you love Yoda jumping around like the Tasmanian Devil, whirling around with his saber. And thats cool. I'm glad you enjoyed it. Hell, I love the look of Yoda's saber, it's pretty awesome. I'm just not big into him using it. But, like I said, that's my problem I guess. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I've been ruined by the RedLetterMedia &quot;Mr. Plinkett&quot; reviews of the prequels.<br /> <br /> If you really want to know my issues with Yoda and the Lightsaber, watch this video:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Blkx6axytKQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Blkx6axytKQ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Blkx6axytKQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Blkx6axytKQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It sums up my thoughts pretty good. Not sure you'll be into some of the humor of it, but that'll save you from watching the whole review. Though, I do invite you watch the Plinkettt Reviews of all the Star Wars prequels, as they are genius!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=525182#post525182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obi-Wan wasn't relying on a cane to hobble around. To me, that's the difference between Jedi Master Kenobi using a lightsaber and Jedi Master Yoda using a lightsaber. It's similar to my reaction in the second movie when R2-D2 suddenly sprouted rockets and began flying all over the place. It's jarring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! Jarring...there you go!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T13:13:16-07:00","id":525822,"title":"","content":"Personally, I loved that Yoda used a lightsaber and I don't think Jedi should ever be portrayed as being beyond using one, but I don't like how they made him use it. Scenes done with fully CG characters usually are noticeably fake even with state of the art CG. That ultra kinetic fighting style they gave him makes things even less grounded, and it looks really fake and takes me out of immersion. Might have worked if it was practical effects enhanced by CGI, but as it stands it doesn't work for me.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(Also, is he the only user of Form IV in the Galaxy, ever? Nobody in any of the movies, cartoons or comics I have seen fights like that) </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T21:09:49-07:00","id":528473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=525628#post525628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just gotta start this by saying I'm not sure the creator of Star Wars, George Lucas, can exactly be trusted these days. I mean, he's just about ruined the OT with all his &quot;improvements&quot; every time a new version is released. I mean, can you honestly tell that Vader screaming NOOOOO improves that scene in Return of the Jedi when he throws the emperor down the shaft? Because I think it completely ruins it. Young Anakins Ghost is horrible. Changing Boba Fetts Voice is terrible. Completing changing the dialogue of the Vader/Emperor scene in Empire is awful. Jabba the Hutt adds nothing to A New Hope, etc. Lucas lost his way I feel...<br /> <br /> You want to see some great &quot;Special Editions&quot; check out what Adywan is doing with the Revisted editions. <a href=\"https://swrevisited.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swrevisited.wordpress.com/</a><br /> <br /> Thats what the special editions should be!</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me clarify: there is a distinct difference between changing things for the movies that had already been done (Han/Greedo -- 'nuff said) vs. adding narratives in later-produced-but-occurring-earlier-in-said-narratives. That is, just because Yoda was even more old and crippled in the first trilogy doesn't mean that he shouldn't have &quot;x&quot; skills/ability in the earlier-set second trilogy. Important distinction, that. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=525628#post525628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I'm still having trouble seeing how Yoda with a lightsaber makes sense. You're telling me why it makes sense to you. Like I've said before, a young Jedi Knight Yoda would absolutely have and use a lightsaber. He is a Jedi after all and the Lightsaber is the weapon of choice for most Jedi. But, 800 year old Jedi Master Yoda doesn't really need one. He might have it, for sentimental reasons, but I still think he'd be way beyond needing to using it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But again, that is a highly peculiar perspective to have. Stop and *really* think about what you're saying/posting. No-no -- don't gloss over it as being a thought you already have in your mind -- <i>really stop and think about why you are holding this perspective in your mind, given that it inherently doesn't jibe with what has been demonstrated in the movies as well as in the novels</i> (which, granted, is a secondary source/canon, but still supportive of and informed by the primary movies). Really think about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=525628#post525628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But hey, I understand you love Yoda jumping around like the Tasmanian Devil, whirling around with his saber. And thats cool. I'm glad you enjoyed it. Hell, I love the look of Yoda's saber, it's pretty awesome. I'm just not big into him using it. But, like I said, that's my problem I guess. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I've been ruined by the RedLetterMedia &quot;Mr. Plinkett&quot; reviews of the prequels.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, now I *know* you haven't been properly reading my posts/responses -- I specifically said that I was *indifferent*, personally, to Yoda using a lightsaber. I couldn't care either way. What I *did* stress, though, was that it made perfect narrative sense for him to not only be skilled at its use, but to have one as well. Please (*please*) go back and re-read my post about the &quot;video-game-esque leveling-up&quot;-mentality that often subtly influences many geeks perspectives about in-narrative qualities. Yoda is most emphatically *not* &quot;so high a level&quot; nor &quot;so powerful&quot; that he wouldn't need the long-symbolic weapon/tool of his order... especially when going up against another powerful force-user, whether Dooku or Palpatine (the former being at least strong enough to make Yoda &quot;work for it&quot;, while the latter is a functional equal -- if differently skilled -- to Yoda). [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=525628#post525628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you really want to know my issues with Yoda and the Lightsaber, watch this video:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Blkx6axytKQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Blkx6axytKQ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Blkx6axytKQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Blkx6axytKQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It sums up my thoughts pretty good. Not sure you'll be into some of the humor of it, but that'll save you from watching the whole review. Though, I do invite you watch the Plinkettt Reviews of all the Star Wars prequels, as they are genius!</div> </div> </div> </div>I *get* the trans-narrative opinion about the *use* of the sabers, in the broad, but that really has little bearing on *Yoda's* use of it. If anything, it reinforces the narrator's point at the beginning of the video: when *Yoda* takes his lightsaber out, you KNOW he means business. That strengthens the comparative narration, not weakens it... (And yeah-yeah -- I know that the tone of the video, in general, is humorous is several respects, but I also know that the guy is serious in terms of what he's saying, too.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=525628#post525628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly! Jarring...there you go!</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Jarring&quot; only if you -- the viewer -- had the strange misconception that a Jedi *Master* <i>wouldn't</i> have a lightsaber and be kick-ass in using it, to boot. Jedi become *better* at using their signature weapon over time, both via mundane skill and by being more adept at using/channeling the force while wielding the weapon -- how that doesn't make sense is news to me. &gt;shrugs&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T21:49:30-07:00","id":528524,"title":"","content":"Can we please stop?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T06:39:44-07:00","id":528757,"title":"","content":"As you said &quot;please&quot;, your wish is my command.<br /> <br /> &gt;brandishes lightsaber and leaps into combat&lt;<br /> <br /> (Did I do that right?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T17:36:42-07:00","id":530438,"title":"","content":"So....what do people think about the apparently new faction in The Force Awakens: The First Order? Or that new Chrome Trooper. What about the new bad guy with the cross-guard lightsaber(speaking of lightsabers)?<br /> <br /> Also...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=93uSIKzPmik\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=93uSIKzPmik\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=93uSIKzPmik\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=93uSIKzPmik </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T19:39:28-07:00","id":605223,"title":"","content":"RISE FROM YOUR GRAVE.<br /> <br /> So. I'm jonesing for some Star Wars, and I'm wondering if the Clone Wars and Rebels series are any good. Which, if either of them, should I watch?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T20:09:17-07:00","id":605252,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen Rebels, but I'm making my way through Clone Wars. There are things I REALLY like about it and other things I hate. It doesn't really fit with the rest of Star Wars. If you consider it a parallel dimension that has many similarities to the regular Star Wars universe, it's great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T15:19:04-07:00","id":606006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=605252#post605252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen Rebels, but I'm making my way through Clone Wars. There are things I REALLY like about it and other things I hate. It doesn't really fit with the rest of Star Wars. If you consider it a parallel dimension that has many similarities to the regular Star Wars universe, it's great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you. In fact, I almost wish they had gone parallel universe with it. It'd have been awesome for them to do something unexpected and against what we know, then it feel like there some stakes to be raised!<br /> <br /> But, it was good for what it was, for the most part. I still need to finish the series I suppose...I bailed out right at the last season...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T21:57:02-07:00","id":606331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=606006#post606006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Totally with you. In fact, I almost wish they had gone parallel universe with it. It'd have been awesome for them to do something unexpected and against what we know, then it feel like there some stakes to be raised!<br /> <br /> But, it was good for what it was, for the most part. I still need to finish the series I suppose...I bailed out right at the last season...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, parallel dimensions isn't really a Star Wars thing. Star Trek, they do that all the time, but it would feel out of place in Star Wars. As would, for that matter, time travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T07:33:39-07:00","id":606552,"title":"","content":"True. One thing that Star Trek and Star Wars share is that neither is particularly big on hard science; but beyond that, they're very different: Star Trek is very much \u201cscience fiction\u201d, with high-concept episides that explore various what-if scenarios such as altered history; whereas Star Wars is much more \u201cspace fantasy\u201d, with traditional fantasy concepts wrapped in space opera trappings. And traditional fantasy doesn't really deal with parallel realities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T21:56:04-07:00","id":610386,"title":"","content":"Just watched the first part of Star Wars: Rebels.<br /> <br /> By the Force... this is Star Wars. This is what I wanted. This is what I've been missing.<br /> <br /> This. Is. Star Wars.<br /> <br /> To anyone who loves Star Wars: Watch this show!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T13:47:26-07:00","id":612572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=610386#post610386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just watched the first part of Star Wars: Rebels.<br /> <br /> By the Force... this is Star Wars. This is what I wanted. This is what I've been missing.<br /> <br /> This. Is. Star Wars.<br /> <br /> To anyone who loves Star Wars: Watch this show!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It gets better!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Season Two looks even more awesome, based on the first ep they showed us! Buuut...there's a pretty big spoiler I don't want to reveal, so I'll just *strongly* advise you to watch Clone Wars, as well.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And, all that stuff I wrote about expanding the subplot between Fett and Solo? Looks like Disney has similar ideas:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://screenrant.com/star-wars-han-solo-boba-fett-spinoff-movie/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static0.srcdn.com/assets/images/sr-logo-full-colored-light.svg?v=3.8\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://screenrant.com/star-wars-han-solo-boba-fett-spinoff-movie/\" target=\"_blank\"> ScreenRant </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://screenrant.com/star-wars-han-solo-boba-fett-spinoff-movie/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://screenrant.com/star-wars-han-solo-boba-fett-spinoff-movie/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T14:14:45-07:00","id":612595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=612572#post612572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It gets better!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Season Two looks even more awesome, based on the first ep they showed us! Buuut...there's a pretty big spoiler I don't want to reveal, so I'll just *strongly* advise you to watch Clone Wars, as well.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, see, here's the problem with that: As I understand it, Clone Wars is in the oeurve (is this an appropriate use of that word?) of the prequels... and that's just... hm.<br /> <br /> Clone Wars might be a really good show! But, I'm just not eager to go to the spa that's next to the landfill, if you get my drift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T14:51:17-07:00","id":612622,"title":"","content":"I hear you, but the important thing to remember is that the show is NOT directly made by the same folks who DID the prequels, so it shouldn't be tarred withthe same brush just because it takes place during the same time frame. I'm sure we can both think of stories where the reverse was true. So, try to take it on its own merits. The fact that a large majority ofthe SW fandom (so far as I see) loves the show while still hating the prequels should tell you something!<br /> <br /> Give it a shot (keeping in mind that, like many shows, it takes a bit to find its stride).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T16:14:39-07:00","id":612771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=612622#post612622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hear you, but the important thing to remember is that the show is NOT directly made by the same folks who DID the prequels, so it shouldn't be tarred withthe same brush just because it takes place during the same time frame. I'm sure we can both think of stories where the reverse was true. So, try to take it on its own merits. The fact that a large majority ofthe SW fandom (so far as I see) loves the show while still hating the prequels should tell you something!<br /> <br /> Give it a shot (keeping in mind that, like many shows, it takes a bit to find its stride).</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, if you say so.<br /> <br /> Just so you know, though (Spoiler alert):<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I already know that Fulcrum, Hera's Rebel handler, is Ahsoka Tano, Anakin's apprentice from the Clone Wars era. I found that out when I was doing some basic research on the show.<br /> If that's supposed to be the big reveal, well, already spoiled for me.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T18:34:29-07:00","id":612878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=606331#post606331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, parallel dimensions isn't really a Star Wars thing. Star Trek, they do that all the time, but it would feel out of place in Star Wars. As would, for that matter, time travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually ran a Star Wars game years ago that involved time travel. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The players didn't do the traveling mind you, but still. They seemed to really enjoy it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T21:07:32-07:00","id":612999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=612771#post612771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, if you say so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just keep in mind that the &quot;tone&quot; is different, just as the prequels' was from the OT...as they should be, given they're telling a different part of the story with themes of its own. Regardless of what one may think of the *quality*of the PT, it must be noted that the *tone* had to be its own thing. <br /> <br /> Rebels is making a *very* conscious effort to &quot;recapture&quot; the tone ofthe OT, and they're coming pretty close, IMO. It reminds to be seen if this is something the NT is attempting, or even if it *should* do so, rather than be its own thing...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just so you know, though (Spoiler alert):<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I already know that Fulcrum, Hera's Rebel handler, is Ahsoka Tano, Anakin's apprentice from the Clone Wars era. I found that out when I was doing some basic research on the show.<br /> If that's supposed to be the big reveal, well, already spoiled for me.</div></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, I was referring to how all but one of the main cast is surprise-killed off near the endof S1. Er, spoiler, I guess?<br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">This doesn't actually happen...OR DOES IT?? Mystery and Uncertainty restored!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T00:51:10-07:00","id":613080,"title":"","content":"I've taken a closer look at the Clone Wars series, and I've struck upon something.<br /> <br /> All of the characters look like they are made of wood.<br /> <br /> Wood that moves. And talks.<br /> <br /> ... Yeah, I'm gonna just have to take your word for it that the show is good. I'll just stick with Rebels, thank you. :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T10:49:27-07:00","id":613651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=613080#post613080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've taken a closer look at the Clone Wars series, and I've struck upon something.<br /> <br /> All of the characters look like they are made of wood.<br /> <br /> Wood that moves. And talks.<br /> <br /> ... Yeah, I'm gonna just have to take your word for it that the show is good. I'll just stick with Rebels, thank you. :/</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very deliberate...and not a sign of, as I thinkyou're suggesting, poor animation.<br /> <br /> As you may know, GL is a huge fan of classic cinema and tv, and he felt that CGI made for a good format to make the show a partial homage to the old <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yrCRYmVr0B8\" target=\"_blank\">Thunderbirds</a> tv show, where the characters were all string puppets. If it helps, this look doesn't last, tho I'm not sure how long it persisted; you don't even notice it after awhile. Go ahead and look at a random scene from the later eps to see how much the style changes...<br /> <br /> Animation is often tricky like this. I know Transfans who swore off Transformers Animated just because of the drastically stylized animation design...and missed out on some really cool character and plot developments because of that. But as always, YMMV!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T07:32:05-07:00","id":615048,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oi7KPDi_yQI\" data-code=\"oi7KPDi_yQI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/oi7KPDi_yQI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QqedbxGxfgE\" data-code=\"QqedbxGxfgE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/QqedbxGxfgE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T12:45:30-07:00","id":632627,"title":"","content":"I always check <a href=\"https://www.darkhorizons.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.darkhorizons.com</a> for all of the information and trailers for upcoming movies and what not. Then, I will also go to <a href=\"https://www.rainiertamayo.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.rainiertamayo.com</a> to watch what I can for free. The latter also included TV shows like The Flash, Arrow, Under the Dome, and many others. I found it when I was searching for a way to watch Game of Thrones online. And, it also has that show, and The Walking Dead, and many other... check it out.<br /> <br /> As far as the new Star Wars movies go, I am exceedingly hopefully that they have removed the suck factor that was instilled in the prequels that should never have been made... ever... may Jar Jar burn in hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1707-baldurkhan","name":"Baldurkhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T16:11:59-07:00","id":635120,"title":"","content":"\u2026or rot in the desert. (I heard a rumor that one of the new movies might include an \u201ceaster egg\u201d to this effect.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T08:43:24-07:00","id":672033,"title":"","content":"The store I work at has the new Star Wars section set up ever since &quot;Force Friday&quot; hit. One of my coworkers got the remote control droid and is really impressed at how cool it is! Everyday I pass by the cardboard stand-up of the new characters, marveling at the fact that I have no idea who they are, but will know them all extremely well soon enough!<br /> <br /> Sure, I could stop and read the backs of their action figures, and I'm tempted, but I'm trying to go into this thing as spoiler free as possible! Let's see how long THAT lasts...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T15:17:19-07:00","id":707528,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.comicbookmovie.com/fansites/JoshWildingNewsAndReviews/news/?a=126021\" target=\"_blank\">New Star Wars Movie Poster Revealed!</a> Possible Spoiler??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/a