":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T18:08:46-07:00","id":721311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=712849#post712849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta say, I *really* like what John Williams does with his iconic themes in the new trailer! Unfortunately, he's getting up in years, and just had to miss scoring a Steven Spielberg film for health reasons (the first one he's EVER missed in SS's career!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).<br /> <br /> Heaven forbid, but if he should be incapable of scoring the rest of the SW films, who would you like to see succeed him?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea...I don't know who could ever replace him. It'd be damn hard to do...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T02:05:18-07:00","id":728180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=721311#post721311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea...I don't know who could ever replace him. It'd be damn hard to do...</div> </div> </div> </div>Tru fact : When Steven Spielberg first asked John Williams to do the music for Schindler\u2019s List, Williams said that there was no way he would be able to do that film justice, and that Spielberg should look for a better composer. Spielberg replied, \u201cI know, but they\u2019re all dead.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T00:19:22-08:00","id":758133,"title":"","content":"I've got something on my mind and I have to get it out.<br /> <br /> I have seen someone who shall go unnamed profess the belief that Jedi never kill. That their ultimately lethal weapon is intended to end a fight before it got lethal, and that media that portrays Jedi as warriors is incorrect on that count.<br /> <br /> I find this aspersion to be completely ludicrous.<br /> <br /> Fact: There are precisely two full Jedi characters in the original trilogy: Obi-Wan and Yoda.<br /> Fact: Of these two Jedi, only Obi-Wan found himself in a situation that warranted a violent response.<br /> Fact: It is true that Kenobi tried to defuse the situation with diplomacy.<br /> Fact: It is also true that when that failed and somebody pulled a blaster, Kenobi <i>lopped a dude's arm off</i> and swung at a second guy at <i>point blank range</i>.<br /> Fact: There was a <i>lot</i> of blood.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: Jedi prefer non-lethal solutions when possible, but won't hold back when killing force is called for.<br /> <br /> And let's not even get<i> started</i> on Luke.<b> Yowza</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T04:11:02-08:00","id":758390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcod