ow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unless of course he's the chap on the left side of the poster with his face hidden...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At this point it is confirmed that Kylo Ren is not Luke Skywalker.<br /> <br /> On another note Mark Hamill more or less confirmed he will return as Luke in episode 8 and I am starting to fear for Han Solo's life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T07:16:25-08:00","id":773932,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah. He's gone from Action Hero to Wise Mentor; and in Star Wars, Wise Mentors don't have a very high survival rate. I just hope he gets a glorious send-off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T13:56:18-08:00","id":775017,"title":"","content":"I once read that Harrison Ford suggested that Han be killed during <i>Return of the Jedi</i>; and that George Lucas considered it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T03:13:49-08:00","id":775893,"title":"","content":"This is most likely Luke from the trailers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.flickeringmyth.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/star-wars-force-awakens-r2d2-01-636-380.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making Star Wars WoD conversion. Gonna be done when it's done. Hopefully not too long now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2217-darthmrn","name":"DarthMRN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T12:44:29-08:00","id":776149,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://instantrimshot.com/index.php?sound=rimshot&amp;play=true\" target=\"_blank\">I think that's R2D2.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-28-2015, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T19:35:31-08:00","id":776377,"title":"","content":"Harrison Ford wanted Han killed off in ether Empire or Jedi (I think it was the later), and I wouldn't be surprised to see it happen.<br /> <br /> Hamil's talked in interviews about how he pitched to George Lucas the idea of Luke taking a heel turn in Jedi. Despite concern amongst fans, I'd be surprised to see that happen now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T21:39:33-08:00","id":776415,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, \u201cAlways two there are: a master and an apprentice.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T01:35:44-08:00","id":776486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=776415#post776415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, \u201cAlways two there are: a master and an apprentice.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, we currently have both. Supreme Leader Snoke(Andy Serkins) and Kylo Ren(Adam Driver). I hope that we see some different story elements on Luke's (self-?) exile than the ones they used for Yoda and Obi-Wan.<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you guys think are the chances of Snoke being Darth Plagueis? I am still not convinced that he is but it seems to be the most popular theory out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T09:05:23-08:00","id":776617,"title":"","content":"For good reason. Plenty of indications, and greater thematic appropriateness than any new villain would add. Ties up loose ends from the Prequels too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making Star Wars WoD conversion. Gonna be done when it's done. Hopefully not too long now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2217-darthmrn","name":"DarthMRN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T19:41:34-08:00","id":776949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=776486#post776486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we currently have both. Supreme Leader Snoke(Andy Serkins) and Kylo Ren(Adam Driver). I hope that we see some different story elements on Luke's (self-?) exile than the ones they used for Yoda and Obi-Wan.<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you guys think are the chances of Snoke being Darth Plagueis? I am still not convinced that he is but it seems to be the most popular theory out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. I kind of hope not...but, we'll see how it goes.<br /> <br /> In the book Star Wars Aftermath, there is talk of finding the Darkside in the far reaches of the galaxy(and beyond it), so perhaps Snoke is something from there...?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T06:31:33-08:00","id":777111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=776486#post776486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys think are the chances of Snoke being Darth Plagueis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible. Maybe Sidious kept his brain in a jar after the betrayal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T19:48:04-08:00","id":778053,"title":"","content":"I do worry from what we've seen that Luke will end up some poor cousin Darth Vader. I also wonder at first that we have a similar story to the pre-Old Republic going on too. Though I admit the newer trailers made it feel less that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T07:38:11-08:00","id":779794,"title":"","content":"Well, I finally caved and got a ticket online, one of the only times I've ever done so. Was surprised at how many spots for the first showing on the 17th are still open, maybe people just figure they'll all be taken and didn't bother looking? <br /> <br /> BTW, if you're in or abouts Austin, Texas, <a href=\"http://www.cntraveler.com/stories/2015-11-19/17-hours-alamo-marathon-star-wars-the-force-awakens?mbid=social_cp_facebook_ars\" target=\"_blank\">then you have a chance to see ALL the movies leading up to the new one!</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=776149#post776149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://instantrimshot.com/index.php?sound=rimshot&amp;play=true\" target=\"_blank\">I think that's R2D2.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Either that, or Mark has REALLY let himself go!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Apparently, he even went online to personally debunk rumors that Skywalker was Kylo Ren; if true, I can see Abrams chewing him out for ruining &quot;The Mystery&quot; that he so often cultivates among fans! <br /> <br /> I never thought Luke was KR, but I strongly suspect that he may have been his Master, that Ren was his first student, but history repeated, and he fell to the Dark Side and betrayed his Master. Maybe he's got Luke imprisoned somewhere...<br /> <br /> I also don't get the &quot;feel&quot; of a Bad Guy Name from &quot;Kylo Ren&quot;, so I'm expecting him to do a Face Switch pretty soon, maybe even in the next movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T13:03:44-08:00","id":780076,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://scontent.cdninstagram.com/hphotos-xaf1/t51.2885-15/s480x480/e35/11355852_792366110885285_74185686_n.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Not exactly the strongest debunking ever. But given the sheer number of villains already, and how dang safe Disney is being with this film, I have strong doubts he has gone dark. I think there is a different reason for his face being hidden...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making Star Wars WoD conversion. Gonna be done when it's done. Hopefully not too long now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2217-darthmrn","name":"DarthMRN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T09:57:49-08:00","id":783494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarthMRN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=780076#post780076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly the strongest debunking ever. But given the sheer number of villains already, and how dang safe Disney is being with this film, I have strong doubts he has gone dark. I think there is a different reason for his face being hidden...</div> </div> </div> </div>Query: How is Disney being &quot;safe&quot; with this movie? I hadn't heard anything to suggest that...<br /> <br /> I will note that, after the disastrous reaction they got from killing off Chewie in the novels, there seems to have been an unwritten/unofficial rule in place that the EU would NEVER again kill off any of the movie characters. Which I think is a real shame, straitjacking the creators like that, but fan overreaction ruining things isn't new...Anyway, I just hope that the creators of the new movies aren't similarly bound. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CC8THtokVdg\" target=\"_blank\">Speaking of Mark Hamill</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T10:09:26-08:00","id":783501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=783494#post783494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will note that, after the disastrous reaction they got from killing off Chewie in the novels, there seems to have been an unwritten/unofficial rule in place that the EU would NEVER again kill off any of the movie characters. Which I think is a real shame, straitjacking the creators like that, but fan overreaction ruining things isn't new...Anyway, I just hope that the creators of the new movies aren't similarly bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chewie was killed because the <i>author</i> was straightjacketed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T10:59:11-08:00","id":783527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=783501#post783501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chewie was killed because the <i>author</i> was straightjacketed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Explain, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T14:36:43-08:00","id":788346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=783501#post783501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chewie was killed because the <i>author</i> was straightjacketed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The implication being that the author was forced to write that event by editorial? Regardless of *why* it happened, my point about the fan reaction and (possible) company reaction stands.<br /> <br /> Anywho, just a couple of hours until the first showing; I'm gonna leave early in anticipation of a long line and holiday traffic. Been psyching myself up all day with a marathon of all the movies, which I'm just wrapping up now. <br /> <br /> Last thoughts before heading into a new era of SW fandom: Mostly, I just hope they don't screw this up! One criticism I've had from watching the previews was the heavy leaning on nostalgia; clearly, the filmmakers are tryingto appeal to the disgruntled fans who have loudly decried the prequels, with lots of &quot;this is SW as you remember it&quot; (a process also seen in SW: Rebels)! This can be both good and bad; regardless of the quality of its execution, at least TPM introduced some *new* things in the SW universe. Most of what I've seen so far from TFA is along the lines of &quot;Look, TIE fighters chasing the Falcon! Just like you remember from your childhood, right?!&quot; <br /> <br /> Of course, these are just a relative few images meant to lure us in, so hopefully this won't be *that* desperate or widespread throughout the movie/s. Hopefully, there will be plenty of new ideas, just executed much better than in the last movies we got! <br /> <br /> Well, I'll know soon enough, and will let you all know, too! See ya on the other side, guys!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T15:02:02-08:00","id":788356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=788346#post788346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Last thoughts before heading into a new era of SW fandom: Mostly, I just hope they don't screw this up! One criticism I've had from watching the previews was the heavy leaning on nostalgia; clearly, the filmmakers are tryingto appeal to the disgruntled fans who have loudly decried the prequels, with lots of &quot;this is SW as you remember it&quot; (a process also seen in SW: Rebels)! This can be both good and bad; regardless of the quality of its execution, at least TPM introduced some *new* things in the SW universe. Most of what I've seen so far from TFA is along the lines of &quot;Look, TIE fighters chasing the Falcon! Just like you remember from your childhood, right?!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit I wasn't really excited about the new movie until io9 posted an international trailer. <a href=\"http://io9.gizmodo.com/this-the-force-awakens-trailer-is-probably-your-last-hi-1747287133\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.gizmodo.com/this-the-forc...-hi-1747287133</a> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T16:34:38-08:00","id":788395,"title":"","content":"From a reviewer I trust, the ever colorful <a href=\"http://moviebob.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Moviebob</a>:<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;It's fine.</b> Relax.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;And\u2026 yeah, so be it, I\u2019ll say it, you guys win:<br /> <br /> <b>STAR WARS is back</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>THANK THE FORCE.</b><br /> <br /> I knew there was a reason that fanfare got to me every time! My fears are dispelled. I'm ready to have my socks knocked off!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T19:32:13-08:00","id":788476,"title":"","content":"Just got back. Good movie. Felt unfinished (as in, you can tell it's setting up a trilogy too much). May have leaned a bit too hard on the introductions of the old cast. But, do want to see where they take this.<br /> <br /> And, I'm calling it <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Rey is Luke's daughter </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T19:32:59-08:00","id":788477,"title":"","content":"Aaand, I'm back! Well, that was...interesting!<br /> <br /> Any questions, inquiries, spoiler requests?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: Sure was weird seeing the opening *without* the 20th Century Fox Fanfare...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 12-17-2015, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T20:36:28-08:00","id":788510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=788477#post788477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Sure was weird seeing the opening *without* the 20th Century Fox Fanfare...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Man, that <i>does</i> sound weird. Is it the Disney fanfare now?<br /> <br /> Question: How many Force users are in the movie? (Not <i>who</i>, just how many.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T20:56:38-08:00","id":788514,"title":"","content":"Just got back from seeing it.<br /> <br /> I thought it was excellent! Star Wars is back! That is all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T21:27:04-08:00","id":788521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=788395#post788395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a reviewer I trust, the ever colorful <a href=\"http://moviebob.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Moviebob</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that's pretty on point! I only disagree with a couple of points there...<br /> <br /> NO SPOILERS here, btw, just notes on general story/tone/mood, etc:<br /> <br /> I had no problem with the dialog at all. In fact, this may well be THE funniest SW movie ever! And yet, I overheard people saying that they didn't expect that it would be &quot;so dark&quot;...honestly, it topples Empire from its place as the darkest of the Originals, although it may be on par with Revenge.<br /> <br /> The thing that really got me, and that I most struggled with, in opposition tothe above link, was how much this did NOT look and feel like a traditional SW film. It felt like...If you were a fan of the original Battlestar Galactica or any of the Stargate series, and then saw the recent BSG series, or Stargate Universe, it's that kind of disconnect. This movie is *very much* a Modern Film, using techniques like desaturated colors to get that &quot;realistic&quot; feel Hollywood is so in love with (thankfully, there's virtually no usage of Shaky-Cam, at least none that were strong enough for me to remember)! Modern filmmakers/audiences just prefer a darker, more &quot;realistic&quot; aestethic and content, so that's just the zeitgeist, really...<br /> <br /> This even extended to the music. John Williams' score seemed pretty light on the flourishes and fanfares, seemingly influenced by Hans Zimmer-esque droning sounds, in places; sadly, nothing in it really grabbed me. Well, I need to give it a listen by itself, maybe I was distracted by all the imagery. Which is pretty great, btw, there are a few truly beautiful shots that stood out as almost Painterly! <br /> <br /> But yeah, the film had this mix of looking and feeling very modern, while still trying to capture that Classic SW feel. People may disagree on how well it nailed it, but I think it did. The newer leads are likable and work very well together. The older ones, despite all the cynical sniping the actors have made about SW over the years, surprised me by selling me on them, which I guess just means that they're very good at *acting*, right? Harrison Ford in particular seems to be having a ball! And despite my fears, there was a very good mix of story time/material both everyone (well, Poe got a bit shafted, I guess). <br /> <br /> But these are good people, who like each other, and will risk it all for each other. I concur, I really want to see where they go next, honestly even more than I did for the original Star Warriors!<br /> <br /> And, yeah, some of the plot background could really use some shoring up, not just to show how things got from ep 6 to 7, but I'm still unclear on how exactly things are set up in *this* era. <br /> <br /> But is it a Good movie? Technically, pretty much everything they put up on screen was probably as well done as it could be. Acting, effects, sets, costumes, I'd say they knocked it out of the park! Aside from the soundtrack, which was the last thing I expected to be &quot;meh&quot; about, but there you are. The plot? Well, SW was never about great plot, and MB nailed it when he summarized it as kind of a rehash of the Original SW (with strong elements from the EU for flavoring, I'd add!). But whatever, it's cool and fun, and honestly, may be the most technically accomplished SW movie out of ALL of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, good? Yes. Should you go see it? HELL, yes!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T21:32:39-08:00","id":788522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=788510#post788510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, that <i>does</i> sound weird. Is it the Disney fanfare now?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the Magic Kingdom logo, but with Watto instead of Tinkerbell. No, but seriously...um, I actually fo