userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T05:18:29-08:00","id":791503,"title":"","content":"I haz theories.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Rey was the youngest/strongest of Luke's trainees before being dropped off on Jakku. Kylo Ren didn't kill all of the other trainees just like Vader didn't actually kill all of the Jedi (like Kanan from Rebels or Ahsoka Tanno). Kylo is the leader of the Knights of Ren because they are other students of Luke's who followed Ben Solo in changing sides. Luke hid Rey to prevent her from being taken along with the other kids Ben converted instead of killing, and Luke probably tampered with her memory before leaving her under the watch of Max Von Sydow, who I believe is the old version of Kanan from Rebels, just like Obi Wan watched over Luke.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T05:55:43-08:00","id":791516,"title":"","content":"The following is a discussion of the argument that Rey from <b>Star Wars: the Force Awakens</b> is a Mary Sue. It is nearly spoiler-free because I will not be discussing Rey or the movie directly: I will instead be discussing the original trilogy as a point of comparison. However, the comparisons I make will be enough to lead a clever person to deduce certain spoilers, so if you're worried, now is the time to close this window. <br /> <br /> Okay, they're gone. Let's talk Episode IV.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Consider for a moment that in the original trilogy (and we will be ignoring the prequels for how much they contradict their own canon), Obi-Wan Kenobi is not telekinetic. That is a power Darth Vader possesses, as shown by him choking a dude from slightly further away than if he just did it with his hands, but not Obi-Wan. Obi-Wan, the only Jedi Knight we ever meet and who must be the representative example of all Jedi Knights, only has powers of foresight so mild Han can reasonably dismiss them as mere intuition, and powers to convince stupid people to do what he wants. Extremely mild telepathy, of the variety that a skeptic could scoff off as con artistry. <br /> <br /> So he takes Luke under his wing, and after a bit of training over the course of a couple of hours, Luke's powers have already surpassed anything we ever see Obi-Wan do: His intuition is so sharp he can see while blind and block needle-thin blasts with a narrow rod. That's genuine prescience right there, no matter what Han Solo thinks.<br /> <br /> But that's not even the most powerful thing Luke does. No, the most powerful thing he ever does, the thing that everything else in the trilogy shrivels in comparison to, is his attack on the Death Star. <br /> <br /> Wedge Antilles warns the audience in the briefing scene that the shot needed to destroy the Death Star is impossible even for a computer. Luke disagrees, but Wedge is right: Someone tries to make the shot with a computer and fails. His torpedoes can't fit through the exhaust port's aperture and detonate on the surface. Only Luke can make that shot, and he does it by exerting telekinetic force and precision unparalleled by anything else ever showed in the movies: He seized control of <i>two</i> missiles traveling at whatever absurd velocity is necessary for a dogfight and made them turn <i>ninety degrees</i> in such tight formation they both go through a hole barely big enough to accommodate them, then level out and fly straight to the Death Star's core. On two hours of training, he can do what a targeting computer can't and he can control the trajectories of two air-to-air missiles. Simultaneously. Darth Vader's recreation of <b>Poltergeist</b> on Cloud City shrivels in shame compared to the mighty Force cock swinging between Luke's legs. The only person who can even compete us the Emperor making lightning from nothing, and even then, all he's doing is converting one kind of energy (the Force) to electricity. Converting energy to electricity is no big thing. People do that shit all the time with machines. <br /> <br /> Seriously, I cannot overstate the amount of power it takes to overcome the velocity of two missiles at the same time with that level of precision. If you were to stand in traffic while two cars bear down on you at seventy miles per hour and you made them both swerve just by thinking at them real hard, that would still be magnitudes less impressive than what Luke did, and he did it on two hours of training that definitely did <i>not</i> include Telekinesis 101. He taught himself to do that. <br /> <br /> What Rey accomplishes in the final ten minutes of the movie is <i>nothing</i> compared to what Luke did. <br /> <br /> Also, I don't want to hear about her piloting skills being unrealistic. In Episode IV, no one in the Rebellion thinks it's weird that a farmer's skill at driving a pickup truck translates to being able to fly an F-14 in a combat situation with no training. The universe they live in is one where that's just an expected skill. Rey has a better reason for her piloting skills than Luke does.<br /> <br /> So, in short, I disagree with the assessment that Rey is any kind of Mary Sue.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T06:12:15-08:00","id":791521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791090#post791090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw it yesterday.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding your thoughts on Kylo Ren:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Kylo Ren is a stupid, emotional teenager.<br /> <br /> That is not a criticism of the movie or the acting or the writing. It's a thought I had while examining Kylo Ren's visual design and thinking to myself, &quot;My god, he's unattractive. Every single choice they've made about his clothes and hair makes him look gangly, misproportioned, and lanky, like a Ferris Bueller wearing Cameron's dad'd clothes <i>ohhhhhh</i> I get it. That was <i>intentional</i>.&quot; Kylo Ren is a little boy with tons of daddy issues (issues with both his daddies), trying to live up to the idea of his grandfather he never even met so it's a complete fantasy he cut from whole cloth. He's not a man like Darth Vader was; he's a boy playing make-believe. He's not committed to his role as a villain. Remember, even Snoke warned him that killing Han would be a trial he's not ready for, and what happens? He ignores his second daddy's advice, kills Han anyway, and loses so much control and focus from it that despite having done it before in the movie like it's nothing, despite having been <i>warned it was about to happen</i> by Chewie's roar of rage, he still gets shot in the gut like a punk. Because he is a punk. His powers don't change the fact that he's a punk.<br /> <br /> So when Rey faces off against him, displaying no more impressive knowledge of the Force than Luke did as outlined in my previous post, let's remember the state Kylo Ren was in: He was bleeding out from a gut wound, and he was in such enormous emotional turmoil from having murdered his own father that he apparently couldn't even use the Force enough to knock Finn around and had to do it with his lightsaber.<br /> <br /> Kylo Ren is a punk who nearly got his ass kicked by a woman we've already seen kicking multiple punks' asses simultaneously (those two punks on Jakku who tried to steal BB8). Now, in the next movie, if he's finished his training, he might not be such a punk getting his punk ass kicked, but in this movie? I think it's well established he's not half as bad-ass as he thinks he is, and that's before you factor in all the dialogue that explicitly tells us he's still in training.<br /> <br /> Kylo Ren doesn't lose because Rey is so awesome. Kylo Ren loses because Kylo Ren sucks a lot more than he thinks he does.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T06:34:55-08:00","id":791536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791516#post791516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in short, I disagree with the assessment that Rey is any kind of Mary Sue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I regret that I can only like your post once, so QFT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T07:12:15-08:00","id":791552,"title":"","content":"If any of my theory turns out to be correct then Rey is most definitely not a Mary Sue. And Jim's assessment of Kylo Ren seem pretty spot on to me.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnother question, did anyone else notice during the pivotal light saber fight that the two blades seemed to merge together to form a purple blade from someone's perspective, and do you think that was more foreshadowing? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-fami