 of rage, he still gets shot in the gut like a punk. Because he is a punk. His powers don't change the fact that he's a punk.<br /> <br /> So when Rey faces off against him, displaying no more impressive knowledge of the Force than Luke did as outlined in my previous post, let's remember the state Kylo Ren was in: He was bleeding out from a gut wound, and he was in such enormous emotional turmoil from having murdered his own father that he apparently couldn't even use the Force enough to knock Finn around and had to do it with his lightsaber.<br /> <br /> Kylo Ren is a punk who nearly got his ass kicked by a woman we've already seen kicking multiple punks' asses simultaneously (those two punks on Jakku who tried to steal BB8). Now, in the next movie, if he's finished his training, he might not be such a punk getting his punk ass kicked, but in this movie? I think it's well established he's not half as bad-ass as he thinks he is, and that's before you factor in all the dialogue that explicitly tells us he's still in training.<br /> <br /> Kylo Ren doesn't lose because Rey is so awesome. Kylo Ren loses because Kylo Ren sucks a lot more than he thinks he does.</div></div> </div> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Agreed.<br /> <br /> Ren's oh-so-cool weapon of choice isn't just cool because it's new; it's cool because it's a <i>perfect encapsulation of his character</i>.<br /> <br /> Taking a close look at this weapon, it's the saber of someone with little-to-no regard for patience, forethought or restraint. It's slapdash and looks unfinished, with exposed internal components and wiring on the outside of the body. It's blade is unstable, an almost surefire sign that either the crystal or the saber's components were put together improperly. The way Kylo uses it (<i>has</i> to really, with those side emitters), it should have a longer hilt to provide more force and control, but it's the same length as a regular saber.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hm. I want an intimidating weapon; something to give me the edge over those do-gooder dorks! But I don't have the time or inclination to learn how to use a double-bladed lightsaber; what should I do? I know! I'll stick two smaller blades on and make a claymore! That's the gimmick I need!&quot;<br /> <br /> Kylo Ren's weapon is a tool for a thug: sacrificing precision and elegance for brute force and shortcuts.<br /> <br /> <i>I absolutely adore it.</i></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{