is weapon, it's the saber of someone with little-to-no regard for patience, forethought or restraint. It's slapdash and looks unfinished, with exposed internal components and wiring on the outside of the body. It's blade is unstable, an almost surefire sign that either the crystal or the saber's components were put together improperly. The way Kylo uses it (<i>has</i> to really, with those side emitters), it should have a longer hilt to provide more force and control, but it's the same length as a regular saber.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hm. I want an intimidating weapon; something to give me the edge over those do-gooder dorks! But I don't have the time or inclination to learn how to use a double-bladed lightsaber; what should I do? I know! I'll stick two smaller blades on and make a claymore! That's the gimmick I need!&quot;<br /> <br /> Kylo Ren's weapon is a tool for a thug: sacrificing precision and elegance for brute force and shortcuts.<br /> <br /> <i>I absolutely adore it.</i></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I also took the crossguard as a sign of his reverence for his grandfather. He's probably aware that almost every time Vader was defeated in a lightsaber duel, it was due to having his hand cut off. Same thing happened to his uncle, who we know he trained under, and can probably assume he learned at least some lightsaber combat from. It makes a lot of sense that he would want to build his own lightsaber in such a way that will insure the same won't happen to him.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T10:18:38-08:00","id":791665,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Looks to me like Kylo's &quot;precaution&quot; didn't pay off so well.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bAs for the crossguard light saber design, it's an ancient, inefficient Sith design that Kylo used and the crossguard is actually a venting system for the excess plasma energy that design produces, to keep it from overloading the containment field around the energy blade. That's not speculation, it's the official explanation for the design. I read up on a bunch of stuff prior to the movie which is why I enjoyed it so much more than my friend who went into it blind and was confused by a lot of things, like the difference between the Rebellion and Resistance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 12-23-2015, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T10:58:31-08:00","id":791689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791552#post791552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If any of my theory turns out to be correct then Rey is most definitely not a Mary Sue. And Jim's assessment of Kylo Ren seem pretty spot on to me.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnother question, did anyone else notice during the pivotal light saber fight that the two blades seemed to merge together to form a purple blade from someone's perspective, and do you think that was more foreshadowing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh i miss that one. Episode 8: The windu strikes back :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791665#post791665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Looks to me like Kylo's &quot;precaution&quot; didn't pay off so well.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bAs for the crossguard light saber design, it's an ancient, inefficient Sith design that Kylo used and the crossguard is actually a venting system for the excess plasma energy that design produces, to keep it from overloading the containment field around the energy blade. That's not speculation, it's the official explanation for the design. I read up on a bunch of stuff prior to the movie which is why I enjoyed it so much more than my friend who went into it blind and was confused by a lot of things, like the difference between the Rebellion and Resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I friend told me there was a book, explaning all that stuff. Im really curious about the difference between rebellion and the resistance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T11:20:08-08:00","id":791699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791536#post791536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I regret that I can only like your post once, so QFT.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, bro.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791552#post791552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAnother question, did anyone else notice during the pivotal light saber fight that the two blades seemed to merge together to form a purple blade from someone's perspective, and do you think that was more foreshadowing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did and I do. They did something similar during the Anakin-Dooku fight in Episode II, which I thought was one of the better parts of the movie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791609#post791609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that in Empire Strikes back, as we are discussing the original trilogy, yoda doesnt show surprise at luke attempts to lift his Xwing from the swamp and indeed show knowledge in how to train him in that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but I can't penetrate this sentence. What are you trying to say here? Is it a comparison between Yoda and Obi-Wan? Because I don't think it's fair to compare a Jedi <i>Knight</i> to a Jedi <i>Master</i>.<br /> <br /> (You know, thinking about these movies from a chronological perspective, I just want to say words like &quot;Jedi&quot; are common and accepted by us, but the actors saying them were saying them for the first time, and they deserve credit for making us believe them. Moving on.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791609#post791609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I wouldn't call the Jedi mind trick a con. It's direct mind control.</div> </div> </div> </div>You and I as omniscient audience know that, but an observer in the universe would not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791609#post791609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even in the EU, it shows something that requires knowledge of the Force to which Luke's attempts at fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't matter. The EU has been explicitly declared irrelevant by Disney.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791609#post791609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a pretty big exaggeration.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not. You can assume Obi-Wan has other powers if you want to, but in the original trilogy, we never see them. Luke surpasses what we see him do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791609#post791609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The velocity of the torpedoes is of no concern as he is already moving at top speed on his own ship.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does matter. The speed at which an object is moving is a factor in how much energy is required to redirect that object. Why do you think it drained Iron Man's arc reactor to redirect the nuke in <b>Marvel's Avengers</b>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791609#post791609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Luke's training with Obi-Wan was days instead of hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not a thing we are shown. What is your source for this assertion?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791609#post791609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Luke is this supposed master of telekinesis, then why he [does he have] so much trouble forcepulling his lightsaber in Empire Strikes Back?</div> </div> </div> </div>Use of the Force relies on calm and focus. Luke was beaten up, freezing, in danger of being eaten, and hung upside down so blood flow to his brain was clouding his mind. You saw him have to focus on calming himself down to get it to work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791609#post791609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, you are referring to me here?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791609#post791609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must ask, how is what you said contradicting what i said?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say I'm contradicting you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T11:43:34-08:00","id":791714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791665#post791665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Looks to me like Kylo's &quot;precaution&quot; didn't pay off so well.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bAs for the crossguard light saber design, it's an ancient, inefficient Sith design that Kylo used and the crossguard is actually a venting system for the excess plasma energy that design produces, to keep it from overloading the containment field around the energy blade. That's not speculation, it's the official explanation for the design. I read up on a bunch of stuff prior to the movie which is why I enjoyed it so much more than my friend who went into it blind and was confused by a lot of things, like the difference between the Rebellion and Resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's awesome. By my little bit of research, it's looking like the reason for all that excess energy is a cracked crystal? That leads me to wonder if he cracked his intentionally, or if it was due to some sort of mishap. I also wonder if it's natural or synthetic, since irregular synth crystals that produced excess energy and risk shorting out were a thing in the EU, but we don't know if that'll make it to Disney's new cannon or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T12:26:41-08:00","id":791741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791699#post791699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, but I can't penetrate this sentence. What are you trying to say here? Is it a comparison between Yoda and Obi-Wan? Because I don't think it's fair to compare a Jedi <i>Knight</i> to a Jedi <i>Master</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791699#post791699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;<i>Consider for a moment that in the original trilogy (and we will be ignoring the prequels for how much they contradict their own canon), Obi-Wan Kenobi is not telekinetic. That is a power Darth Vader possesses, as shown by him choking a dude from slightly further away than if he just did it with his hands, but not Obi-Wan. Obi-Wan, the only Jedi Knight we ever meet and who must be the representative example of all Jedi Knights, only has powers of foresight so mild Han can reasonably dismiss them as mere intuition, and powers to convince stupid people to do what he wants. Extremely mild telepathy, of the variety that a skeptic could scoff off as con artistry.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>As if the telekinesis was something beyond the reach of Obi Wan. Yet disregarding the EU, neither him nor yoda show surprise at luke advancement or surprise when he manage to do telekinesis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791699#post791699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You and I as omniscient audience know that, but an observer in the universe would not.</div> </div> </div> </div>So?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791699#post791699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's not. You can assume Obi-Wan has other powers if you want to, but in the original trilogy, we never see them. Luke surpasses what we see him do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet the other jedi we saw doesnt seem surprise at luke progress or powers which is indicative that while talented he is not near the level of a master jedi. That and the fact that he gets his ass handed to him by vader in Empire strikes back when Yoda tells him he hasnt complete his training. You might be only counting a new hope in you argument. And in the original trilogy Obi Wan says that yoda was his master and yoda does train luke in telekinesis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791699#post791699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does matter. The speed at which an object is moving is a factor in how much energy is required to redirect that object. Why do you think it drained Iron Man's arc reactor to redirect the nuke in <b>Marvel's Avengers</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all what the Avengers have to do with this? Are the same universe now? Should i expect a star wars/avengers crossover? Because im totally watching that.<br /> <br /> That raises a lot of question that star was doesnt answer. From its weight, to whether the torpedos are matter or energy. The &quot;energy usage&quot; is also in question as Yoda says that the size doesnt matter and speed barely if both object are moving at barely different speeds and there is no wind resistance (or maybe there is, its star wars after all). And in that same vein, shitty sith as he is<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Kylo manage to stop a blaster in mid air without any visible effort, something that vader barely mange to do so. So by your logic he must be the best jedi/sith of his generation, which he is not.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Again by you parameter of &quot;only taking the original trilogy and nothing else&quot; then size and speed doesnt matter as yoda said in episode 5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791699#post791699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not a thing we are shown. What is your source for this assertion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I vaguely remember reading it on the novelization but from <a href=\"http://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Luke_Skywalker#Force_powers\" target=\"_blank\">http://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Luke_...r#Force_powers</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, most of what he learned was self-taught due to Kenobi's, and later Yoda's, <u><b>few days of mentorship before their demise</b></u>, and Kenobi's sporadic guidance from beyond the Netherworld of the Force </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Use of the Force relies on calm and focus. Luke was beaten up, freezing, in danger of being eaten, and hung upside down so blood flow to his brain was clouding his mind. You saw him have to focus on calming himself down to get it to work. </div> </div> </div>And by your logic that some movements with telekinesis require &quot;more energy&quot; than others a simple trick like that one way less energy than the torpedos. So it either relies on calm and focus or &quot;energy&quot; which make size and density matter? Which one?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Rey manages to do a mind trick without any instruction. After exhausting herself to prevent kylo to mindrape her the previous scene and during a time constrain and stressful situation.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791699#post791699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.<br /> I didn't say I'm contradicting you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh ok, just making sure.<br /> <br /> In the end i believe the character is a mary sue. Those 2 scenes broke it for me and they could have being handle better<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Rey just destroying the manacles with the force a la vader in episode 3 and leia huging chewie</div></div> </div> </div> and while its fine you disagree you seem to keep changing &quot;what counts&quot; for the arguments in your favor. First it was only the trilogy but then you ignore stuff from the V and VI, so now its only the New Hope and then its new hope with only the parts we saw and no posibility to infer. And then its only to infer when it suit your argument (because you can infer that kenobi cant do telekinesis but i cant infer he does with the evidence supporting both. You can infer that size and speed matter even though its contradicted in episode 5 but i can infer that the mindtrick is a hard trick to pull off). You said EU doesnt matter, which is fine but then there is lot of stuff that never gets an explanation, you try to introduce rl science on the argument on the setting in which light travels on less velocity than a bullet (or the same) and there is noise in space but ignore any EU explanation on the rules of how and why.<br /> <br /> So yeah, believe what you want honestly this argument meant more to you than me apparently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791714#post791714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's awesome. By my little bit of research, it's looking like the reason for all that excess energy is a cracked crystal? That leads me to wonder if he cracked his intentionally, or if it was due to some sort of mishap. I also wonder if it's natural or synthetic, since irregular synth crystals that produced excess energy and risk shorting out were a thing in the EU, but we don't know if that'll make it to Disney's new cannon or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>He cracked it to be more edgy. Oh please let that be the canon reason, please.<br /> <br /> I never realize how much i wanted a Sith Poser in the star wars until i we got one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 12-23-2015, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T13:17:51-08:00","id":791760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791741#post791741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[stuff]</div> </div> </div> </div>I was doing my usual point-by-point response when I realized I have completely lost track of what your central argument is, LokiRavenSpeak. You seem to be arguing that nothing Luke accomplished is a big deal, except when it comes to comparing his accomplishments to Rey's, in which case they're a huge deal and she shouldn't even be able to fly a plane like he can despite having been involved in retrofitting the damned thing. It leaves me with the impression that you're not following a track of logic to a conclusion, but rather defending a conclusion by using whatever tracks of logic you can cobble together, and I'm just less interested in dealing with that than I used to be. So, I'm just going to tackle two things:<br /> <br /> First, you keep mentioning people not being surprised as a defense of Luke being able to do what he can do, as if other people's responses are the deciding factor. If that's the case, then shouldn't no one being surprised at Rey's accomplishments justify them?<br /> <br /> Second, I brought up <b>Marvel's the Avengers</b> because it is an example I'm sure you'd be familiar with of the principle I am trying to illustrate, which is that the faster a thing is moving, the harder it is to redirect. &quot;Momentum = Mass x Velocity&quot; isn't a completely accurate model, but it's close enough for government work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T13:54:51-08:00","id":791781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791760#post791760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was doing my usual point-by-point response when I realized I have completely lost track of what your central argument is, LokiRavenSpeak. You seem to be arguing that nothing Luke accomplished is a big deal, except when it comes to comparing his accomplishments to Rey's, in which case they're a huge deal and she shouldn't even be able to fly a plane like he can despite having been involved in retrofitting the damned thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Again, i never mentioned Reys ability to fly. Nor i have a problem with it.<br /> <br /> 2) My point is that you are overblowing what luke did in episode 4. The death star shot while important wasnt as massive force trick, it was more a nudge or a lucky shot (depends on how you watch that scene if we ignore EU). And you are the one who bring the comparison between luke and rey, not me. Im arguing the luke in episode 4 was far inferior from the Rey in VII in both usage and knowledge of the force with no apparent reason as to why is so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791760#post791760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, you keep mentioning people not being surprised as a defense of Luke being able to do what he can do, as if other people's responses are the deciding factor. If that's the case, then shouldn't no one being surprised at Rey's accomplishments justify them?</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to keep using the fact that we dont see Obi wan deflecting laser and using plenty of force powers (in the original trilogy) as defense as to why Luke is more powerful in IV than Obi Wan. You seem to ignore episode 5 as to how and why the force works as your defense.<br /> <br /> And the noone except the stormtrooper saw rey do what she did. And again that my main problem, that particular use of the force she display. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You could argue that force pull is a fairly instintive use of the force, and kylo`s wound + that &quot;connection&quot; of rey with luke`s lightsaber made her won the battle of will for it. Which is fine, i can buy that. But her pulling the jedi mindtrick from her ass when in similar stressful situation luke barely could get the force pull? Thats where for me the character passed from &quot;choosen one&quot; territory to &quot;mary sue&quot; territory.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791760#post791760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, I brought up <b>Marvel's the Avengers</b> because it is an example I'm sure you'd be familiar with of the principle I am trying to illustrate, which is that the faster a thing is moving, the harder it is to redirect. &quot;Momentum = Mass x Velocity&quot; isn't a completely accurate model, but it's close enough for government work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that in V yoda state that size doesnt matter, and for that matter neither speed if you count Kylo scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791760#post791760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It leaves me with the impression that you're not following a track of logic to a conclusion, but rather defending a conclusion by using whatever tracks of logic you can cobble together, and I'm just less interested in dealing with that than I used to be. So, I'm just going to tackle two things:</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be more you with arguments like<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791760#post791760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider for a moment that in the original trilogy (and we will be ignoring the prequels for how much they contradict their own canon)</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay just the original trilogy. But then when i cite example in the trilogy that contradict your argument you fall back into.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791760#post791760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's not. You can assume Obi-Wan has other powers if you want to, but in the original trilogy, we never see them. Luke surpasses what we see him do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay so now we cant assume anything based on context? So what about this big pile of assuming?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791760#post791760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wedge Antilles warns the audience in the briefing scene that the shot needed to destroy the Death Star is impossible even for a computer. Luke disagrees, but Wedge is right: Someone tries to make the shot with a computer and fails. His torpedoes can't fit through the exhaust port's aperture and detonate on the surface. Only Luke can make that shot, and he does it by exerting telekinetic force and precision unparalleled by anything else ever showed in the movies: He seized control of <i>two</i> missiles traveling at whatever absurd velocity is necessary for a dogfight and made them turn <i>ninety degrees</i> in such tight formation they both go through a hole barely big enough to accommodate them, then level out and fly straight to the Death Star's core. On two hours of training, he can do what a targeting computer can't and he can control the trajectories of two air-to-air missiles. Simultaneously. Darth Vader's recreation of<b>Poltergeist</b> on Cloud City shrivels in shame compared to the mighty Force cock swinging between Luke's legs. The only person who can even compete us the Emperor making lightning from nothing, and even then, all he's doing is converting one kind of energy (the Force) to electricity. Converting energy to electricity is no big thing. People do that shit all the time with machines.</div> </div> </div> </div>You assuming (incorrectly) that size and speed matter even though V contradict that. You are assuming that making 2 misiles twist 90 degree angle is the most impressive force display in the trilogy. You assuming that the misiles have weight (even though they just look like light in the movie). Then you are assuming that RL life rules apply to the setting of sound in space, even though that by RL science those misiles were in a frictionless space.<br /> Sorry but no, im not the one twisting logic to win an argument here.<br /> <br /> So yeah you can assume size and speed matter, that those misiles have weight, that RL logic applies and thats the more powerful display of the force if you want but in the original tril....sorry in IV we never see any of that, if we only take the movie as it we see it not as omniscient viewver as you say here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791760#post791760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You and I as omniscient audience know that, but an observer in the universe would not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then he didnt direct the shot with the force but it look like he just use the force to know when to shoot. You can assume Obi Wan cannot do any telekinesis if you want too. But in the original trilogy we are told that, size and speed dont matter. We see Obi Wan master training luke in telekinesis as is nothing rare in a jedi. We see that rules of RL dont apply to the setting. We see better displays of the force, like stoping a blaster shot with the force and lighting. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 12-23-2015, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T14:13:33-08:00","id":791786,"title":"","content":"Loki's argument is that Rey is a Mary Sue. My earlier argument via theory was that Rey is not a Mary Sue and you will find out later on why that isn't so, the reason she isn't has not yet been presented because this movie is only the first act in a three part arc and it picks up well after the real story has actually started. The beginning of the movie isn't the beginning of this particular story, The story actually begins with Kylo first turning to the Dark Side. It seems like JJ's favorite way to present a story, Alias' presentation is similar to how this arc has been presented, Rey is Star Wars' Sydney, who seemed like a Mary Sue until her background was revealed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 12-23-2015, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T14:21:13-08:00","id":791792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791781#post791781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[stuff]</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, dude, I already told you once I don't have the fire I used to have for going point-by-point in defense of my arguments, especially when I think I made my arguments pretty well. I'm not gonna do this...but I am gonna respond to the &quot;size matters not&quot; bit because this is a theory I've been building for a while and I'm proud of it:<br /> <br /> Size matters not to a Jedi. Size matters very much to the object the Jedi is interacting with. An X-wing is a huge, heavy machine that's only meant to move in certain limited configurations; if you don't distribute its weight evenly and very carefully while lifting it, it will fall apart under its own weight. It would be like how a car should behave when Superman lifts it over his head: Yeah, I'll grant that Superman is strong enough to lift a car over his head, but the car is not structurally sound enough to bear all of its weight on two points as wide as his palms, and it should fall down his body like a hula hoop if it even lasts long enough to get over his head in the first place.<br /> <br /> I believe that is why Yoda had to lift it out of the water so carefully, because more than using the Force to lift something up, he also had to be very aware of the X-wing's stress points and make sure he wasn't picking it up by its wings (which would break them off) or by the body (which would also break the wings off), but rather creating a molded pillow of energy to support every part of the ship according to its structural needs. If he didn't need to be careful with it, if the Force is just magic and can lift cars over Superman's head because fuck it, then Yoda was kind of being a prick by moving it so slowly and show-offishly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T14:41:56-08:00","id":791802,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It's obvious that Rey's innate talent for the force is hereditary, right? I mean, they all but come right out and say it to us, she's got to either be Luke's or Leia's daughter. Right? The reason that no one is surprised that Luke is so skilled in the force and advances so quickly is because he's the son of Anakin Skywalker - the Chosen One who was literally conceived by the force. Likewise, the audience doesn't question the fact that Kylo Ren/Ben Solo is so skilled in the force that he can effortlessly stop a blaster bolt in mid-air and keep it suspended there while he delivers his villanous monologue, to say nothing of his ability to rip thoughts from victims' minds, despite the fact that he has besn shown to be an undertrained, emotionally unstable, petulant child with middling lightsaber skills. He too is descended from Anakin, so it's only natural that his reach would exceed his grasp when it comes to the force, therefore the audience doesn't question the fact that the most pathetic excuse for a Sith seen in the films so far has also displayed some of the most impressive feats of force use (Luke's directing the torpedoes notwithstanding). By the same token, with how heavily Rey's connection to Anakin's bloodline is implied, it should come as no surprise to us as an audience that she too would excel at the force once she realizes she has it.<br /> <br /> Also, unrelated but does anyone else agree that Ben is a significantly better name for Han and Leia's son than Jacen?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Re: &quot;Size matters not&quot;, what Yoda said in response to Luke's complaint that moving rocks around is one thing but the X-wing was completely different was &quot;No. No different. Only different in your mind.&quot; Well, the mind plays a huge role in one's manipulation of the force. What Yoda was trying to teach Luke was that his only limitations were those he placed on himself. It was a &quot;there is no spoon&quot; moment. Yes, obviously picking up a big object with the force takes greater control than picking up a smaller object, but in principle it's the same, a Jedi only needs to allow himself to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-23-2015, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T15:09:57-08:00","id":791809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791802#post791802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It's obvious that Rey's innate talent for the force is hereditary, right? I mean, they all but come right out and say it to us, she's got to either be Luke's or Leia's daughter. Right? The reason that no one is surprised that Luke is so skilled in the force and advances so quickly is because he's the son of Anakin Skywalker - the Chosen One who was literally conceived by the Force. Likewise, the audience doesn't question the fact that Kylo Ren/Ben Solo is so skilled in the force that he can effortlessly stop a blaster bolt in mid-air and keep it suspended there while he delivers his villainous monologue, to say nothing of his ability to rip thoughts from victims' minds, despite the fact that he has been shown to be an undertrained, emotionally unstable, petulant child with middling lightsaber skills. He too is descended from Anakin, so it's only natural that his reach would exceed his grasp when it comes to the Force, therefore the audience doesn't question the fact that the most pathetic excuse for a Sith seen in the films so far has also displayed some of the most impressive feats of Force use (Luke's directing the torpedoes notwithstanding). By the same token, with how heavily Rey's connection to Anakin's bloodline is implied, it should come as no surprise to us as an audience that she too would excel at the Force once she realizes she has it.<br /> <br /> Also, unrelated but does anyone else agree that Ben is a significantly better name for Han and Leia's son than Jacen?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Re: &quot;Size matters not&quot;, what Yoda said in response to Luke's complaint that moving rocks around is one thing but the X-wing was completely different was &quot;No. No different. Only different in your mind.&quot; Well, the mind plays a huge role in one's manipulation of the force. What Yoda was trying to teach Luke was that his only limitations were those he placed on himself. It was a &quot;there is no spoon&quot; moment. Yes, obviously picking up a big object with the force takes greater control than picking up a smaller object, but in principle it's the same, a Jedi only needs to allow himself to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Doesn't the last paragraph contradict the first? If Force ability is passed through the blood, if it's based in a physical system, then that implies the ability to manipulate it has limits based on the strength of the inherited talent; not every child of a blonde-haired, blue-eyed Jedi has blonde hair and blue eyes.<br /> <br /> I'm not actually advocating for that position, though. I'm just asking if you think there's a contradiction. Let me know what you think. I think I take a middleground position, that nature and nurture are both endlessly complex factors and it does no one any practical good to try to reduce things down to a one-or-the-other approach; and I think Luke's trick with the torpedoes was possible at least in part because he didn't comprehend the enormity of how impossible it is to do what he did and therefore had no doubts about it not working. It's interesting to note that once his formal training began, that's when his powers seemed to wane, and one can infer that's because training shows how much he doesn't know and instills self-doubt that interferes with the serenity and clarity a Jedi Knight needs.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T16:28:07-08:00","id":791843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791786#post791786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loki's argument is that Rey is a Mary Sue. My earlier argument via theory was that Rey is not a Mary Sue and you will find out later on why that isn't so, the reason she isn't has not yet been presented because this movie is only the first act in a three part arc and it picks up well after the real story has actually started. The beginning of the movie isn't the beginning of this particular story, The story actually begins with Kylo first turning to the Dark Side. It seems like JJ's favorite way to present a story, Alias' presentation is similar to how this arc has been presented, Rey is Star Wars' Sydney, who seemed like a Mary Sue until her background was revealed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly i think your theory is probably right. Or the worse alternative of<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">That Rey is Luke daughter........i really REALLY hope they dont go there.<br /> <br /> Though either way that has a kinda horrible implication &quot;Im gonna drop this 4 maybe 7 year old in this hostile planet under the care of this guy who is gonna slave her for food rations.....instead of proper home. After all the skywalkers come from a long line of neglecting parents.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791802#post791802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Also, unrelated but does anyone else agree that Ben is a significantly better name for Han and Leia's son than Jacen?</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I dont really, maybe it was better put in the EU but leia and han didnt have that strong connection to Obi Wan. In the movies is Luke who has the strongest connection and even after his death luke still calls him Ben instead of Obi Wan.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T19:13:22-08:00","id":791914,"title":"","content":"There appears to be a lot stretching back through this thread, and I have little interest or patience for it, but one simple thing stands out to me: I find the assertion that we are supposed to see Luke's success at the Death Star as a display of telekinetic manipulation to be a tremendous stretch, barely implied by the film at all. Given that by that point in the film we've seen little show of telekinesis as something that Jedi are actually capable of (Vader has his choking thing, but apart from being distinct to him at that point, it would seem to exist more as an expression of character than a general utility), it would seem to be something both irrelevant and unintuitive as an explanation for his achievement. By that point, the Force has been communicated to Luke in largely spiritual terms, as a subject of perception and intuition and strength over the mind; to make a precise shot without the aid of an inaccurate computer is building upon the scene in which he blocks blaster shots without the aid of his deceitful eyes, not a scene for an unrelated character choking somebody from a distance. Whether or not such an achievement constitutes him being more powerful than Obi-Wan, well... when your experience of the Force so far amounts to matters of certainty, and awareness of a larger world, I would say that being able to step unhesitatingly into death so thoroughly that you completely transcend your crude matter to become a more luminous being is still a few steps beyond making an extremely difficult shot well, and neither are really something that a collection of video game superpowers hold a candle to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T20:03:14-08:00","id":791930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791914#post791914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There appears to be a lot stretching back through this thread....</div> </div> </div> </div>(I *hate* when I'm gone from around here for a week or two -- all the threads I'd actually be interested in always get too blown-up to participate in effectively because too many pages have gone by... #InternetGeekProblems)<br /> <br /> I agree with your post, above, completely. It's very easy to tell the video-gamers from the movie/TTRG-ers in this regard: I've seen this conversation for years and years, and it always comes back to someone suggesting that Luke may have telekinetically guided the proton torpedoes into the vent (which is ridiculous -- it's obvious that he didn't &quot;Forces:4/Correspondence:2&quot; it, but Correspondence:2/Entropy:1 (or Time:2)'d it... he used the Force to sense the opportune moment to fire that would be &quot;correct&quot;... which is proportional to his abilities at that point and more narratively -- as well as metaphysically -- on-point...). I remember that coming up/getting hashed back in '97 when the re-issues were in theaters; the gamer-geek conversations around these parts were *ridiculous*....<br /> <br /> <br /> ...and I am suspecting that, if I go back and look over the past 35 pages, I'll likely see some around here, again, too....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T03:34:13-08:00","id":792084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791930#post791930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I *hate* when I'm gone from around here for a week or two -- all the threads I'd actually be interested in always get too blown-up to participate in effectively because too many pages have gone by... #InternetGeekProblems)<br /> <br /> I agree with your post, above, completely. It's very easy to tell the video-gamers from the movie/TTRG-ers in this regard: I've seen this conversation for years and years, and it always comes back to someone suggesting that Luke may have telekinetically guided the proton torpedoes into the vent (which is ridiculous -- it's obvious that he didn't &quot;Forces:4/Correspondence:2&quot; it, but Correspondence:2/Entropy:1 (or Time:2)'d it... he used the Force to sense the opportune moment to fire that would be &quot;correct&quot;... which is proportional to his abilities at that point and more narratively -- as well as metaphysically -- on-point...). I remember that coming up/getting hashed back in '97 when the re-issues were in theaters; the gamer-geek conversations around these parts were *ridiculous*....<br /> <br /> <br /> ...and I am suspecting that, if I go back and look over the past 35 pages, I'll likely see some around here, again, too....</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, just 1 or 2 pages i was discussing that with JimB. But to be honest its really not clear, even the wikia has the 2 takes on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T07:47:04-08:00","id":792172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791503#post791503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haz theories.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Rey was the youngest/strongest of Luke's trainees before being dropped off on Jakku. Kylo Ren didn't kill all of the other trainees just like Vader didn't actually kill all of the Jedi (like Kanan from Rebels or Ahsoka Tanno). Kylo is the leader of the Knights of Ren because they are other students of Luke's who followed Ben Solo in changing sides. Luke hid Rey to prevent her from being taken along with the other kids Ben converted instead of killing, and Luke probably tampered with her memory before leaving her under the watch of Max Von Sydow, who I believe is the old version of Kanan from Rebels, just like Obi Wan watched over Luke.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you! Pretty much what I was thinking as well...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T11:10:13-08:00","id":792259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=791503#post791503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haz theories.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Rey was the youngest/strongest of Luke's trainees before being dropped off on Jakku. Kylo Ren didn't kill all of the other trainees just like Vader didn't actually kill all of the Jedi (like Kanan from Rebels or Ahsoka Tanno). Kylo is the leader of the Knights of Ren because they are other students of Luke's who followed Ben Solo in changing sides. Luke hid Rey to prevent her from being taken along with the other kids Ben converted instead of killing, and Luke probably tampered with her memory before leaving her under the watch of Max Von Sydow, who I believe is the old version of Kanan from Rebels, just like Obi Wan watched over Luke.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I somehow missed this post. Now that I've seen it, I love this theory! It fits much better than the other popular one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T11:14:07-08:00","id":792261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=792084#post792084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, just 1 or 2 pages i was discussing that with JimB. But to be honest its really not clear, even the wikia has the 2 takes on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think the &quot;force targeting&quot; theory makes *much* more sense in the narrative of the film than the &quot;Telekenesis&quot; theory does. But Telekenesis explains the otherwise inexplicable sharp curve the torpedoes make at the end there. Neither theory is a perfect fit, and to be honest it's not terribly relevant which one you subscribe to. One way or another, Luke used the force to make a shot that would otherwise have been near impossible. Either way it was well beyond his usual force aptitude at and around that point in the story, likely because he didn't realize how significant a feat it was, and therefore didn't mentally limit himself like he did with the X-wing in Empire. The exact details of how he used the force to make the shot are incidental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-24-2015, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T13:42:07-08:00","id":792347,"title":"","cont