0, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Rey was the youngest/strongest of Luke's trainees before being dropped off on Jakku. Kylo Ren didn't kill all of the other trainees just like Vader didn't actually kill all of the Jedi (like Kanan from Rebels or Ahsoka Tanno). Kylo is the leader of the Knights of Ren because they are other students of Luke's who followed Ben Solo in changing sides. Luke hid Rey to prevent her from being taken along with the other kids Ben converted instead of killing, and Luke probably tampered with her memory before leaving her under the watch of Max Von Sydow, who I believe is the old version of Kanan from Rebels, just like Obi Wan watched over Luke.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Hang on. So, if we assume this theory is correct, how do we explain the fact that <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Rey thought Luke Skywalker was a myth?</div></div> </div> </div> Amnesia? Repressed memories?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-24-2015, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T18:46:02-08:00","id":792474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=792359#post792359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine Wedge would have had a hard time hitting those womp rats. To me, Luke's dismissive reaction to the difficulty of the shot based on past experience is a sign that he has always had some level of force sensitivity, he just wasn't aware of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was more about his optimism.<br /> <br /> I can see what you mean, but it sort of takes away from Luke as a character if he's just a pinball for the force and has no real success beyond what it allows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T19:07:33-08:00","id":792482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=792412#post792412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hang on. So, if we assume this theory is correct, how do we explain the fact that <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Rey thought Luke Skywalker was a myth?</div></div> </div> </div> Amnesia? Repressed memories?</div> </div> </div> </div>The going theory is whoever Rey is, someone deliberatly force-erased her memories. Consider, she's eaiting for someone to come get her, but she doesn't seem to know who","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T19:18:17-08:00","id":792487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=792474#post792474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought it was more about his optimism.<br /> <br /> I can see what you mean, but it sort of takes away from Luke as a character if he's just a pinball for the force and has no real success beyond what it allows.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, he's talented outside of the force. I'm just inclined to take Wedge Antilles' expertise on what is or isn't possible with an X-Wing than Luke's, and the force was demonstratably what allowed him to make that shot, which further supports the claim that it's otherwise impossible, even for a computer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T20:23:07-08:00","id":792509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=792474#post792474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought it was more about his optimism.<br /> <br /> I can see what you mean, but it sort of takes away from Luke as a character if he's just a pinball for the force and has no real success beyond what it allows.</div> </div> </div> </div>It helps that using the Force is something you have to <i>train</i> and <i>practice</i> to do well, so even if you're extremely talented like Luke, it's not a given that robs a character of agency. You have to <i>earn</i> it with work.<br /> <br /> I agree with you that's it's better that Luke is an ace at flying all on his own, though.<br /> <br /> Tangent: Holy Hell, womp rats are bigger than <i>2 meters</i>! They're bigger then a <i>full-grown man</i>! No wonder you have to gun these things down with vehicle mounted weapons!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T20:31:14-08:00","id":792512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=792509#post792509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It helps that using the Force is something you have to <i>train</i> and <i>practice</i> to do well, so even if you're extremely talented like Luke, it's not a given that robs a character of agency. You have to <i>earn</i> it with work.<br /> <br /> I agree with you that's it's better that Luke is an ace at flying all on his own, though.<br /> <br /> Tangent: Holy Hell, womp rats are bigger than <i>2 meters</i>! They're bigger then a <i>full-grown man</i>! No wonder you have to gun these things down with vehicle mounted weapons!</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was a little weird too. Really, a computer targeting system has more than a 6 foot margin of error?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T20:43:00-08:00","id":792519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=792512#post792512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that was a little weird too. Really, a computer targeting system has more than a seven-foot margin of error?</div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to three-foot torpedoes traveling at Christ knows what speeds, possibly being expected to turn down a tunnel by computer-guided controls relayed to the torpedoes' propulsion systems (or possibly not; I'm not sure the guys planning the attack understood that the angle the fighters were approaching from was so far from a straight shot)...yeah, I don't doubt that six feet is a tiny margin of error. Certainly Wedge thought so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T02:13:27-08:00","id":792678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=792482#post792482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The going theory is whoever Rey is, someone deliberatly force-erased her memories. Consider, she's eaiting for someone to come get her, but she doesn't seem to know who</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's what I said, the last line in my theory says who I think did what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T03:38:48-08:00","id":792692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=792519#post792519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to three-foot torpedoes traveling at Christ knows what speeds, possibly being expected to turn down a tunnel by computer-guided controls relayed to the torpedoes' propulsion systems (or possibly not; I'm not sure the guys planning the attack understood that the angle the fighters were approaching from was so far from a straight shot)...yeah, I don't doubt that six feet is a tiny margin of error. Certainly Wedge thought so.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what i understood the tricky part of the shoot is that approaching the vent vertically wasnt an option because it was too well defended while the corridor horizontally was less so. I dont remember where i read that though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T18:09:05-08:00","id":792890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=792692#post792692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember where I read that, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you had to read it. I don't remember his exact words, but I'm pretty sure General McBeardo explicitly said the exhaust port was too well-guarded for a frontal assault, so they'd have to skim along that trench.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T02:00:21-08:00","id":793482,"title":"","content":"Moar theory.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So in the prequel trilogy when Palpatine is telling Anakin about Darth Plagueis he mentions a few things. Plagueis is such a master of the Dark Side that he can both overcome death physically (as opposed to spiritually like the Jedi later do) and he can direct midichlorians to create new life. That leads us to the inferred conclusion that Anakin's immaculate conception was really engineered by Plagueis. He then lets Sidious &quot;kill&quot; him and take his place so he can slip into the background with no one being aware he is still around, not even his former apprentice. Anakin falls, as he was expected to, since he was supposed to bring balance and there were so many Jedi his fall was a foregone conclusion. Now that seems like a short term plan for someone called Plagueis the Wise. Anakin meets a girl, has kids who are both strong in the Force, and one is eventually trained to the point he supposedly surpasses his father (arguably).<br /> <br /> Now we have Luke, with a 20 year gap between the time of RotJ and TFA teaching and training a new group of kids, but we don't know about any relationships that Luke may have had or if he had any kids. There are enough theories out there that Rey is his daughter that are plausible that I'm going with that assumption, and also assuming part of the reason Luke failed was because he broke the Jedi rule of not falling in love, he followed in his fathers footsteps and fell in love, having a family no one was supposed to know about. It would help explain him hiding Rey on a remote desert planet like he was raised on, as well as explaining his self imposed exile. It's really a hypothesis if you want to be technical about it since I rely on a large untested assumption. <br /> <br /> And who has been manipulating the Skywalkers from the beginning, Plagueis that's who. Snoke is most likely Plagueis (and since the First Order has been modeled on the Nazis who's to say Snoke isn't engaging in a eugenics project of his own?) He certainly looks like someone whose head was struck by a lightsaber. He also seems to be showing patience for Kylo Ren even though Kylo seemingly failed him multiple times in the movie, the hallmark of someone with a long term plan. The clues seem to be there to support this theory, but who has been countering Plagueis moves, keeping the Skywalkers on the Light path in opposition to Plagueis' design? Could Luke have actually been introduced to the mother of his child by an agent of the Light Side, in order for her to give birth to a female Light Side counter to Plagueis' male project? I'd keep an eye on Maz Kanata over the next two movies. Over a thousand years old, gains possession of Anakin/Luke's blue saber just so Rey can find it, guides Rey through her Force vision, female counterpart to Snoke's male, yeah she's a major player IMO. </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T20:20:44-08:00","id":793918,"title":"","content":"I would find it to be kind of weird that Rey's insistence that her family is going to come back for her was anything more elaborate than denial, with Jakku as a focal point of dependence, but I suppose considering the director something with an unnecessary degree of elaboration is not off the table... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it sort of takes away from Luke as a character if he's just a pinball for the force and has no real success beyond what it allows.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;Do you mean it controls your actions?&quot; &quot;Partly, but it also obeys your commands.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T01:38:59-08:00","id":794038,"title":"","content":"Yeah, count me in the Rey is not a Mary Sue camp.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Appart from all that's been said here, there are strong hints that Rey has been exposed to force training before the event of the movie.<br /> 1) When Maz tries to give her Luke's saber, her answer looks a darn lot like &quot;not again&quot;, which hints that she's been exposed to that sort of stuff before.<br /> 2) The turning point in the fight against Kylo is when he says he ought to train her : her reaction to that is freezing for a moment, and then going on the offensive for the first time in the fight ; only stopping, calming down and starting to flee once more when her and Kylo are separated by the gulf.<br /> <br /> I take out three things from that : she has an experience with the force, and it's not a good one. She was probably trained before, and when reminded of it, react with violence. And last but not least, once she starts out on the path of violence, she takes a moment to go back to what was her primary objective (fleeing) instead of trying to kill kylo.<br /> <br /> My theory is that Rey was trained. By a dark side user. I don't know if she remembers it or not, but it does explain both those things and the fact that once she gets over what's apparently holding her back, she quickly shows great talents in the force. Mayyyybe she's a Solo or a Skywalker, but I kinda hope not. I'd like us to get at least some fresh jedi blood. </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T11:42:02-08:00","id":794292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=794038#post794038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, count me in the Rey is not a Mary Sue camp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto. Rey rocks, Force Awakens rocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T12:41:42-08:00","id":794329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=794038#post794038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, count me in the Rey is not a Mary Sue camp.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Apart from all that's been said here, there are strong hints that Rey has been exposed to force training before the event of the movie.<br /> 1) When Maz tries to give her Luke's saber, her answer looks a darn lot like &quot;not again&quot;, which hints that she's been exposed to that sort of stuff before.<br /> 2) The turning point in the fight against Kylo is when he says he ought to train her : her reaction to that is freezing for a moment, and then going on the offensive for the first time in the fight ; only stopping, calming down and starting to flee once more when her and Kylo are separated by the gulf.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I would add that her escape from the interrogation chamber struck me as someone struggling with a technique that she had tried and failed to use in the past, pointing to incomplete training.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T14:57:32-08:00","id":794404,"title":"","content":"And I would like to add somethi g demo strated by Finn fighting Ren before Rey. By having him go firstn it showed just what an amateur with a lightsaber could do (not much). Finn weilded it likemost fans use their toy lightsabersn lots of wild swings and reckless thrusts.Then, Rey rook up the saber and showed actual technique. She was even able to use the Force to focus her attacks. Thus, it allowed the writers to give another subtle hint that Rey had some training.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T05:05:09-08:00","id":794765,"title":"","content":"I am unconcerned with the idea of Rey being a Mary Sue, but I see mild credibility in it. Not for the Force; I see its portrayal in the film as a welcome return to focusing more on it as a mystical and intuitive thing. More in the portrayal of how quickly she apparently takes to operation of an unfamiliar complex machine. I don't actually have a problem with her and the Millenium Falcon, but I would still honestly view it as borderline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T18:00:05-08:00","id":795252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=793482#post793482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moar theory.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So in the prequel trilogy when Palpatine is telling Anakin about Darth Plagueis he mentions a few things. Plagueis is such a master of the Dark Side that he can both overcome death physically (as opposed to spiritually like the Jedi later do) and he can direct midichlorians to create new life. That leads us to the inferred conclusion that Anakin's immaculate conception was really engineered by Plagueis. He then lets Sidious &quot;kill&quot; him and take his place so he can slip into the background with no one being aware he is still around, not even his former apprentice. Anakin falls, as he was expected to, since he was supposed to bring balance and there were so many Jedi his fall was a foregone conclusion. Now that seems like a short term plan for someone called Plagueis the Wise. Anakin meets a girl, has kids who are both strong in the Force, and one is eventually trained to the point he supposedly surpasses his father (arguably).<br /> <br /> Now we have Luke, with a 20 year gap between the time of RotJ and TFA teaching and training a new group of kids, but we don't know about any relationships that Luke may have had or if he had any kids. There are enough theories out there that Rey is his daughter that are plausible that I'm going with that assumption, and also assuming part of the reason Luke failed was because he broke the Jedi rule of not falling in love, he followed in his fathers footsteps and fell in love, having a family no one was supposed to know about. It would help explain him hiding Rey on a remote desert planet like he was raised on, as well as explaining his self imposed exile. It's really a hypothesis if you want to be technical about it since I rely on a large untested assumption.<br /> <br /> And who has been manipulating the Skywalkers from the beginning, Plagueis that's who. Snoke is most likely Plagueis (and since the First Order has been modeled on the Nazis who's to say Snoke isn't engaging in a eugenics project of his own?) He certainly looks like someone whose head was struck by a lightsaber. He also seems to be showing patience for Kylo Ren even though Kylo seemingly failed him multiple times in the movie, the hallmark of someone with a long term plan. The clues seem to be there to support this theory, but who has been countering Plagueis moves, keeping the Skywalkers on the Light path in opposition to Plagueis' design? Could Luke have actually been introduced to the mother of his child by an agent of the Light Side, in order for her to give birth to a female Light Side counter to Plagueis' male project? I'd keep an eye on Maz Kanata over the next two movies. Over a thousand years old, gains possession of Anakin/Luke's blue saber just so Rey can find it, guides Rey through her Force vision, female counterpart to Snoke's male, yeah she's a major player IMO. </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Could be..... I like it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T22:40:50-08:00","id":795403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=794765#post794765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am unconcerned with the idea of Rey being a Mary Sue, but I see mild credibility in it. Not for the Force; I see its portrayal in the film as a welcome return to focusing more on it as a mystical and intuitive thing. More in the portrayal of how quickly she apparently takes to operation of an unfamiliar complex machine. I don't actually have a problem with her and the Millenium Falcon, but I would still honestly view it as borderline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. I think by the time she pilots it they've sufficiently established her affinity for complex machinery. Besides, while the Falcon may be heavily modified, at the end of the day it's still a Corellian YT-1300f. The fact that she knew the modifications Unkar Plutt had made to it indicates that she either spoke with him about how he was modifying it, or she was familiar enough with the model to recognize how this one was different from the standard model, and Plutt doesn't strike me as the type to make casual conversation about his muscle ship restoration project, at least not with Rey. I don't see anyone complaining about Poe's intimate knowledge of the weapons system of a tie fighter, and the only justification he gives for it is &quot;I can fly anything.&quot; I'd say Rey's piloting cred is significantly better established than his.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T13:33:14-08:00","id":796998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlequin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">while the Falcon may be heavily modified, at the end of the day it's still a Corellian YT-1300f.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is the... Kalishnikov of star ships? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlequin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that she knew the modifications Unkar Plutt had made to it indicates that she either spoke with him about how he was modifying it, or she was familiar enough with the model to recognize how this one was different from the standard model, and Plutt doesn't strike me as the type to make casual conversation about his muscle ship restoration project, at least not with Rey.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's kind of part and parcel with the piloting predicament. Does it make sense for her to have so much understanding of how the thing works? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlequin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Rey's piloting cred is significantly better established than his.</div> </div> </div> </div> The guy who did it for a living and presumably had years of experience with it, versus the person who had spent most of her life scavenging and cleaning scrap metal for food?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T14:35:37-08:00","id":797022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=796998#post796998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is the... Kalishnikov of star ships?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno what Kalishnikov is, but seems to be pretty universally recognized as a junker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=796998#post796998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's kind of part and parcel with the piloting predicament. Does it make sense for her to have so much understanding of how the thing works?</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly does she have to do for it to make sense that she has this knowledge? Poe literally just informs us that he has it and we accept it because he's a resistance pilot. Rey's background is kept intentionally vague, so all we have to work from is her actions throughout the course of the film. She demonstrates her technical and piloting skills significantly better than Poe ever does, and yet we question if she should be able to? What ever happened to &quot;show, don't tell&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=796998#post796998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The guy who did it for a living and presumably had years of experience with it, versus the person who had spent most of her life scavenging and cleaning scrap metal for food?</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't actually know either of those things are facts. Poe apparently is a pilot for the resistance, but beyond that we don't know his profession, or anything about his background besides &quot;I can fly anything&quot;. How did he acquire this unlimited knowledge of ships and how to operate them? That's never explained. Likewise, we don't know that Rey spent most of her life scavenging and cleaning scrap metal for food. We know that's what she was doing at the point where we were brought into this extremely <i>en media res</i> story, and we know that she was left on Jaku as a fairly young girl. Everything before being left there and everything between being left there and the first time we see her on the film is still unknown. She clearly demonstrates skill with technology, linguistics, and the force. The natural conclusion to draw from this, in my opinion, is that there's more to her backstory that we don't know yet. At the minimum we can safely assume that she does a lot of tinkering with complex machinery in her free time.<br /> <br /> If you don't like the comparison to Poe, how about a more direct analogue. Anakin also lived on a shithole desert planet, working as slave for a pawn shop owner. He &quot;can fix anything&quot; and built a pod racer (which we are told is &quot;the fastest ever&quot;), and a droid with knowledge of over 6 million languages. Out of scraps. When he was nine. Oh, and he had more latent force potential than Yoda. I don't remember anyone calling him a Gary Stu. And already we've seen more justification for Rey's talents than we ever did for Anakin's, nevermind the fact that there are <i>heavy</i> implications that there are big secrets about her past that haven't been revealed yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-30-2015, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T16:33:45-08:00","id":797071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=796998#post796998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Which is the... Kalishnikov of star ships?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see here... *Opens RPG book*<br /> <br /> Hm. Been in circulation for over half a century? Check. Extraordinarily rugged as long as it's well-maintained? Check. Essentially ubiquitous as <i>the</i> light freighter? Check.<br /> <br /> So yeah, pretty much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T17:44:11-08:00","id":797094,"title":"","content":"Ok, getting officially sick of the internet fandom. All I see are people nitpicking minor complaints to declare the movie bad, as well as the now almost universal declaration of Rey as a mary sue (which is just shorthand for &quot;character I don't like didn't have to work as hard as I wanted&quot;)<br /> <br /> Seriously, why is it wrong to enjoy Star Wars anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T17:47:27-08:00","id":797096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=796998#post796998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it make sense for her to have so much understanding of how the thing works?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there is a line with han in which they discuss a new modification the &quot;Boss&quot; of rey (whatshisface) did to the ship and how she discussed with him how installing said modification was a bad idea for that ship. Which implies that she had worked on the ship before, and force users are naturally gifted pilots per episode 1.<br /> <br /> Though, im curious how nobody discuss the whole<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">After han death Leia completely ignores chewie and hugs rey when both characters didnt share a single scene before that point. When i rewatch it there wasnt even a sideglance between chewie and leia. I almost expected chewie to extend his arms for a hug and scream &quot;PSYCHE!!!&quot; and leave Leia hanging.<br /> <br /> It baffles me how out of character that scene was. Kinda make me think of this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k8jTs92QQs4\" data-code=\"k8jTs92QQs4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/k8jTs92QQs4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797094#post797094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> as well as the now almost universal declaration of Rey as a mary sue (which is just shorthand for &quot;character I don't like didn't have to work as hard as I wanted&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if this thread is any indication not that many people think that she is a mary sue, also while i believe she is a mary sue. That doesnt mean i hate the character itself. She is fine, a massive improvement from anakin thats for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 12-30-2015, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T17:54:49-08:00","id":797099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797094#post797094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, getting officially sick of the internet fandom. All I see are people nitpicking minor complaints to declare the movie bad, as well as the now almost universal declaration of Rey as a mary sue (which is just shorthand for &amp;quot;character I don't like didn't have to work as hard as I wanted&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously, why is it wrong to enjoy Star Wars anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much enjoyed the movie. Granted, it wasn't the revolutionary step forward in special effects that the original trilogy was, but I wasn't expecting it to be. It did what it needed to do to assure me the series is returning to form in terms of writing, directing, and use of practical effects where appropriate. It was a little heavy-handed on the nostalgia but I don't blame them since they were trying to win back a fandom that had been burned by poorly handled sequels before. The &quot;Rey is a Mary Sue&quot; nonsense is something I've come to expect with every strong female lead. Nothing new there. Overall it was a solid film, not a masterpiece, but a solid film. Looking forward to seeing where they take it from here.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I think some folks are just determined not to like any Star Wars movies besides the original cuts of 4, 5, and 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T17:58:26-08:00","id":797100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797096#post797096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, im curious how nobody discuss the whole<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">After han death Leia completely ignores chewie and hugs rey when both characters didnt share a single scene before that point. When i rewatch it there wasnt even a sideglance between chewie and leia. I almost expected chewie to extend his arms for a hug and scream &amp;quot;PSYCHE!!!&amp;quot; and leave Leia hanging.<br /> <br /> It baffles me how out of character that scene was. Kinda make me think of this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k8jTs92QQs4\" data-code=\"k8jTs92QQs4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/k8jTs92QQs4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I never really got the impression that Lea and Chewey were all that close. Or that Chewey was the hugging type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T18:00:38-08:00","id":797103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797100#post797100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never really got the impression that Lea and Chewey were all that close. Or that Chewey was the hugging type.</div> </div> </div> </div>They huged when they meet with han but when they come back from destroying death star 3 they ignore each other, its kinda funny. Even if they werent that close, they sure as hell were more close than Leia and Rey.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797099#post797099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Rey is a Mary Sue&quot; nonsense is something I've come to expect with every strong female lead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because every female character should automatically be exempt from criticism.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> On the whole Luke accomplishments in IV vs Reys accomplishments.<br /> <br /> Lets assume for the sake or argument that the whole shoot on the death star thing is as big as force feat as JimB blows it up to be. Under that assumption the more i think about it maybe its a narrative thing.<br /> <br /> The blowing of the death star was the &quot;Final shot&quot;, the last ditch effort of the rebels. The &quot;last&quot; action scene of the action movie if you will. I think its somehow ignored as a OP moment because of that.<br /> <br /> Same with Rey and her duel with Kylo and her winning the constest of will. I never felt that was her being OP, it was the final action scene between the lead and the bad guy. I guess as audience there is more leeway one gives to that part of a movie than other. Maybe it was maybe it wasnt but i never felt it was.<br /> <br /> The mind trick scene though? That one did feel that way, it wasnt a climax of any sort. Just a little fake &quot;time pressure&quot; scene that was resolve with her pulling a power.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 12-30-2015, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T18:23:56-08:00","id":797118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797103#post797103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, because every female character should automatically be exempt from criticism.</div> </div> </div> </div> Please, let's not get dramatic, Rey has been subjected to a lot of BS analysis. God forbid the action hero not have a penis.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T18:41:40-08:00","id":797126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797118#post797118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Please, let's not get dramatic</b></u>, Rey has been subjected to a lot of BS analysis. <b><u>God forbid the action hero not have a penis.</u></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Do what i say not what i do.<br /> <br /> Yes the character has been subjected to a lot of BS analysis but also being given a free pass for being a female hero too from many others. Or better put anyone not thinking she is great has being labelled a &quot;woman hater man animal&quot;.<br /> <br /> I heard the argument &quot;batman is given a free pass but Rey doesnt get it because she is a woman&quot;. I think is BS, batman is not given a free pass universally by everyone for how much of a mary sue he is, neither should her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 12-30-2015, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T18:54:45-08:00","id":797131,"title":"","content":"Let's not turn this into an argument about feminism, please. Rey is not beyond criticism by any means, nor is any female character. Or any male character. But a significant amount of the criticism I've seen of Rey is uwarranted, and a significant amount can also be said of many other characters in the series and has not been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T19:44:39-08:00","id":797150,"title":"","content":"Thenone quote out there on the net that reallystuck out for me basically went &quot;figures someone from Tumblr would like the mary sue&quot;.<br /> <br /> I still say all the stuff she does is meant to be clues that this girl at some point began training, even if she doesnt remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T20:42:56-08:00","id":797168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797126#post797126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do what i say not what i do.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I think you missed the joke. I'll try to be more obvious next time.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T22:20:17-08:00","id":797196,"title":"","content":"Hmm...looking at the &quot;common Mary Sue traits&quot; page on TV Tropes, if I am particularly harsh about it Rey might qualify. But then so would Luke, Anakin, Revan, the Exile, and many of the other Star Wars protagonists of various novels, games and comics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T01:47:44-08:00","id":797236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797168#post797168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you missed the joke. I'll try to be more obvious next time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah sorry about that, my bad there. the tone deaf nature of writting forum <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797196#post797196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...looking at the &quot;common Mary Sue traits&quot; page on TV Tropes, if I am particularly harsh about it Rey might qualify. But then so would Luke, Anakin, Revan, the Exile, and many of the other Star Wars protagonists of various novels, games and comics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, videogames protagonist (revan/Exile) are mary sues. For the player to explore the full world it kinda necesitates that. Like commander Sheppard in Mass effect. Also to a degree Cade Skywalker too, though it was supposse to be a point in the story that it was cut short sadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 12-31-2015, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T10:21:47-08:00","id":797409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlequin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly does she have to do for it to make sense that she has this knowledge</div> </div> </div> </div> Exist in a context in which it would intuitively be connected. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlequin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poe literally just informs us that he has it and we accept it because he's a resistance pilot.</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually find the line &quot;I can fly anything&quot; to be less significant as an excuse for being able to fly the TIE, and more as an introduction to the character's cocksure attitude and giving a nice flow of quippy dialogue between him and Finn. Still, the fact that he's introduced into the film piloting a ship is enough to lend credibility to the idea that he has experience piloting ships. It's not just that Rey pilots the thing, it's that it's the very first time she's so much as hinted to be abe to, the context does not imply experience, and she has such an extreme familiarity with it right down to being able to figure out how to jury-rig it to produce traps. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlequin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, we don't know that Rey spent most of her life scavenging and cleaning scrap metal for food. We know that's what she was doing at the point where we were brought into this extremely en media res story, and we know that she was left on Jaku as a fairly young girl. Everything before being left there and everything between being left there and the first time we see her on the film is still unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div> This makes me think of the fallacy of complexity; the problems with the idea of assuming that a premise is reasonable so much as a highly complex (and often unspoken) basis is present. I, personally, do not see the implication of an ultra-convoluted background for the character based on being given Dark Side training, or having been a former pilot, or anything else, and I think the abundance of people assuming there is such is, well... it can mostly be laid at the feet of J.J. Abrams being so much as associated with the project, but I'd also see it as pointing to a few holes in the storytelling. Personally, I don't care for it; I saw what unnecessary complication and bloated backstory did to a fluffy action-adventure yarn in Pirates of the Caribbean, and have no desire to see it repeated here. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlequin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">She clearly demonstrates skill with technology, linguistics, and the force.</div> </div> </div> </div> That she can understand Wookiee is another aspect that feels a bit borderline to me, another thing that feels incongruous with her context and where having to assume an unhinted at convoluted background is more of an evasion then an explanation. I mean, if it was what the film was going for, I feel as though having her vision of her own past should not have been her being dropped off as an infant in the exact place and scenario in which we start with her. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlequin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anakin also lived on a shithole desert planet, working as slave for a pawn shop owner. He &quot;can fix anything&quot; and built a pod racer (which we are told is &quot;the fastest ever&quot;), and a droid with knowledge of over 6 million languages. Out of scraps. When he was nine. Oh, and he had more latent force potential than Yoda. I don't remember anyone calling him a Gary Stu.</div> </div> </div> </div> Perhaps not the specific term, but I'm reasonably sure that a lot of people found the whole 9-year old expert pilot thing to be incredibly stupid (all of it, really, that's just the one that stands out the most to me given that it's a climactic achievement). I couldn't say personally, though, I have no idea what the Internet was like in the late 90s, I didn't personally get on it until 2003 (and didn't become involved in online discussions until years afterwards). <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlequin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Rey is a Mary Sue&quot; nonsense is something I've come to expect with every strong female lead.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh absolutely; there's a lot of vile shit mixed in there. I actually like the character of Rey; I don't even have an actual issue with her capacity to fly the Falcon and to talk about it with enough expertise to impress Han, especially when it's all in service to creating a dynamic action-adventure yarn. I just note some incongruities that I'd like to analyse and deconstruct; it's why I keep using the term &quot;borderline&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T10:30:17-08:00","id":797412,"title":"","content":"Oh shoot, I forgot something... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlequin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What ever happened to &quot;show, don't tell&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay, so the thing about 'show, don't tell' is that it undermines the credibility of a character/scenario and is just lazy writing besides when there's something talking at length about some quality that never actually gets depicted (note; we see Poe come back for piloting on Swamp Bar planet, which is the film's moment to show us how good he is, and I at least think it's effective). It stands out especially when a writer doesn't know how to depict the talent, leaving it as a hole in the story, or something that gets shown and bungles it. So yeah, you've got to depict characters as exhibiting the traits we're supposed to see them as having, whether or not they're talked about. That does not mean that they can be depicted as doing basically anything without any reference to context. 'Show don't tell' does not automatically mean that showing a thing is superior storytelling, especially if the thing doesn't make sense; when people see a thing that doesn't match the surroundings, it increases a sense of artificiality. On top of that, appealing to an unseen or mentioned background is kind of the opposite of showing, and implicitly acknowledges that the film has not depicted a thing that is necessary to preserving its own credibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T11:18:50-08:00","id":797433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797409#post797409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes me think of the fallacy of complexity; the problems with the idea of assuming that a premise is reasonable so much as a highly complex (and often unspoken) basis is present. I, personally, do not see the implication of an ultra-convoluted background for the character based on being given Dark Side training, or having been a former pilot, or anything else, and I think the abundance of people assuming there is such is, well... it can mostly be laid at the feet of J.J. Abrams being so much as associated with the project, but I'd also see it as pointing to a few holes in the storytelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this come way before J.J Abrams, for someone who has nothing but contempt for the EU, Lucas made Episode 2 completely dependent of the EU.<br /> <br /> As its stand right now, now that EU is null, the movie alone is just a mess of poorly explained characters and surroundings. Until wookiepedia, i never knew who the hell was dooku and why he was relevant pre sith, what the deal with Sifo-Dyas, why the republic was in chaos and how. And while Episode 1 had similar problems, episode 2 really feel like compelling story.....that we just watch part 3 of a completely different trilogy that we never saw.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797409#post797409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On top of that, appealing to an unseen or mentioned background is kind of the opposite of showing, and implicitly acknowledges that the film has not depicted a thing that is necessary to preserving its own credibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this, instead of wasting those shoot of rey remembering stuff we already know (being left on the planet) we could use those flashback to show her hardships on the planet or better stablish her abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 12-31-2015, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T11:49:39-08:00","id":797443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797433#post797433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with this, instead of wasting those shoot of rey remembering stuff we already know (being left on the planet) we could use those flashback to show her hardships on the planet or better stablish her abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I mean, the beginning of Rey's scenes already gave us a glimpse at her hardships (hard, dangerous scavenging just to get scraps of food, dealing with other scavengers competing for the <i>same stuff</i>, presumably).<br /> <br /> By the way, Rey's quick adjustment to Force powers just struck me as the practiced talent of somebody who's used to having to adapt quickly for survival who <i>also</i> grew up hearing the &quot;legends&quot; about what Jedi could do. After rebuffing a force assault by Kylo Ren, she's aware that she <i>has</i> the power, and then starts trying out the things she's heard.<br /> <br /> Like, Rey's quick, self-taught Force acumen was totally fine to me. I'm also fine with her knowing how to pilot complex machines: it's clear that she tinkers, and while mechanical skill doesn't equate to piloting skills, she indicates to Finn that she's a pilot. It's clear that even given her skill at piloting, she's not going to try to leave Jakku given her crippling abandonment issues.<br /> <br /> Regarding her background, I <i>really</i> hope that she's not related to <i>anybody</i>. Just a random force-sensitive without any major connection to any of the other big players.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T12:47:23-08:00","id":797465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797409#post797409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exist in a context in which it would intuitively be connected.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, can you give an example of what that might look like? What would have had to happen differently in the film to adequately contextualize her abilities for you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797409#post797409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually find the line &quot;I can fly anything&quot; to be less significant as an excuse for being able to fly the TIE, and more as an introduction to the character's cocksure attitude and giving a nice flow of quippy dialogue between him and Finn. Still, the fact that he's introduced into the film piloting a ship is enough to lend credibility to the idea that he has experience piloting ships. It's not just that Rey pilots the thing, it's that it's the very first time she's so much as hinted to be abe to, the context does not imply experience, and she has such an extreme familiarity with it right down to being able to figure out how to jury-rig it to produce traps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I was being a bit hyperbolic. I too took the &quot;I can fly anything&quot; line as indicative of Poe's attitude more than his actual talent as a pilot. What I'm trying to get at is that Poe is able to rattle off instructions for operating a TIE fighter's weapon system as though by rote, and pilot a TIE fighter with ease. The context that justifies this seems to me to be &quot;he's a Resistance pilot.&quot; Keeping in mind that outside of this one instance, Resistance pilots are only ever seen piloting X-wings, why is it that this is considered sufficient context to justify piloting a TIE, while Rey's demonstrated familiarity with machinery and implied experience working on or at least discussing the modifications to the Falcon itself not considered sufficient context to justify her ability to pilot that same ship? Why is her knowledge of engineering considered to compound her Mary Sueness, but the same is not said of Poe's exceptional piloting skills? It looks to me like his skills are cited as their own justification, while Rey's skills are cited as the reason she shouldn't have them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797409#post797409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes me think of the fallacy of complexity; the problems with the idea of assuming that a premise is reasonable so much as a highly complex (and often unspoken) basis is present. I, personally, do not see the implication of an ultra-convoluted background for the character based on being given Dark Side training, or having been a former pilot, or anything else, and I think the abundance of people assuming there is such is, well... it can mostly be laid at the feet of J.J. Abrams being so much as associated with the project, but I'd also see it as pointing to a few holes in the storytelling. Personally, I don't care for it; I saw what unnecessary complication and bloated backstory did to a fluffy action-adventure yarn in Pirates of the Caribbean, and have no desire to see it repeated here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would she need to have a complex backstory to justify the fact that she can fly a YT-1300f? Maybe she just spends her free time working on ships and flying them around Jaku? Luke did the same on Tattooine, though we never saw him do it either. It wasn't dramatically relevant to show it. All he had to do was say &quot;I'm not a bad pilot myself&quot; and no one complained that he could fly an X-wing despite never being shown to have flown one before. But when Rey demonstrates familiarity with the modifications &quot;one half portion&quot; guy had made to the Falcon, that's not seen as contextualizing her ability to pilot it? Why?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797409#post797409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That she can understand Wookiee is another aspect that feels a bit borderline to me, another thing that feels incongruous with her context and where having to assume an unhinted at convoluted background is more of an evasion then an explanation. I mean, if it was what the film was going for, I feel as though having her vision of her own past should not have been her being dropped off as an infant in the exact place and scenario in which we start with her.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest, her understanding of Wookee and what ever language BB8 speaks did strike me as a bit out of left field. But I'd rather give the writers the benefit of the doubt and assume there's a reason for it that will be made clear in the later films. And again, it doesn't have to be complex. It could be as simple as &quot;it was a manifestation of her latent force sensitivity&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797409#post797409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps not the specific term, but I'm reasonably sure that a lot of people found the whole 9-year old expert pilot thing to be incredibly stupid (all of it, really, that's just the one that stands out the most to me given that it's a climactic achievement). I couldn't say personally, though, I have no idea what the Internet was like in the late 90s, I didn't personally get on it until 2003 (and didn't become involved in online discussions until years afterwards).</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, I don't know what the adult fandom thought of Anakin's backstory at the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797409#post797409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh absolutely; there's a lot of vile shit mixed in there. I actually like the character of Rey; I don't even have an actual issue with her capacity to fly the Falcon and to talk about it with enough expertise to impress Han, especially when it's all in service to creating a dynamic action-adventure yarn. I just note some incongruities that I'd like to analyse and deconstruct; it's why I keep using the term &quot;borderline&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's reasonable. I think it's mostly the &quot;Mary Sue&quot; label that I object to, more than the critique of her writing. The term seems to be shorthand for &quot;female character that I don't like and think should have had to work harder for what she had&quot; and to be much more commonly applied than the equivalent term for male characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-31-2015, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T13:26:18-08:00","id":797492,"title":"","content":"I just want to point something out. Rey is at least somewhat familiar with the Falcon, as indicated by the line &quot;that's a hunk of garbage&quot; when Finn asks &quot;why not take that ship?&quot; when running from the FO. Again, people miss or ignore one line of dialogue and then miss a lot of context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T15:08:17-08:00","id":797524,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile, I'm just going to sit back and enjoy a Star Wars movie that's a space fantasy rooted in character drama rather than technical accuracy. These are action movie heroes; they don't need deep justifications for what they can do.<br /> <br /> That said, I fully expect to get more details on Rey's backstory in the next film. And I will not be one bit surprised if she turns out to be a Skywalker. Not just the &quot;strong in the Force&quot; thing, but the technical acumen is a very Skywalkery characteristic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T15:40:12-08:00","id":797536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797465#post797465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. The term seems to be shorthand for &amp;quot;female character that I don't like and think should have had to work harder for what she had&amp;quot; and to be much more commonly applied than the equivalent term for male characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always heard the term applied as unisex. Remember first reading the term on discussions about sasuke from naruto back when i liked anime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T16:02:12-08:00","id":797542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797536#post797536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always heard the term applied as unisex. Remember first reading the term on discussions about sasuke from naruto back when i liked anime.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is sometimes used for male characters, yeah. The term actually originally referred to a very specific archetype of fan fiction OC, which happened to be female in the iconic example but could technically be any gender. It has evolved into a much more general term for characters who are &quot;too perfect&quot; or sometimes for characters that serve as stand-ins for the author (where the original meaning was both). Some folks use the term for characters of all genders, while other people use Gary Stu or Marty Stu (depending on their preference between rhyming and alliteration) for male characters. Either way, the &quot;this character's positive traits are undeserved&quot; complaint, what ever name is used for it, seems to me to be made about female leads more often than male leads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T16:15:49-08:00","id":797547,"title":"","content":"So, if Rey's character development in the future reasonably explains how she did everything, will the detractors start liking this movie? Or will it only drive them into an even greater frothing rage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T17:12:30-08:00","id":797558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797547#post797547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if Rey's character development in the future reasonably explains how she did everything, will the detractors start liking this movie? Or will it only drive them into an even greater frothing rage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who cares? Let haters hate if it makes them feel better about their lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T19:18:57-08:00","id":797596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlequin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, can you give an example of what that might look like? What would have had to happen differently in the film to adequately contextualize her abilities for you?</div> </div> </div> </div> Honestly? Something more like what Anakin was doing in Episode I; mechanic employed in a space port. Rather than just go around cutting up parts and bringing them to a dealer, somebody in something like indentured servitude to put the things back together, fix them up to be sold. Have the idea that between living in the place for years and what she's been employed as, she's had a lot of conversations with pilots, and picked up a lot of languages. Hell, I think running through that field of starships and having an expert opinion on them could work better if there was a prior establishment of her having basically built all of them. And it's all a lot more sensible than Anakin because she's an adult who's built up this stuff over years rather than a child (also, you don't introduce her with a ridiculous &quot;are you an angel&quot; line). Is it rehashing a bit? Sure, but the whole movie did that, and did it well, and I think between what I'm saying and what I'm picturing, it would still wind up being significantly different. I think if they change about... three scenes in the first act, you could get all of that in. I think I could even specify them, if anybody cares. To me, that would constitute showing, rather than telling, a talent set before it operates for the plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T08:07:22-08:00","id":797820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=797596#post797596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Honestly? Something more like what Anakin was doing in Episode I; mechanic employed in a space port. Rather than just go around cutting up parts and bringing them to a dealer, somebody in something like indentured servitude to put the things back together, fix them up to be sold. Have the idea that between living in the place for years and what she's been employed as, she's had a lot of conversations with pilots, and picked up a lot of languages. Hell, I think running through that field of starships and having an expert opinion on them could work better if there was a prior establishment of her having basically built all of them. And it's all a lot more sensible than Anakin because she's an adult who's built up this stuff over years rather than a child (also, you don't introduce her with a ridiculous &quot;are you an angel&quot; line). Is it rehashing a bit? Sure, but the whole movie did that, and did it well, and I think between what I'm saying and what I'm picturing, it would still wind up being significantly different. I think if they change about... three scenes in the first act, you could get all of that in. I think I could even specify them, if anybody cares. To me, that would constitute showing, rather than telling, a talent set before it operates for the plot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm too easy to please, but I feel like all those things are established by her scavenging (how else would she know market value if she didn't know what the parts do?) and being possibly the sole human in the settlement (why wouldn't she learn languages?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T08:20:00-08:00","id":797823,"title":"","content":"When I first watched the movie (and speaking as someone who has a decidedly middling interest in Star Wars), I did find is slightly stretched to imagine that Rey would have had opportunity to learn what she knew, particularly about piloting and later about using the Force. That's not news, though; Luke did about the same thing. For any criticism that's levied against her to be credible, the same must be levied against Luke.<br /> <br /> Star Wars is a mythical, uncomplicated place, where space ships are seemingly never locked or require any kind of code to start and where I can fully believe Rey Avatar Stating in the Kylo Ren battle. Without mentioning the M-word, we know that some are stronger with the Force than others. Rey is the Hero, and so she is Special, and strong with the Force. That's not enough to warrant a Mary Sue label.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 01-01-2016, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T08:32:20-08:00","id":797825,"title":"","content":"...I never thought about how no spaceship in the galaxy seems to need a door key. Or ignition key. I <i>have</i> thought about how they seem not to need fuel, but god damn, I'm starting to think Han had it coming if he didn't even spring for a Club to lock the steering wheel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T06:34:47-08:00","id":798228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">how else would she know market value if she didn't know what the parts do</div> </div> </div> </div> A catalogue might help. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">being possibly the sole human in the settlement (why wouldn't she learn languages</div> </div> </div> </div> The film presents being possibly the sole human in the settlement in terms of her spending all of her time alone, dealing solely with the person who provides her food (and speaks the same language as her). <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luke did about the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's framed differently. The actual occasion in which Luke uses his piloting skills comes at the very end, and while the setup of him mentioning on three occasions that he knows how to pilot and expressing that desire to attend the Academy is relatively minor, it's still more than nothing. Rey jumps right in with the thing, and has the nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T14:49:53-08:00","id":799813,"title":"","content":"Just got back from my second viewing.<br /> <br /> At first I wasn't particularly behind the idea of Rey getting in a romance with Poe or Finn (SPOILER: They don't in this movie, don't worry). It just seemed too obvious, too predictable, and thus, tired.<br /> <br /> But after seeing the chemistry between Daisy Ridley (Rey) and John Boyega (Finn) in instant action-adventure friendship... yeah, I'd be okay with it if they went that direction.<br /> <br /> Also (Double SPOILER alert)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I don't care if Finn does or doesn't have the Force - he's a Jedi. He's a good man who has taken up the lightsaber to fight for what's right. He's a Jedi.<br /> <br /> The new Jedi Knights should totally recruit worthy non-Force-sensitives. Finn deserves it.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 01-03-2016, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T15:19:18-08:00","id":799830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=799813#post799813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just got back from my second viewing.<br /> <br /> At first I wasn't particularly behind the idea of Rey getting in a romance with Poe or Finn (SPOILER: They don't in this movie, don't worry). It just seemed to obvious, to predictable, and thus, tired.<br /> <br /> But after seeing the chemistry between Daisy Ridley (Rey) and John Boyega (Finn) in instant action-adventure friendship... yeah, I'd be okay with it if they went that direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I like them better as friends, but I'd be ok with a romance developing out of that friendship.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/2645-star-wars-new-movies?p=799813#post799813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also (Double SPOILER alert)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I don't care if Finn does or doesn't have the Force - he's a Jedi. He's a good man who has taken up the lightsaber to fight for what's right. He's a Jedi.<br /> <br /> The new Jedi Knights should totally recruit worthy non-Force-sensitives. Finn deserves it.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I guess that depends on how you define it. But that's absolutely a question I'd be interested to see the new trilogy raise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T10:59:05-08:00","id":800649,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I was thinking of the subject of real life ship breakers (per the subject of how I'm sure a lot of them could not design a ship, let alone pilot one, because they're different skill sets), and I had this image in which Rey may have been more useful to her boss/owner when she was younger, because she could squeeze into tighter spaces to get at the really intricate parts.<br /> <br /> Could it be something behind why she's being paid less than she expects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <